upporter.care@mungos.org | Bin address to allow us to claim Gift Aid. For further information please see our privacy policy | REGULATOR at www.mungos.org/privacy-policy. | Registered Charity No 1149085, Company No 8225808, Housing Association NoLH0279 ~—~ Post to: Freepost, St Mungo’s NFC-IN00-03",Newspaper,NA,NA
010b,"CORONAVIRUS APPEAL | In Yemen, years of conflict and | the pandemic have decimated the | YEARS OF CONFLICT. | 2.3 million healthcare system. Millions are | children under five at risk of acute malnutrition. Your | projected to suffer support is helping us to provide | acute malnutrition. | fgod to families in desperate need, | & before it’s too late. | In Syria, virus cases continue to | a“ rise. Families who've fled conflict | are living in tents damaged by | severe floods and facing sub-zero | temperatures. With your help, | we're working to provide essential | a supplies, including hygiene kits, | to help them survive. | : , a r a combined with conflict, locusts | ‘i ¥ aN The largest ane flooding has left many families | locust lifestatian living off just one meal a day - | in 25 years has and it’s not enough. Donations can | eradicated crops. help us provide emergency grants | so people can buy the essentials | they need to survive. | Over 1.5 million | living in muddy, | overcrowded, | ‘last resort’ sites. | iaan/Islamic Relief | The pandemic is pushing the world’s most fragile states towards | catastrophe. Disrupted health services are overwhelmed, | and existing crises such as hunger, conflict and displacement | have been magnified. Millions are going hungry in places like £100 | Syria, Yemen and Somalia. DEC charities are working tirelessly | to provide a lifeline. Please, save lives, donate now. ; | SAVE LIVES. DONATE NOW. | DONATE TODAY: TEXT ‘TIMES’ TO ‘70150’ TO GIVE £10, CALL 0370 60 60 900 OR VISIT | MEMBER Sz actionaid —_7ageintemnational CAF+D €'3 aid Concern 1 af | CHARITIES care oy) | BU ocr ee | Children | Donations will be used to support the world’s most fragile places. Lines open 24 hours every day. *Texts are free but donations will be added to the bill and must have bill | payer's permission. Any donations received after 30th April 2021 could go to our emergency fund. Customer Service number 01204 770 822. Reg Charity No. 1062638. | | enclose a cheque made payable to DEC Coronavirus Appeal, or debit my Visa / Delta / Mastercard / AMEX / Maestro / Solo / Visa Electron / JCB / CAF Charitycard. (Please circle one) | Please send donations by post to: DEC Coronavirus Appeal, PO Box 999, London EC3A 3AA. | | would like to give: Card Number Expiry Date . | es0[_] sso[_] s100[ J omee[ TT] 6C TET TITTETTITITITt) CLL) CL | Date Signature Title ~ | Initials Sumame | Address | Postcode | Tick Add 25% to your donation at no extra cost to you — Yes — | want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | make in the future or have made in the past 4 years to the | Disasters Emergency Committee. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all | my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Gift Aid is reclaimed by the charity from the tax you pay for the current tax year. Your address is | needed to identify you as a current UK taxpayer. The tax reclaimed will be used to help fund the whole of the DEC’s work. | We will process your details for the purpose of this donation. For more details please see www.dec.org.uk/privacy-policy REGULATOR | We only get in touch to tell you how your donation is being spent or if other large scale disasters happen. If you would prefer not to hear from us email support@dec.org.uk . A023 - TIMES NEWS 25",Newspaper,NA,NA
