019,"FRIEND WANTED | | Are shana | | Caring ¢ | Concerned about t ackling in just ice ? | LOOKing, For a way To make a aitference? | _ HelpAge International UK, trading as Age International, is a registered charity (no. 1128267-8) anda subsidiary ie ae | of Age UK (charity no. 1128267 and registered company no. 6825798); both registered in England and Wales. | The tegistered address is Tavis House, 1-6 Tavistock Square, London WC1H 9NA. ae age International | f Registered with ore , | | | FR! FUNDRAISING gm , 7 ‘ | a, REGULATOR C¥recycle 10204623 03/21 11436 | , | ~~ - foe gra he et er een ie Si no tn | Inside: Your Friendship labels | ; When q friend puts | he world | it makes ¢ | q better piace | | ge | ae ‘ Tavis H | ~ageinternational tics | London WC1H 9NA | www.ageinternational.org.uk | 0800 032 0699 | contact@ageinternational.org.uk | Lines open | Mon-Fri 9am-5pm | Will you be a friend? Spring 2021 | Dear friend, | If you’ve opened this envelope, I believe you are just the friend we are looking for - someone who | cares about the most vulnerable older people around the world and is willing to take action to | tackle the injustice they face. | Does that sound like you? | I hope it does, because I’d like to invite you to join our community of friends at Age International. | By giving a regular gift each month, you could provide the practical support that older people living | in poverty need as we navigate our way out of the pandemic and into the uncertain years to come. | I don’t know if you’ve heard of Age International, but we help some of the most disadvantaged | older people around the world. You’ll perhaps recognise us as the international arm of Age UK. | Our work builds on a long and distinguished history stretching back to the 1960s. We focus on the | older people who need us most, helping them access healthcare that is tailored to their needs | and working with their communities to ensure they are cared for. We support older people to earn | a living or get the pensions they deserve. We challenge age-related prejudice and discrimination | wherever we find it. And when a disaster strikes, we ensure that older people are not forgotten. | In short, our goal is to redefine what it means to be older in today’s world. | Does that sound like something you would like to be part of? | Again, I hope it does. Because it’s only thanks to the kindness of our supporters that we can | help people overcome the difficulties and injustice that getting older can bring. I’d like to give | you an example of the work we do with a | focus on one country where we’re proud | to have helped pioneer an inclusive, Coronavirus has had a profound impact on | community-led approach to supporting older people around the world — especially | older people: Vietnam. the most disadvantaged, whom we support. | In Vietnam, more than 40% of people But it’s not just about surviving coronavirus. | aged 60 and over do not receive any form It’s about all the effects that have come with | of pension. Roughly the same proportion lockdowns, pressure on health systems and | lack the health insurance card that many further instability. It’s about the impact on the | others rely on. As a result, many older people | struggle to live healthy and dignified lives. health, income and isolation of older people. | To address this, we helped to establish a A regular gift will help us to support more older | network of Older People’s Associations: people as the world deals with the impact of | community-based organisations that COVID-19 in the months and years to come. The | support healthy ageing through a variety work we do has never been more important - will | of activities and provisions. One of the most you become a friend of Age International and | crucial of these provisions is social care. help some of the older people who need us most? | By recruiting and training local volunteers, Please complete and return the enclosed form | we’re able to equip people from the to help older people in need. Remember to | community with the skills needed to look follow social distancing guidelines if posting your | after those who aren't able to fully care for response. Alternatively, give securely online at | ageinternational.org.uk/friend or call our friendly | Please turn over... helpline on 0800 032 0699. | themselves. Whether it’s going out to buy food or fetch medicine, | cooking, cleaning, personal care, or doing the laundry - they | lend a helping hand, when there might be no one else there to | support them. | In a small village called Hong Thai, Miss Tuyet receives care at | home along with her severely disabled brother. Neither of them | can walk, so without anyone there to help, even the most basic | of tasks is a struggle. But her carers - older people themselves | - have helped to provide relief from these everyday struggles, | along with a friendly face. This support has transformed their | lives. As Miss Tuyet tells us: “The feeling of sitting there alone and | thinking about my disabilities was so sad and made me burst into | tears. But luckily, the volunteers have come, and they have helped | ease my sadness.” | Miss Tuyet is just one example of an older person receiving | Credit: Simon Rawles/Age International | support at home through what - in recent years-has grown = _Wgss Taget's volunteer CAnenrs | to become a network of more than 16,000 carers: the largest | in Vietnam. It’s an example of what can be achieved when help hen with everyclay Ea | like-minded people come together. People who want tocreate £kKe Cookina,, cheanimea, and | a kinder world, where everyone is valued and respected, no pe oe ss | matter their age. If I had the space, I’d give you many more a | examples. But one stark fact remains: without regular financial support, we simply wouldn’t be | able to help disadvantaged older people around the world. Without the generosity of people like | you, I don’t know what would have happened to Miss Tuyet and her brother. | Matching older people with their volunteers - and providing training and ongoing support through | their local Older People’s Association - is only possible by working with communities on the ground. | That’s how we can reach the most vulnerable older people with the right support, that they most need. | That takes time. It takes commitment. And it takes the generosity of somebody like you. | That’s why I would like to invite you to become a friend of Age International by committing to a | regular gift each month. You can use the enclosed form to respond (please stay safe on your trip to | the post box), you can give online at ageinternational.org.uk/friend or you can call 0800 032 0699. | By starting a regular gift today, you will help bring more comfort and security to some of the most | disadvantaged older people, as the number of people aged 60 and over continues to grow around | the world. Words don’t do justice to the difference you could make. | I’ll be sure to keep you up to date with the work that you help fund (if you choose to hear from | us). And from time to time, I’ll introduce you to some of the people you’ve helped, so you can see | exactly what your gifts are helping to achieve. | Around the world, so many people can be cast aside or isolated - simply because of their age. | It isn’t right, and your gift could help us tackle this injustice head-on by providing the basic | essentials older people need and deserve. Whether here in the UK, or the other side of the world, | later life brings similar challenges. By becoming a friend, you will help to transform the lives of | people who are ageing in some of the poorest parts of the world. | I hope you will join me in making this difference. | nna PS. By becomine, Q friend % fae International, | Ce 4 Roles wilh touch the Lives So many, atclen pele anomead | | world. Le also enchosect some stickens which L hoe | a ne t wilh serve a a nemimden % the cliggenence that youn | anaging Director : , | Age International oft Coulel make. Thank you | Registered with | ; (FR) FUNDRAISING | Follow us: @/AgeInternational Q@@Age_Int @@age_international REGULATOR | HelpAge International UK, trading as Age International, is a registered charity (no. 1128267-8) and a subsidiary | of Age UK (charity no. 1128267 and registered company no. 6825798); both registered in England and Wales. | The registered address is Tavis House, 1-6 Tavistock Square, London WC1H SNA. 1D204623 03/21 LS946 | When you become a friend of Age International, | you'll be helping to change lives. | You could help provide essential healthcare to older people who | would otherwise struggle to access what they need. Candeado, from | Mozambique, had very poor eyesight - but the glasses he received | from Age International changed his life. | “It made a big difference when I got my glasses. Before, I could not do | anything for myself. I could barely eat and I could not even go to the | toilet by myself. Now, I can do everything.” | Credit: Judith Escribano/Age International | Join with fellow supporters like | actress Miriam Margolyes | “I would urge people - if you have a charitable instinct, and if you | care about the world we live in, and if you recognise that there are | other older people in the same position as you all over the world, | who need your help, and you can do something about it...Give what | you can. | “People who may never know you, will bless you for giving them a | chance of happiness. You can give them the gift of a further life.” | Credit: Simon Rawles/Age International | You can trust Age International | to be there for older people | In 1961, a dedicated group launched the Help the Aged | Refugee Appeal to assist older people escaping conflict | and disaster abroad. This appeal was the start of the | organisation that would go on to become Help the Aged | and then, together with Age Concern England, formed Age UK. The desire to help older people | in need wherever they are was always part of the charity and to recognise this more formally, | Age International was formed as a separate organisation in 2012. | Image: Age International archive | Today, Age International is a UK leader in supporting older people overseas, working with in-country | partners through a localised approach, and as the UK member of the global HelpAge network. Our | vision is a world in which women and men everywhere can lead dignified, healthy and secure lives | as they grow older. But, as back in the 1960s, we depend on the generosity of supporters like you to | help realise this vision. | Project examples are illustrative of | rete the Age International’s programme and | uke ~ be Q <rule nc? Please tim aren to cow) donations will be used to support | ; ionae. Age International’s work worldwide, | prem and become @ friencl % A a Internat: where the need is greatest. | Dear friend, | Will you help transform the lives of some of the world’s most . age international | disadvantaged older people? Whether it’s enabling them to access the | healthcare they need, providing age-friendly aid when disaster strikes, or empowering older people | to access the pension they deserve, your support could fund vital programmes around the world. | Please let me know how much you would like to give on the form below. Thank you for your support. | Chris Roles, Managing Director | Yes, I’ll be a Friend to older people | I would like to give LJ£9amonth [_J£13amonth [_]My choice of £ a month | starting on [_]1st [_]15th of (month), (year) | Please choose a start date at least one month from now. | Instruction to your Bank or Building Society to pay by Direct Debit DIRECT | Please fill in the form and send it to: Age International, Debit | Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, Chippenham, SN14 6NG Service user number | Name and full postal address of your Bank or Building Society 4/318/21015 | To: the Manager (your bank’s name) | Reference number (Age International use only) | Address | Instruction to your Bank or Building Society: | Please pay Age International Direct Debits from the account | Postcode detailed on this instruction, subject to the safeguards assured | by the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand that this instruction | Name(s) of account holder(s) may remain with Age International and, if so, details will be | passed electronically to my Bank/Building Society. | Account number Sort code Signature(s) Date | Banks and Building Societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account. | My details MXAQ-21CG01-C009 | Title [| First name L Surname | | | Home address | | L Postcode | | | Telephone | Email| | | Keep in touch to hear how your ongoing support is helping older people | We’d like to keep in touch with you to let you know about the vital work we do for older people, our appeals, | products and services, and how you can support us. We will never sell your data. | Yes please, I would like to receive communications by email] phoneL] SMSC] | I do not wish to receive communications by post(_] You can change your mind at any time by phoning | 0800 032 0699 or emailing contact@ageinternational.org.uk | For further details on how your data is used and stored: ageinternational.org.uk/privacy | Gift Aid Declaration giftaid uw | (Yes, I want Age UK and its partner organisations* to treat all donations I have made for the four | years prior to this year, and all donations I make from the date of this declaration until I notify you otherwise, as Gift | Aid donations. I am a UK tax payer and understand that if I pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the | amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | ; *Age Cymru, Age Scotland and Age NI. Please ensure you provide your full name and address, and | Today s date | \) L | ly | | | let us know if you wish to cancel your declaration, or if your tax status, name or address changes. | Please return this form 