027,"CHAIN OF LIFE AROUND THE WORLD | Chain Around the | of life world with MSF | WE’RE PROUD OF HOW WE SPEND | 10 steps to getting | vital vaccines to where YOUR CONTRIBUTIONS | they're needed (MSF UK Annual Report 2019) | 85% 13% 2% | ON OUR HUMANITARIAN WORK ON FUNDRAISING (WE RAISE ON OFFICE MANAGEMENT | £8.24 FOR EVERY £1 WE SPEND) | Ensuring that our medical teams | are properly equipped with | vaccines and equipment can be a | major logistical challenge. If the | supply chain breaks down, the | vaccination campaign can't go | ahead. That's why we work hard | to make sure that the materials | get to our teams where - and | SUDAN | An MSF team ride by donkey | from Rokero to Umo in central | Darfur to provide medical care in | a remote region with no roads. | Photograph © MSF | when — they need them. NIGER | A woman waits for treatment at | an MSF clinic in Diffa. Malaria | is the leading cause of death in | Niger, and in 2020 teams saw a | 100 per cent increase in mataria | cases across all MSF | Photograph © Jasmin Lavoie/MSF | We transport medicines, | equipment and supplies around | the world by land, sea and air. | Vaccines are a particular challenge. | From the moment of manufacture | to the point of vaccination, they | must be kept at between 2 and 8 | degrees Celsius to avoid spoilage. | To make sure that their | temperature stays stable, we | use the ‘cold chain’ procedure. | SOUTH SUDAN | MSF staff carry a wounded | person on a stretcher in | Pieri, nor South | medical needs. Photograph C | Albert Masias/MSF | Sudan, where MSF runs a | health centre. Photograph © | Shirly Pador/MSF | Bueatrston Jerry Rctiey | YOUR SUPPORT MAKES OUR WORK POSSIBLE PLEASE HELP US SAVE LIVES AND DONATE AT MSF.ORG.UK/DONATE YOUR SUPPORT MAKES OUR WORK POSSIBLE PLEASE HELP US SAVE LIVES AND DONATE AT MSF.ORG.UK/DONATE YOUR SUPPORT MAKES OUR WORK POSSIBLE PLEASE HELP US SAVE LIVES AND DONATE AT MSF.ORG.UK/DONATE | IRAQ | A nurse treats a COVID-19 | patient in Al-Kindy hospit