028,"A free Will-writing service to | protect all that’s in your heart | We've teamed up with the Goodwill Partnership to offer 2 free | Will-writing service to help you protect everyone and everything | you care about. | Simply chat through your wishes via video cali, over the phone or | in your own home,* then receive your Will — which is checked by | a solicitor — directly to your door. | There's no obligation to donate to the RSPCA — but if animais | are in your heart, will you help us protect them always. with a gift | in your Will? | To book your appointment: | © Call: 0800 169 0004 & Visit: www.rspca.org.uk/willwriting | (I za negucerad with | 1 2) =| ND IPRA ASIN IG | ) REGULATOR | *Home appointments may not be immediately | available due to Covid-19. | Offer only available to residents of & | Wales. Only simple Wills included. Full terms & | conditions apply: www.rspca.org.uk/willwriting | All photos: RSPCA Photolibrary. | Goodwill | Partnership | Registered charity in England and Wales 219099. | The RSPCA helps animals in England and Wales and | does not operate in : | Part of REMEMBER A CHARITY",Newspaper,NA,NA
029,"a cure can’t come gm (Alzheimer’s | soon enough >) ag | Dementia | the system needs | to do better | people | living with dementia | ens ear | Please leave a gift in your Will to Alzheimer’s Society. | Your gift will help fund research into a cure. And until we get there, you'll help tackle the injustices in the | system to ensure nobody has to face dementia alone. | Your gift could safeguard the future of our vital support services. During the pandemic we have stepped | into the gap left by government neglect, to help people struggling to cope with isolation, anxiety and fear | under lockdown. | Your gift could help us push towards better diagnosis, treatments and care. A bequest of just 1% of your | estate, could help achieve the step-change we all desperately want to see. | If we in the dementia community don’t look out for each other, who will? With a gift in your Will to Alzheimer’s | Society, you can create a kinder, fairer future for people living with dementia. You can make sure they are | not forgotten. | Not , Request your free guide to leaving a gift in your Will today. | ] lew Visit alzheimers.org.uk/notforgotten, ca!| 0370 011 0290 or fill out | | and return the form below. | L) Please send me my free guide to leaving a gift in my Will | Title  --s_—~Firstname Last name | y Address t | i Postcode I | ; Email eae 7 ae ; Pai = _ Phone __ ary ONY eens Bl ee | i We'dlove to send you updates on our life-changing services and research, as We will never sell your details to any third parties. Please see i | f ~=well as our fundraising, campaigning and volunteering activities. Please tick alzheimers.org.uk/privacy for more information. If you'd like to | | § below to let us know you're happy for us to stay in touch. change what you receive from us at any time, please call our 1 | ; ; : friendly team on 0330 333 0804. | | co Bi Byemail _ Byphone _ Please don’t contact me via post i | y | Postin your own envelope to: Freepost NOT FORGOTTEN i | Y, ; | : Registered with | , ou donot need astamp or any other address details Rr) CUNDRAISING ; | | Please follow Government isolation and distancing guidelines if posting. REGULATOR i | t Registered charity no. 296645. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, Wales and Northern Ireland. LGPRAQ121M i | & ca",Newspaper,NA,NA
030,"Your kindness | means no one | gets left behind | With your support during the pandemic, we can continue to make food and | medicine deliveries, give emergency cash support, and help people struggling | with loneliness and mental health problems. | You have the power to keep volunteers like Emmanuel going. | To give help or get help, please visit | redcross.org.uk | BritishRedCross - #PowerOfKindness",Newspaper,NA,NA
031,"ate BritishRedCross | Noone You can help | left behind. someone who | has nowhere | : It’s never been more import’ else to tur Nn. | The power | of kindness | To donate: | Call O800 023 0827 | Visit redcross.org.uk/act | Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact from British Red Cross. | Text ACT NO to 70141 to give £10 without consenting to calls & texts | Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England Crrecycle | and Wales (220949), Scotland (GC037738) and Isle of Man (0752). When you hove shed | UK Office | 44 Moorfields | London | EC2Y 9AL | 0300 456 11 55 | redcross.org.uk | The British Red Cross Society, | incorporated by Royal Charter | 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), | Scotland (SC037738) and Isle | of Man (0752). | mim BritishRedCross | left behind. | It’s never been more important to make sure that | no one falls through the cracks. | Dear reader, | ‘No one left behind.’ | Here at the British Red Cross, that is our single mission right now. And I’m writing to you today because we | need your help to achieve it. | | think | speak for all of us when | say that 2021 has got off to a challenging start. For you, perhaps you've been | shielding, had to juggle childcare against work, or dealt with the stresses of job uncertainty or financial insecurity. | For the people we support, it’s been tough. | Many have been facing the shock of financial rock bottom. Some have been forced to make impossible choices | between buying food, paying to keep the electricity running or clothing their children. We've also been seeing first- | hand the pandemic’s serious toll on people’s mental health. | And the truth is, today, the pressures are still there. You'll already be aware that food insecurity, financial crises and | mental health illnesses are on the rise. For some, the burden of the pandemic has been building gradually, and is | now too much to manage alone. People are reaching their breaking point. | That’s why I’m asking if you can please help with a donation. | Back in April 2020, we launched our UK coronavirus appeal so we could quickly reach people who were slipping | into vulnerable situations. Our teams sprung into action — delivering basics that no one should have to go without | (like food and regular medical prescriptions), giving emergency financial support through our Hardship Fund, and | setting up a national support line for those who would otherwise fall through the cracks. | Almost one year later, with the pandemic raging on, the phone is still ringing. | continued overleaf | Please pledge whatever you can. | | would like to make a donation of: | [Jes [ ]e1o [ ]e25 [ ]#50 Mychoice |£ | [ | | enclose a cheque or postal order, made payable to ‘British Red Cross’ OR | Gift Aid allows us to claim back ‘ . d wt | 25p of tax for every £1 you give, I! QA | making your donation go further | | am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross | to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, | as well as any future donations, until | notify them | otherwise. Please tick to confirm | | understand that if | pay less income / capital gains tax | than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations | in the tax year in which they are received, it is my | responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to | let us know of any changes to your tax status including | changes to your name or address or if you need to | cancel this agreement. | [__] Please debit my Credit / Debit or CAF Card with the amount specified | crsvo.{ | | | }LT TTI LETT} Litt | | EE EG | Title (please tick): MrL_] Mrsl_] missl_] msL_] other[ | *Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are happy for us to | contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and how you can | donate and help in other ways. | visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch, e-mailing | mailenquiries@redcross.org.uk writing to FREEPOST | RED CROSS or calling Freephone 0800 2 800 491. | Name Surname Keeping in touch | rer We're so grateful for your support, thank you. As part | “a of the Red Cross, we write to you to tell you about 2 | Postcode how your gifts help transform lives and how you can g | : donate and help in other ways, as well as to update 5 | Telephone you about our news and services. If you would rather 3 | Email’ we didn't communicate with you in this way, you > | can change the way we contact you at any time by & | Since the start of 2021, the number of calls to our support line has spiked — per week it’s between 400 to 600 calls. | In fact, January — specifically the very first day of lockdown, 5 Jan 2021 - was the busiest time since last August. | That’s why we’ve relaunched our UK appeal this year, and we’re asking for your help. | We have teams working in communities across the UK, and we’re linked up with local support groups too. So | we’re able to organise food and medicine deliveries, emergency cash help, or more recently, transport to vaccine | appointments, for the caller on the end of the line. | We also give emotional support to those who've lost sight of brighter days ahead. Our trained, friendly Red Cross | volunteers, who staff the line, take the time to listen to what each caller is going through. And for anyone struggling | with loneliness, grief or depression — which, unfortunately, is really common at the moment — this kind of support is | absolutely critical. | Please, if you can, donate now to our UK coronavirus appeal. | As the number of people needing help goes up, the strain on our services gets heavier. On top of the increased | demand on our support line, we’re also supporting the nation’s vaccine rollout and responding to extreme weather | warnings, like Storm Christoph not too long ago. This all comes at a time when more staff and volunteers are having | to self-isolate. | And with our Red Cross charity shops shut for the majority of the year so far, and big fundraising events like | marathons and treks on pause, our front-line teams are under enormous pressure. But through it all, we’re | committed to leaving no one behind. | Help us keep that commitment by donating today. | | want to sign off my letter by passing the (digital) pen over to people who’ve been helped through the support line — | to show you the impact your donation could have. | One person said the Red Crosser that supported them was “very kind and helpful, but most of all, a friendly lady | who didn’t judge.” | Someone else noted that they were “nervous and embarrassed at having to call for help”, but a volunteer put them | at ease. And another told us: “If it was not for the British Red Cross, my children and | would have went hungry.” | If you are in a position to give today, whatever the amount, we’d really appreciate it. | Because what you're really saying with your donation is: “I believe no one should be left behind.” You're stepping | forward to help those who need it most, who have nowhere else to turn. And to me, that’s the ultimate definition of | kindness. | Look after yourself and those around you, | dw Ono The power | EE cess of kindness | P.S. Of course, | hope you’ll be able to help today. But just a reminder — if you need help, please don’t suffer in silence. | We’re a phone call away on 0808 196 3651, every day between 10am-6pm, ready to listen on our support line. | a BritishRedCross (FR) REGULATOR | Your Privacy | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and | will use personal data for the purpose it was collected | \ Call: 0300 023 0827 Cf Visit: redcross.org.uk/act or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for | . example, to provide goods, services or information you | 0 Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation have requested or to administer donations or services | . —— . we provide. We may also analyse data we collect | By texting you consent to future teleohone & SMS marketing contact 20 Getler unGeiatand tha Heotia who suchort us Gr | from British Red Cross. Text ACT NO to give £10 without consenting shite WAG USS on Haier dur eaides. Seimetines thie | to calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message means us combining that data with information from | (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor | communications and services in a more focused and | cost effective way, as well as better meeting your needs | and the needs of others like you. However, we will never | do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and | will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with | previously expressed privacy preferences. For full details | about how we use personal data, our legal basis for | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy | England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738) and Isle of Man (0752). notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy | The British Red Cross will use your donation wherever the need is greatest in the UK, | and at this time our efforts are focused on our response to the Coronavirus/Covid-19 | pandemic and its impact in the UK. | vibes BritishRedCross | Please affix | postage stamp | here to help | reduce our | costs. | Freepost Plus RTUU-JTGU-GLTA | ROOM Q1CI21 | British Red Cross | York House | Wetherby Road | Long Marston | York | YO026 7NH | Return address: British Red Cross, York House, Wetherby Road, Long Marston, York, YO26 7NH BR1 | The power | of kindness | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | C Call: 0300 023 0827 = Visit: redcross.org.uk/act | [] Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text ACT NO to give £10 without consenting to | Calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). | For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738) and Isle of Man (0752).",Newspaper,NA,NA
