041,"a BritishRedCross | Noone You can help | left behind. someone who | has nowhere | ; It’s never been more import: else to tur Nn. | The power | of kindness | To donate: | Call 0800 023 0827 | Visit redcross.org.uk/act | Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact from British Red Cross. | Text ACT NO to 70141 to give £10 without consenting to calls & texts | Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England Crrecycle | and Wales (220949), Scotland (GC037738) and Isle of Man (0752). When you hove fished | UK Office | 44 Moorfields | London | EC2Y 9AL | 0300 456 11 55 | redcross.org.uk | talon BritishRedCross | The British Red Cross Society, | incorporated by Royal Charter | 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), | Scotland (SC037738) and Isle | of Man (0752). | left behind. | It’s never been more important to make sure that | no one falls through the cracks. | Dear reader, | ‘No one left behind.’ | Here at the British Red Cross, that is our single mission right now. And I’m writing to you today because we | need your help to achieve it. | | think | speak for all of us when | say that 2021 has got off to a challenging start. For you, perhaps you've been | shielding, had to juggle childcare against work, or dealt with the stresses of job uncertainty or financial insecurity. | For the people we support, it’s been tough. | Many have been facing the shock of financial rock bottom. Some have been forced to make impossible choices | between buying food, paying to keep the electricity running or clothing their children. We've also been seeing first- | hand the pandemic’s serious toll on people’s mental health. | And the truth is, today, the pressures are still there. You'll already be aware that food insecurity, financial crises and | mental health illnesses are on the rise. For some, the burden of the pandemic has been building gradually, and is | now too much to manage alone. People are reaching their breaking point. | That’s why I’m asking if you can please help with a donation. | Back in April 2020, we launched our UK coronavirus appeal so we could quickly reach people who were slipping | into vulnerable situations. Our teams sprung into action — delivering basics that no one should have to go without | (like food and regular medical prescriptions), giving emergency financial support through our Hardship Fund, and | setting up a national support line for those who would otherwise fall through the cracks. | Almost one year later, with the pandemic raging on, the phone is still ringing. | continued overleaf | Please pledge whatever you can. | | would like to make a donation of: | [Jes [ ]e1o [ ]e25 [ ]#50  Mychoice |£ | a | enclose a cheque or postal order, made payable to ‘British Red Cross’ OR | Gift Aid allows us to claim back ‘ . d it | 25p of tax for every £1 you give, I! QA | making your donation go further | | am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross | to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, | as well as any future donations, until | notify them | otherwise. Please tick to confirm | | understand that if | pay less income / capital gains tax | than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations | in the tax year in which they are received, it is my | responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to | let us know of any changes to your tax status including | changes to your name or address or if you need to | cancel this agreement. | [__] Please debit my Credit / Debit or CAF Card with the amount specified | cwsvo.{ | | |} LT TT |_LT tT Litt | | oe | | | Title (please tick): MrL_] MrsL_] missL_] ms[_] other| | *Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are happy for us to | contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and how you can | donate and help in other ways. | visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch, e-mailing | mailenquiries@redcross.org.uk writing to FREEPOST | RED CROSS or calling Freephone 0800 2 800 491. | Name Surname Keeping in touch | had We're so grateful for your support, thank you. As part | = of the Red Cross, we write to you to tell you about 2 | Postcode how your gifts help transform lives and how you can g | : donate and help in other ways, as well as to update a | Telephone you about our news and services. If you would rather 3 | Email’ we didn't communicate with you in this way, you >= | can change the way we contact you at any time by ® | Since the start of 2021, the number of calls to our support line has spiked — per week it’s between 400 to 600 calls. | In fact, January — specifically the very first day of lockdown, 5 Jan 2021 - was the busiest time since last August. | That’s why we’ve relaunched our UK appeal this year, and we’re asking for your help. | We have teams working in communities across the UK, and we’re linked up with local support groups too. So | we’re able to organise food and medicine deliveries, emergency cash help, or more recently, transport to vaccine | appointments, for the caller on the end of the line. | We also give emotional support to those who've lost sight of brighter days ahead. Our trained, friendly Red Cross | volunteers, who staff the line, take the time to listen to what each caller is going through. And for anyone struggling | with loneliness, grief or depression — which, unfortunately, is really common at the moment — this kind of support is | absolutely critical. | Please, if you can, donate now to our UK coronavirus appeal. | As the number of people needing help goes up, the strain on our services gets heavier. On top of the increased | demand on our support line, we’re also supporting the nation’s vaccine rollout and responding to extreme weather | warnings, like Storm Christoph not too long ago. This all comes at a time when more staff and volunteers are having | to self-isolate. | And with our Red Cross charity shops shut for the majority of the year so far, and big fundraising events like | marathons and treks on pause, our front-line teams are under enormous pressure. But through it all, we’re | committed to leaving no one behind. | Help us keep that commitment by donating today. | | want to sign off my letter by passing the (digital) pen over to people who’ve been helped through the support line — | to show you the impact your donation could have. | One person said the Red Crosser that supported them was “very kind and helpful, but most of all, a friendly lady | who didn’t judge.” | Someone else noted that they were “nervous and embarrassed at having to call for help”, but a volunteer put them | at ease. And another told us: “If it was not for the British Red Cross, my children and | would have went hungry.” | If you are in a position to give today, whatever the amount, we’d really appreciate it. | Because what you're really saying with your donation is: “I believe no one should be left behind.” You're stepping | forward to help those who need it most, who have nowhere else to turn. And to me, that’s the ultimate definition of | kindness. | Look after yourself and those around you, | dow Ono The power | a of kindness | P.S. Of course, | hope you'll be able to help today. But just a reminder — if you need help, please don’t suffer in silence. | We’re a phone call away on 0808 196 3651, every day between 10am-6pm, ready to listen on our support line. | a BritishRedCross (FR) REGULATOR | Your Privacy | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and | will use personal data for the purpose it was collected | \ Call: 0300 023 0827 Cf Visit: redcross.org.uk/act or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for | . example, to provide goods, services or information you | 0 Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation have requested or to administer donations or services | we provide. We may also analyse data we collect | By texting you consent to future teleohone & SMS marketing contact $e hatiey understand ie peodia who sxceatiue c | from British Red Cross. Text ACT NO to give £10 without consenting Histo Wii) tis oF delve nur oacvices, Seinetince this | to calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message means us combining that data with informeiion fons | (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor | communications and services in a more focused and | cost effective way, as well as better meeting your needs | and the needs of others like you. However, we will never | do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and | will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with | previously expressed privacy preferences. For full details | about how we use personal data, our legal basis for | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy | England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738) and Isle of Man (0752). notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy | The British Red Cross will use your donation wherever the need is greatest in the UK, | and at this time our efforts are focused on our response to the Coronavirus/Covid-19 | pandemic and its impact in the UK. | vies BritishRedCross | Please affix | postage stamp | here to help | reduce our | costs. | Freepost Plus RTUU-JTGU-GLTA | ROOM Q1CI21 | British Red Cross | York House | Wetherby Road | Long Marston | York | YO26 7NH | Return address: British Red Cross, York House, Wetherby Road, Long Marston, York, YO26 7NH BR1 | The power | of kindness | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | € call: 03000230827. LJ visit: redcross.org.uk/act | [] Text ACT to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text ACT NO to give £10 without consenting to | Calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). | For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738) and Isle of Man (0752).",Newspaper,NA,NA
042,"Over the next thirty years, the pressures of dementia will push hundreds of thousands of families to | breaking point. | A gift in your Will to Dementia UK will help fund more specialist dementia nurses - called Admiral Nurses | - so no family ever has to cope with dementia alone. | After family and friends have been taken care of, any gift, however small or large, will help families facing | dementia long into the future. | Call: 0300 365 5500 Email: giftsinwills@dementiauk.org | Visit: www.dementiauk.org/GIW | Or return this form to: | Gifts in Wills Manager, Dementia UK, | 7th Floor, One Aldgate, London EC3N 1RE UK | Registered charity in England and Wales (1039404) and Scotland (SCo047429) Helping families face dementia | _] Mr [_] Mrs {_] Ms [_] Other |_]No post please | Name Dementia UK will use your address to send you your guide to | gifts in Wills. We would also like to keep you updated by post | Address on ways you can fundraise to support our work in the future. | If you would prefer not to hear from us, please let us know by | ticking the box above. To change how you hear from us at any | Postcode time, contact our Supporter Care team on 0300 365 5500 by | email supportercare@dementiauk.org. For full details on how | Registered with | FUNDRAISING we store and use your personal information, please see our | REGULATOR Privacy Policy at dementiauk.org/privacypolicy | GIW-Guardian",Newspaper,NA,NA
043,"Your kindness | gives Mary hope. | Initially, Mary was unsure about the Covid-19 vaccine. She’s not too keen on injections. | But your help means British Red Cross volunteers can be there in vaccination centres | across the nation, helping to put people like Mary at ease as they take the step to | protect themselves and others against the virus. | By supporting the British Red Cross, you can help those who need it, | when they need it, in ways they need it most. | To give help or get help, please visit | redcross.org.uk | haa BritishRedCross : #PowerOfKindness",Newspaper,NA,NA
044,"Your kindness | means no one. | gets left behind | With your support during the pandemic, we can continue to make food and | medicine deliveries, give emergency cash support, and help people struggling | with loneliness and mental health problems. | You have the power to keep volunteers like Emmanuel going. | To give help or get help, please visit | redcross.org.uk | BritishRedCross #PowerOfKindness",Newspaper,NA,NA
045,"Over the next thirty years, the pressures of dementia will push hundreds of thousands of families to | breaking point. | A gift in your Will to Dementia UK will help fund more specialist dementia nurses - called Admiral Nurses | - so no family ever has to cope with dementia alone. | After family and friends have been taken care of, any gift, however small or large, will help families facing | dementia long into the future. | Call: 0300 365 5500 Email: giftsinwills@dementiauk.org | Visit: www.dementiauk.org/GIW | Or return this form to: | Gifts in Wills Manager, Dementia UK, | 7th Floor, One Aldgate, London EC3N 1RE U K | Registered charity in England and Wales (1039404) and Scotland ($C047429) Helping families face dementia | (_] Mr {_] Mrs (_] Ms [_] Other _] No post please | Name Dementia UK will use your address to send you your guide to | gifts in Wills. We would also like to keep you updated by post | Address on ways you can fundraise to support our work in the future. | If you would prefer not to hear from us, please let us know by | ticking the box above. To change how you hear from us at any | Postcode time, contact our Supporter Care team on 0300 365 5500 by | Registered with email supportercare@dementiauk.org. For full details on how | FUNDRAISING we store and use your personal information, please see our | REGULATOR Privacy Policy at dementiauk.org/privacypolicy  GIW-Telegraph",Newspaper,NA,NA
046,"NAP2021CT-O1Y | Thousands of young people have been made | homeless by the continuing crisis. | They call them the ‘Lost Generation’. Thousands of young people who have lost their jobs and their | homes as a result of the continuing crisis. Every night more homeless young people are at risk, on | our streets. Since the beginning of the pandemic, we have seen a huge surge in calls to our Helpline. | We are facing the biggest homeless crisis in our history. We must be able to answer every call we | can. That's why we need your urgent help right now. Your gift today could be the turning point for | a young person in desperate need. | Call 0800 472 5798 now. | Visit centrepoint.org.uk/coronavirus | or search ‘Centrepoint Urgent’ | Registered office address: Central House, 25 Camperdown Street, London E1 8DZ. Company no. 1929421. Registered with i | Registered Charity no. 292411. Housing association no. H1869. VAT registration no. 649 345 018. We sometimes use models and change REGUI MOR | the names of the young people we work with to protect their identity: however al! stories are true and as told by the young person.",Newspaper,NA,NA
