050,"WaterAid MMV Ul | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LIST | WaterAid | York House | Wetherby Road | Long Marston | YORK | YO26 7NH | 77p on clean water, decent | toilets and good hygiene | 23p on fundraising* | op te | Why do we eK) a aoa git | _rcase = nee al eae ee TS mae i came a mA a | Water: th | A personal view from Olga Ghazaryan, | Director of International Programmes at WaterAid. | @ Thanks to people | like you, 9 out of | 10 people now | have clean water. | @ But, today, over | 800 children | under 5 will die | from diseases | caused by dirty | water and poor | sanitation. | @ Please give a | monthly gift to | help give clean | water pumps and | wells to children | like Roumina. | Do you think charities only | ever bring you bad news? | If so, I've got a brilliant | surprise for you. Right now, | we are making the most | amazing progress. | What does this progress | look like? For me, it looks like | Roumina (pictured above), | a beautiful little girl in | Madagascar who has just | seen clean running water | for the first time in her life. | Little Roumina illustrates a | major turning point; right now, | 9 out of 10 people have clean | water to drink. I like to call | this progress the Clean Water | Revolution. Amoment as | significant as the Magna Carta, | the Industrial Revolution or the | triumph of the Suffragettes - | all movements that have driven | the world forward. | However, over 800 children | still die from drinking dirty water | every day. But this is a crisis | that, together, we can change | Please give an urgent gift of progress today. Form overleaf. | in a final push for progress. | So, today, will you give a | monthly gift to help save lives? | Your gift could be another vital | drop in a tidal wave of progress. | If we accelerate our pace of | change, the whole of humanity | could have clean water by 2030. | Isn't that incredible? | But we cannot be complacent. | Together, we must gather all | of our efforts in one final push. | Together, we must finish | the job. | WaterAid | Look again at Roumina. | Think of her future. With this | one gift of clean water, so many | other gifts will follow. We call this | the ripple effect. The first gift | is survival, because Roumina | is now more likely to reach her | fifth birthday and stay healthy | as she grows up. She has hope | too. Having a water pump in her | village means she won't have | to trek miles to collect water, | but instead she will have time | to study. That means she can | get an education and earn | a living when she grows up. | That means she can find a | lasting way out of poverty. | Fact: 40 billion hours are | wasted by women and girls | in sub-Saharan Africa every | year collecting water. This | is equal to the hours spent by | the workforce of the world’s | sixth largest economy: France. | So imagine if all these women | and girls weren't forced to waste | their time in drudgery but could | invest it in education. Imagine | the astonishing human potential | that, together, we could unlock. | Progress always comes back to | education. As a mother, | I love seeing children in schools | Registered with | EUNDRAISING | eR) REGULATOR | learning the nine - yes nine! - | steps to proper handwashing: | the world's simplest and most | effective vaccine against deadly | conditions like diarrhoea, | pneumonia, influenza and ebola. | Every pair of hands scrubbing | themselves with soap and water | is another life possibly saved. | I'm passionate about progress | because I've seen the opposite. | In my late 20s, I was in Armenia | when the Soviet Union collapsed | and every public service crashed. | Water was only turned on | for one hour a day. The most | but our success proves that your | monthly donations will make an | extraordinary difference. | Right now, I'd like to invite | you to give a monthly gift | of progress. This will fund | tangible, effective and intelligent | technology to supply clean | water. Not just hand pumps | and wells, but equipment to | harvest rainwater; dams, water | pipes and fresh water springs; | gravity-fed water systems and | school latrines. Each one built to | last. Each one built to save lives. | Let's protect more children | “Today, over 800 children will die from drinking | dirty water. Together, let’s solve this crisis.” | cherished sound at home was | the buzzing of the water in the | pipes. I'll never forget those | days; the link between running | water and progress is absolutely | visceral for me. It’s why I'm in | this job. It’s why I do what I do. | I don’t work for WaterAid | to uphold the status quo. I'm | here to make progress and, | today, I'm asking you to join the | momentum. The progress we're | making is the very best reason | to donate. There are still millions | of people we need to reach, | Please give £2 a month | toWaterAidand, _ | together, we can stop | children dying from | drinking dirty water. | 0300 123 4341* WaterAid | *Calls charged at local rates. Registered charity numbers 288701 (England and Wales) and $C039479 (Scotland) | against disease and, using the | power of the ripple effect, let’s | see what happens when we help | to give 40 billion hours back to | women and girls (I think a lot | will change). | Today, over 800 children will | die from drinking dirty water. | But it doesn’t have to be this | way. Please fill in the enclosed | form and give a monthly gift | to WaterAid. | Together, let's solve this | crisis. Let's push for progress. | Let’s make history. Thank you. | iw ee ww oo eww ee we ew ew ee oe ee eee ce cee ec ewe ewer oes eee we new ee een nn eee opens 6 ees oo meres eee eee ene a See ene sees eee ween eee sees eee eee eeesee=e- | “WaterAid | Yes, I'll join the final push today | £2 could save children’s lives £10 could save children’s lives | in Bangladesh | £5 could save children’s lives in | Niger | in Nepal | Here's my life-changing gift of You can hear how you change lives. We hope you will | fill out your contact details below to hear more about | £2 £5 £10 Surprise us! £ children like Roumina, fundraising, and opportunities to | get involved. If you are happy to hear from us by phone | each month ‘ : | and email, please let us know your details: | Starting onthe 1st 15th 25th —_ until further notice. | (Should be at least four weeks from date | Month Year of signang) Tel no. (home/mobile): | Email: | Title: First name: ‘ | Many people love to receive postal updates. | Tick if you'd prefer not to | WaterAid and WaterAid Trading will use your personal details to | communicate with you in the ways you have agreed to, and as | explained in our Privacy Policy. We may use the information you share | with us and background information about you that we obtain from | publicly available sources to carry out analysis (sometimes using | suppliers) to tailor our communications to be more appropriate and | relevant to your interests. You can withdraw your consent at any time. | For full details, including information about your privacy rights, see our | Privacy Policy at www.wateraid.org/privacy | To change your preferences, or request to stop receiving | communications please contact us on | 020 7793 4594 or supportercare@wateraid.org 20/18x/010 | Surname: | Home Address: | Postcode: | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid | without your full name and address. | BwaterAid Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by direct debit. | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST, WaterAid, York House, York YO26 7NH. (00 NoT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society Service user number | 4'0.6)7/'8'9 | Reference (to be completed by WaterAid) | DIRECT | Debit | To the Manager: Bank/building society | Branch address: | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please | pay WaterAid Direct Debits from the account detailed in | this Instruction 