057,"the. | gorilla | organization | Freepost Plus RTKS-ZCXS-HSBT | The Gorilla Organization | 126 Fairlie Road | SLOUGH | SL1 4PY | Here’s why the gorillas urgently need your help the. | gorilla — | Kahuzi Biega, Congo: organization | Rangers were tracking a family of Grauer’s gorillas when they | observed a baby male with a crude wire snare cutting into his wrist. | Another gorilla had broken the sware free from its pole, but it was | creating an open, bleeding | ee wound. Rangers and vets | — | sedated both baby and | mother, then carefully | removed the snare, and | cleaned and stitched up | the wound. Soon baby was | cuddling his mother again. | Without urgent treatment, | he'd certainly have lost his | ve } hand, and probably his life. | Bahoze, Congo: | When baby mountain gorilla Bahoze was trapped in a smare, her | mother Maganiya tried to remove it. But this only tightened the | snare around Bahoze’s | Br as | ei *_~@ ah | 9 CF ‘ a [ | wrist. Silverback Lulengo p is | was also clearly visibly eal | distressed. He started to | charge the vets. Rangers 4 | managed to calm 4 | him while Bahoze was | successfully treated. One | more Life saved thanks | to the bravery and self- | sacrifice of our rangers. | What's a govillar” | A personal appeal from Bill Oddie | This tiny baby gorilla is as fragile | as one of our own babies | | won't rest until we have saved | the gorillas from extinction. Will | you stand side by side with me? | Anything you give will help: | But they cannot do it alone. The gorillas need your help today too Will you please give £20 to save our last gorillas? | We can still save the gorillas, but only if we act now. 99.9% of all gorillas are still | critically endangered, so there’s no time to waste. | Please fill in the form below or if you prefer you can give by phone 0300 330 0141 | or securely online at www.gorillas.org/donate | gorilla | organization | If everyone who loves animals works together, we can save the | gorillas we all care about so much. So please make a gift today — | and make sure we never have to explain why we let the gorillas go. | Dear Friend, | When my grandchildren were little, they | used to ask me questions no grown-up ever | would. Like ‘what's a gorilla?’ | | told them that gorillas are amazing | creatures — our closest living relatives. What | | didn't say was that gorillas will soon | only exist in zoos or movies — unless we “You and | have the power | protect them right now. jatimmepdoend assem | Bill Oddie, Patron | Gorillas are teetering on the brink of | extinction. They're under more pressure than ever before. Just | thinking about that brings tears to my eyes. | That's why I'm asking for your help today. Will you give just £20 to | save our last precious gorillas before it’s too late? | Because if we don’t do more to protect gorillas right now, we’re | going to have to explain to the next generation how we let them go. | It's over 50 years since Dian Fossey started her amazing work to save | the gorillas — perhaps you remember her story from the film ‘Gorillas | in the Mist’. Dian dedicated her life to saving gorillas. When she was | savagely murdered by poachers, the Gorilla Organization carried on | her mission. Their unique approach really works. That's why I’m so | proud to help them. | * provide ranger patrols to protect | vulnerable gorilla families from | poachers — often at terrible risk | to their own lives | * our rangers form a ‘human | shield’ to keep gorillas safe | from the current epidemic | * remove the increasing number | of snares being found in the gorillas’ habitat and | rescue any baby gorillas from traps before its too late. | Mountain gorillas are incredibly rare. There are just over a thousand | left in the wild — ranging across Rwanda, Uganda and the Democratic | Republic of the Congo (DRC). | Tragically, the Grauer’s gorilla has seen a 78 per cent drop from | 17,000 to just 3,800 individuals in just a single generation. | Gorillas urgently need your help today. | Rangers are prepared to give up their own lives to save the gorillas | At least 200 rangers working alongside the Gorilla Organization in the | DRC have given their lives to save their gorilla ‘brothers and sisters’. | We have recently received reports that six more brave men have | been killed by armed militias in the DRC while protecting gorillas. | Please don't let their bravery have been in vain. | Many more rangers are deep in the forest right now, far from their | homes and loved ones. They never question whether the risks are | worth it. They know the gorillas need their help. They’re ready to risk | everything to keep a baby gorilla out of the poachers’ hands, or to | rescue a youngster from a cruel snare. | Yours sincerely | Bill Oddie | Patron and conservationist | The Gorilla Organization | PS. Extinction is for ever. So please make a gift of £20 to save the | gorillas before it’s too late. | The Gorilla Org | 110 GI | London NW1 8HX | Registered Charity No. 1117131. | E-mail: info@gorillas.org ene www.gorillas.org | an: England and Wale | ion of Joe McKenna. | Here is my gift to support The Gorilla Organization’s work: | (please circle) | £15 £20 £30 | Or my preferred gift of: | £ | How to make your gift | | enclose a cheque/PO payable to: The Gorilla Organization | \_JOR please debit my Mastercard/Visa/Maestro/CAF Card (delete as appropriate) | Account Number 2s oe 2. ee Maestro ONLY | Card Expires : | Your details Title! | First name (in full) | Surname | ane cceceesenccsecsceseecenseeesscsssscesccesscssssnees | Address | | Post code | Make every gift worth 25% more | | YES | am a UK taxpayer” |INO sorry | do not pay tax DATE. | / | \f | *| would like The Gorilla Organization to treat this and all future donations H fi dit | | make from the date of this declaration as Gift Aid donations.|amaUK = _9!/444 | and understand that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital | Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year, 8 | it is my responsibility to pay any difference. 5 | | will notify The Gorilla Organization if | wish to cancel this declaration, change my 8 | name or home address or | no longer pay sufficient Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax. | Can we stay in touch? | Your support makes a huge difference to our work, and we would like to stay in touch | with you to let you know how you are helping and how you could help save gorillas from | extinction. We promise we will never sell or share your details to any other organisation and | will always keep them secure. We will only process your data if we have legal grounds to do | so. This will mainly be by your consent to process your data, or under the rules of legitimate | interest. For full information please read our Privacy Policy at www.gorillas.org/privacy. If you | wish to update these preferences at any time, please email us at info@gorillas.org. Please tick | below if you DO NOT wish to hear from The Gorilla Organization by post. | Please fold and stick this form and return to: Freepost Plus RTKS-ZCXS-HSBT, | The Gorilla Organization, 126 Fairlie Road, SLOUGH SL1 4PY Thank you",Newspaper,NA,NA
