068,"ETHIOPIA EM ERGENCY APPEAL 5 eer | Albert Vifias, MSF emergency | coordinator in Tigray, Ethiopia | Hundreds of thousands | of people have been | forced to leave their | homes in the Tigray region of | northern Ethiopia after fighting | broke out in November last year. | MSF teams have been providing medical care to | affected people since mid-December. Albert Viiias | is MSF’s emergency coordinator in Tigray. | “After several attempts, we finally entered the capital of | Tigray, Mekele, more than a month after the violence | started. The city was quiet. There was electricity, but no | basic supplies. The local hospital was running at 30 to | 40 per cent, with little medication. There were almost | no patients, which is always a very bad sign. | In Adigrat, the situation was very tense and the hospital | was in a terrible condition. Most of the staff had left, | there were hardly any medicines and no food and water. | Some patients were malnourished. | We supplied the hospital with medicines and bought | emergency food in the markets that were still open. | Together with the remaining staff, we cleaned the | building and organised waste collection. Little by little | we rehabilitated the hospital so that it could function. | NO TELEPHONES | Beyond the hospitals, around 80 or 90 per cent of | the health centres we visited were not functional. | One woman had been in labour for seven days without | being able to give birth. Her life was saved because we | Hospitals, healthcare centres and clinics across | Ethiopia’s Tigray region have been looted, | vandalised and destroyed. | MSF medical teams are working to refurbish hospitals | and provide urgent medical care to people caught | up in this crisis. We are providing medical support in | emergency rooms, maternity wards, and outpatient | departments and are running mobile clinics in rural | towns and villages. We need your help now more | than ever. | MSF relies on donations | from people like you. | £40 _could provide pain relief to 29 patients | Foknat & Comer ee to families displaced by the fighting. £115 could provide dressings kits for 95 | wounded patients | were able to transport her to Mekele. I saw people £228 could cover the costs of a doctor working | arrive at hospital on bicycles carrying a patient from in remote clinics for three days | 30 km away. | £866 could pay for a portable ultrasound | device to help medical teams detect | The impact of the violence is visible in the buildings c : , | underlying health issues in patients | and cars with bullet holes. We saw a population | locked in their homes and living in fear. Everyone | gave us pieces of paper with phone numbers written Please give what you can to our medical | on them and asked us to convey messages to their teams — they'll give everything they can | families. People don’t even know if their relatives and in | loved kay b i I h | stillno telephones or telecommunications. | THANK YOU | DONATE NOW | CALL 0800 055 7985 | or make your donation online at: | msf.org.uk/tigray | We're very concerned about what may be happening | in rural areas. Our mobile medical teams are visiting | areas outside the main cities and we've reopened some | health centres. You feel that you offer people some | hope: the feeling that things can improve after two | months without good news.” | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | Title Pt | Surname | | | | | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontiéres UK | Address | | | | | OR C) Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: [ | T | | CardholdernameL_{| | | | | | | | } FE ET TUTE TT TCT TT J pitiite Baa | cadrumber CET T)] C1 TT) CLL) CIT i oo | Expiry date [eT] / [yTy] Today’s date | | 1/| | 1/| | | | ; HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. | Signature Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which provides first-hand accounts of our work. | You will receive Frontline, event invitations and occasional emergency appeals with | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? requests for donations. | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% more | at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | gift nid uw | CJ Opt me in to email | RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | Date /HE/OO | NB: Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | this declaration, so that we can update our records. | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand | accounts from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, | from combating epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | We won't allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing | purposes and we won’t bombard you with appeals. | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations, | and occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change | how you hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling | 020 7404 6600. Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | 100463 | Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, | Chippenham SN14 6NG. Alternatively you can phone 0800 055 7985 or make your donation online at: msf.org.uk/tigray | Charity Registration Number 1026588 | MSFROO55",Newspaper,NA,NA
069,"TEXT TIGRAY | ETHIOPIFA(?) | TRANSFORMING LIVES IN ETHIOPIA | THERE ARE | OVER 1 MILLION | DISPLACED PEOPLE | AS A RESULT OF | VIOLENCE IN THE | TIGRAY REGION | OF ETHIOPIA. | ee oe | ""PEOPLE ARE FLEEING | FOR THEIR LIVES | Communities have been devastated. Food and | water is scarce and there are significant civilian | casualties, including survivors of sexual violence. | Families have been torn apart and the turmoil is unimaginable. | In remote rural areas there is little, if any, aid within reach. | Our local partners are supporting those in desperate need | and reaching the most vulnerable with shelter, basic sanitation | and medical care. | With your help our partners will make sure no one is forgotten. | To donate: www.ethiopiaid.org.uk/Ip/tigray-emergency-appeal | Ei /EthiopiaidCharity FF @Ethiopiaid ff) @ethiopiaiduk | Our Privacy Statement: The information we collect about you is used for administration purposes and for | marketing and fundraising appeals. From time to time we also analyse supporter information to ensure | that our marketing and fundraising materials are appropriate and relevant. We promise to never sell or | swap your details. Please visit our website to read our full privacy statement. You can update how we | communicate with you at any time by calling 01225 476 385 or emailing support@ethiopiaid.org.uk. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | 5 TO 70085 TO DONATE £5 | Texts cost £5 plus one standard rate message and you'll be | opting in to hear more about our work and fundraising via | telephone and SMS. If you’d like to donate but do not wish to | receive marketing communications, text TIGRAYNOINFO 5 to 70085. | Or return the donation form below to us. | First Name: | Surname: | Address: | Postcode: | Email: | EM0421 EAIDO0042 | Please keep in touch with me by email. | Aone off gift of... | [ je1o [ |e25 [ |e50 [ |suPriseuss | ‘a | enclose my cheque/postal order payable to Ethiopiaid | [| Please debit my debit / credit / charity card | corawor| TTT TTTLLLIL LLC IC | oatef CLI | Please return to: Ethiopiaid, Freepost Plus RUAS-USEB-HCUR, | Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | giftaid it HELP US MAKE MORE FROM YOUR GIFT | lam a UK taxpayer and want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | make in the future or ne | made in the past 4 years to Ethiopiaid. | | understand that.if | pay less Income Tax/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on my | donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | In order to gift aid your donation you must tick this box: And also fill in the form below: | Signature: | Title: | First Name: | | ‘| Date: | Please let us know if you want to cancel this declaration, change your name/address or if you no longer pay tax. | Surname: | We like to keep our supporters updated with information about the life-changing difference | they have made to families and communities in Ethiopia. We will use the details you have | provided to share our current fundraising (marketing appeals), newsletters and how | you can help and donate in other ways. You can update your preferences at any time by | emailing support@ethiopiaid.org.uk. | Ethiopiaid, PO BOX 5168, Bath BA1 ORR | Website: www.ethiopiaid.org.uk | Registered Charity No. 802353 (England and Wales) | Company Limited By Guarantee. 2435882 (England and Wales)",Newspaper,NA,NA
070,"ETHIOPIA EMERGENCY APPEAL | MEDECINS SANS FRONTIERES | DOCTORS WITHOUT BORDERS | Albert Vihas, MSF emergency | coordinator in Tigray, Ethiopia | Hundreds of thousands | of people have been | forced to leave their | homes in the Tigray region of | northern Ethiopia after fighting | broke out in November last year. | MSF teams have been providing medical care to | affected people since mid-December. Albert Vifias | is MSF’s emergency coordinator in Tigray. | “After several attempts, we finally entered the capital of | Tigray, Mekele, more than a month after the violence | started. The city was quiet. There was electricity, but no | basic supplies. The local hospital was running at 30 to | 40 per cent, with little medication. There were almost | no patients, which is always a very bad sign. | In Adigrat, the situation was very tense and the hospital | was in a terrible condition. Most of the staff had left, | there were hardly any medicines and no food and water. | Some patients were malnourished. | We supplied the hospital with medicines and bought | emergency food in the markets that were still open. | Together with the remaining staff, we cleaned the | building and organised waste collection. Little by little | we rehabilitated the hospital so that it could function. | NO TELEPHONES | Beyond the hospitals, around 80 or 90 per cent of the | health centres we visited were not functional. | One woman had been in labour for seven days without | being able to give birth. Her life was saved because | MSF teams distribute essential items to families displaced by the fighting. | Photograph © Claudia Blume/MSF | we were able to transport her to Mekele. I saw people | arrive at hospital on bicycles carrying a patient from | 30 km away. | The impact of the violence is visible in the buildings | and cars with bullet holes. We saw a population | locked in their homes and living in fear. Everyone | gave us pieces of paper with phone numbers written | on them and asked us to convey messages to their | families. People don’t even know if their relatives and | loved ones are okay because in many places there are | still no telephones or telecommunications. | We're very concerned about what may be happening | in rural areas. Our mobile medical teams are visiting | areas outside the main cities and we've reopened some | health centres. You feel that you offer people some | hope: the feeling that things can improve after two | months without good news.” | Hospitals, healthcare centres and clinics across | Ethiopia’s Tigray region have been looted, | vandalised and destroyed. | MSF medical teams are working to refurbish hospitals | and provide urgent medical care to people caught | up in this crisis. We are providing medical support in | emergency rooms, maternity wards, and outpatient | departments and are running mobile clinics in rural | towns and villages. We need your help now more | than ever. | MSF relies on donations | from people like you. | £40 _ could provide pain relief to 29 patients | could provide dressings kits for 95 | £115 wounded patients | could cover the costs of a doctor working | £228 in remote clinics for three days | £866 could pay for a portable ultrasound | device to help medical teams detect | underlying health issues in patients | Please give what you can to our medical | teams — they’ll give everything they can | in return. | THANK YOU | DONATE NOW | CALL 0800 055 7985 | or make your donation online at: | msf.org.uk/tigray | Scan to donate | Please give what you can to our medical teams — they'll give everything they can in return | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | |] Title Bae® | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontiéres UK mae | | Address | | | | | | OR CJ Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: | let ] | carthotername TITTTITITTIIIITEItith) oo =a | carder CITT) (TTT) CLE) CLT i oo | Expiry date [MI] / caka Today’s date | | 1/| | 1/EI J | Sins HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? requests for donations. | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% more | at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | date O/HE/O0 | NB: Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | this declaration, so that we can update our records. | gift nid uw | J | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my-donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which provides first-hand accounts of our work. | You will receive Frontline, event invitations and occasional emergency appeals with | [] Opt me in to email | RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand | accounts from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, | from combating epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | We won't allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing | purposes and we won’t bombard you with appeals. | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations, | and occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change | how you hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling | 100458 | 020 7404 6600. Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, | Chippenham SN14 6NG. Alternatively you can phone 0800 055 7985 or make your donation online at: msf.org.uk/tigray | Charity Registration Number 1026588 | MSFR0055",Newspaper,NA,NA
071,"TRANSFORMING LIVES IN ETHIOPIA | THERE ARE | OVER 1 MILLION | DISPLACED PEOPLE | AS A RESULT OF | VIOLENCE IN THE | TIGRAY REGION | OF ETHIOPIA. | PEOPLE ARE FLEEING | FOR THEIR LIVES | Communities have been devastated. Food and | water is scarce and there are significant civilian | casualties, including survivors of sexual violence. | Families have been torn apart and the turmoil is unimaginable. | In remote rural areas there is little, if any, aid within reach. | Our local partners are supporting those in desperate need | and reaching the most vulnerable with shelter, basic sanitation | and medical care. | With your help our partners will make sure no one is forgotten. | To donate: www.ethiopiaid.org.uk/Ip/tigray-emergency-appeal | EthiopiaidChari W @Ethiopiai @ethiopiaiduk | f ty Registered with Lf / P ly vg d P | fe cad a Our Privacy Statement: The information we collect about you is used for administration purposes and for | Mens Phe , marketing and fundraising appeals. From time to time we also analyse supporter information to ensure | _ swap your details. Please visit our website to read our full privacy statement. You can update how we | communicate with you at any time by calling 01225 476 385 or emailing support@ethiopiaid.org.uk. | X = “a 5 REGU LATOR that our marketing and fundraising materials are appropriate and relevant. We promise to never sell or ! | ETHIOPIEAD TEXT TIGRAY 5 TO 70085 TO DONATE £5 | Texts cost £5 plus one standard rate Npweag 2 o and you'll be | opting in to hear more about our work and fundraising via | telephone and SMS. If you'd like to donate but do not wish to | receive marketing communications, text TIGRAYNOINFO 5 to 70085. | Or return the donation form below to us. | First Name: | Surname: | Address: | Postcode: | Email: | Please keep in touch with me by email. EM0421G-_—s EAID0041 | Aone off gift of... | | |je1o { |e25 | |es50 | |supriseuse | 8 | enclose my cheque/postal order payable to Ethiopiaid | [ ] Please debit my debit / credit / charity card | | i rE aSaee Sea - EER | Signature date! | Ht | | | | ‘Please return to: Ethiopiaid, Freepost Plus RUAS-USEB-HCUR, | Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | giftaid it HELP US MAKE MORE FROM YOUR GIFT | lam a UK taxpayer and want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | make in the future or have | made in the past 4 years to Ethiopiaid. | | understand that if | pay less Income Tax/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on my | donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | In order to gift aid your donation you must tick this box: And also fill in the form below: | | Title: [First Name: r | | surname: | Date: | Please let us know if you want to cancel this declaration, change your name/address or if you no longer pay tax. | We like to keep our supporters updated with information about the life-changing difference | they have made to families and communities in Ethiopia. We will use the details you have | provided .to share our current fundraising (marketing appeals), newsletters and how | you can help and donate in other ways. You can update your preferences at any time by | emailing support@ethiopiaid.org.uk. | Ethiopiaid, PO BOX 5168, Bath BA1 ORR | Website: www.ethiopiaid.org.uk | Registered Charity No. 802353 (England and Wales) | Company Limited By Guarantee. 2435882 (England and Wales)",Newspaper,NA,NA
