079,"ETHIOPIA EMERGENCY APPEAL 4 Sevemsaze | Albert Vifias, MSF emergency | coordinator in Tigray, Ethiopia | Hundreds of thousands | of people have been | forced to leave their | homes in the Tigray region of | northern Ethiopia after fighting | broke out in November last year. | MSF teams have been providing medical care to | affected people since mid-December. Albert Viiias | is MSF’s emergency coordinator in Tigray. | “After several attempts, we finally entered the capital of | Tigray, Mekele, more than a month after the violence | started. The city was quiet. There was electricity, but no | basic supplies. The local hospital was running at 30 to | 40 per cent, with little medication. There were almost | no patients, which is always a very bad sign. | In Adigrat, the situation was very tense and the hospital | was in a terrible condition. Most of the staff had left, | there were hardly any medicines and no food and water. | Some patients were malnourished. | We supplied the hospital with medicines and bought | emergency food in the markets that were still open. | Together with the remaining staff, we cleaned the | building and organised waste collection. Little by little | we rehabilitated the hospital so that it could function. | NO TELEPHONES | Beyond the hospitals, around 80 or 90 per cent of | the health centres we visited were not functional. | One woman had been in labour for seven days without | being able to give birth. Her life was saved because we | MSF teams distribute essential items to families displaced by the fighting. | Photograph © Claudia Blume/MSF | were able to transport her to Mekele. I saw people | arrive at hospital on bicycles carrying a patient from | 30 km away. | The impact of the violence is visible in the buildings | and cars with bullet holes. We saw a population | locked in their homes and living in fear. Everyone | gave us pieces of paper with phone numbers written | on them and asked us to convey messages to their | families. People don’t even know if their relatives and | loved ones are okay because in many places there are | still no telephones or telecommunications. | We're very concerned about what may be happening | in rural areas. Our mobile medical teams are visiting | areas outside the main cities and we've reopened some | health centres. You feel that you offer people some | hope: the feeling that things can improve after two | months without good news.” | Hospitals, healthcare centres and clinics across | Ethiopia's Tigray region have been looted, | vandalised and destroyed. | MSF medical teams are working to refurbish hospitals | and provide urgent medical care to people caught | up in this crisis. We are providing medical support in | emergency rooms, maternity wards, and outpatient | departments and are running mobile clinics in rural | ever. | MSF relies on donations | from people like you. | £40 _ could provide pain relief to 29 patients | could provide dressings kits for 95 | £115 wounded patients | £228 could cover the costs of a doctor working | in remote clinics for three days | £866 could pay for a portable ultrasound | device to help medical teams detect | underlying health issues in patients | Please give what you can to our medical | a they’ll give everything they can | in : | THANK YOU | DONATE NOW | CALL 0800 055 7985 | or make your donation online at: | msf.org.uk/tigray | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | | | Title | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontiéres UK | OR C] Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: | Address | Cardholder name| |_| | | | | | | | | | | | | RARER ae | Surname | | Postcod: | cardrumber [TTT] [LITT] CLL) CLT) time | Expiry date [xx] / [xTy] Today's date | I 1/| | 1/| | a | : HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. | Signature | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? requests for donations. | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% more | at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which provides first-hand accounts of our work. | You will receive Frontline, event invitations and occasional emergency appeals with | [] Opt me in to email | RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | gift nid wv | | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | Date I/HS/OH | NB: Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | this declaration, so that we can update our records. | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand | accounts from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, | from combating epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | We won't allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing | purposes and we won’t bombard you with appeals. | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations, | and occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change | how you hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling | 020 7404 6600. Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | 100465 | Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, | Chippenham SN14 6NG. Alternatively you can phone 0800 055 7985 or make your donation online at: msf.org.uk/tigray | Charity Registration Number 1026588 MSFRO055",Newspaper,NA,NA
