092,"£9L000-Wv) | 1u¥z O8S | dOSYYOM | yg aSLuduaj}UuyZ poomM uojUeW | au}ua) UOLZN}OS e}eG FYL | Ply uelysl4yy | XSNN-AVAV-GHLY SN}d Ysodaeau4 | Help a community like Rose’s build | a life-saving dam. | pair of taps E communal water point | cement | We have 7 days to make a huge | stand with families like Rose's, and | millions more people across Kenya | whose lives are threatened daily | by storms, flash floods and drought. | Let's stand together against climate | chaos. Let's work with communities | to help build reliable water systems | - and better futures. | Every drop of water that falls is | precious. So there needs to be a | simple, sustainable and ingenious | way to successfully collect it. Earth | dams do just that. And your gift | today can help build them. | These huge basins are dug in the | ground to collect and store rain | water. It’s then piped into taps | for people like Rose to draw from. | You only have to look at Florence | and her community in the image | opposite to see the difference | an earth dam can make. | Crops grow, land can be farmed, | and families no longer go hungry. | People stand strong and are | better prepared for whatever | life throws at them. | tire | ieee ut lol we | The recent | pandemic has | made a lack of | << water more critical | for people like Rose. | Will you stand against | climate chaos with | , eople in Keny 2 | 1. 95 | You may never meet a more | determined grandmother than | Rose. At 68 years old she makes | a six-hour round trip every other | day to collect water for her family | so they can farm, drink and wash. | She’s hungry and weary but she | goes on. Because she has to. Her | grandchildren’s lives depend on it. | However, she won't have the strength | to do this journey forever. | Kitui County in Eastern Kenya was already in | the grip of a climate emergency. Severe drought | followed by extreme and unpredictable changes | in weather has destroyed crops, killed livestock, | and continues to threaten livelihoods. | Then the pandemic hit. | We know ourselves that water | and washing hands has been | vital in helping to save lives | during the pandemic. But what | if there isn’t any? What if the | nearest water source is miles | away, by foot? What then? This | climate crisis and the pandemic | impacts us all. But people living in | poverty, like Rose and her family, | get hit the hardest. Today, we | can make a stand with people | in Kenya. | e change | | Even before the pandemic hit, | unreliable and unpredictable rainfall | made life a struggle. Today we can | stand against this chaos. Together | we can work with communities like | Rose's to make sure everyone has | easy access to reliable water sources - | now and in the future. | nD FO ey 4 OS5 | Ace | ner f eebeat | mose anda ft er tram) LV | oe a A a - We | Im ana ad Deter ire | Here’s my gift of | | e10 | |e42 | Je335 L_Jother £ | r projects St | such as those featured and where we consider the need is greatest | We will use your donations for proj | Title First Name Surname | Address Postcod | Please make your cheque postal order CAF voucher™ | payable to: Christian Aid. (Please do not send cash by post) *delete as appropriate | debit my Mastercard Visa Maestro CAF Charity Card | Card no. (Piease copy the long number along the middle of your card Start date Expiry date | ssue no Today’s date | Mae pnature | giftaid | Gift Aid your donation to make it worth 25% more, at no extra cost to you. | want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | n the future or t Jate | t Aid. | an Please notify Christian Aid if you: | We would love to tell you how your support is making a difference! | are happy to hear from us by email or telephone, please provide those details below | Ne will keep you updated about our work and the difference your support is making. We promise | lever to share your details with any nisation for marketing purposes. For more information | please visit caid.org.uk/privacy | To save paper, if we have your email address we will send you a thank you by email. | I'd like to know more about leaving a gift in my Will to safeguard this vital work for the future. | Please fold and seal your completed form and send it to | Freepost Plus RTHB-AKAE-UUSX, Christian Aid, The Data Solution “AM-000767 | Centre, Manton Wood Enterprise Park, WORKSOP S80 2RT. | (FR) Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
093,"ETHIOPIA EMERGENCY APPEAL | MEDECINS SANS FRONTIERES | DOCTORS WITHOUT BORDERS | Albert Vihas, MSF emergency | coordinator in Tigray, Ethiopia | Hundreds of thousands | of people have been | forced to leave their | homes in the Tigray region of | northern Ethiopia after fighting | broke out in November last year. | MSF teams have been providing medical care to | affected people since mid-December. Albert Viiias | is MSF’s emergency coordinator in Tigray. | “After several attempts, we finally entered the capital of | Tigray, Mekele, more than a month after the violence | started. The city was quiet. There was electricity, but no | basic supplies. The local hospital was running at 30 to | 40 per cent, with little medication. There were almost | no patients, which is always a very bad sign. | In Adigrat, the situation was very tense and the hospital | was in a terrible condition. Most of the staff had left, | there were hardly any medicines and no food and water. | Some patients were malnourished. | We supplied the hospital with medicines and bought | emergency food in the markets that were still open. | Together with the remaining staff, we cleaned the | building and organised waste collection. Little by little | we rehabilitated the hospital so that it could function. | NO TELEPHONES | Beyond the hospitals, around 80 or 90 per cent of the | health centres we visited were not functional. | One woman had been in labour for seven days without | being able to give birth. Her life was saved because | MSF teams distribute essential items to families displaced by the fighting. | Photograph © Claudia Blume/MSF | we were able to transport her to Mekele. I saw people | arrive at hospital on bicycles carrying a patient from | 30 km away. | The impact of the violence is visible in the buildings | and cars with bullet holes. We saw a population | locked in their homes and living in fear. Everyone | gave us pieces of paper with phone numbers written | on them and asked us to convey messages to their | families. People don’t even know if their relatives and | loved ones are okay because in many places there are | still no telephones or telecommunications. | Were very concerned about what may be happening | in rural areas. Our mobile medical teams are visiting | areas outside the main cities and we've reopened some | health centres. You feel that you offer people some | hope: the feeling that things can improve after two | months without good news.’ | Hospitals, healthcare centres and clinics across | Ethiopia’s Tigray region have been looted, | vandalised and destroyed. | MSF medical teams are working to refurbish hospitals | and provide urgent medical care to people caught | up in this crisis. We are providing medical support in | emergency rooms, maternity wards, and outpatient | departments and are running mobile clinics in rural | towns and villages. We need your help now more | than ever. | MSF relies on donations | from people like you. | £115 | could provide pain relief to 29 patients | could provide dressings kits for 95 | wounded patients | could cover the costs of a doctor working | in remote clinics for three days | £228 | could pay for a portable ultrasound | device to help medical teams detect | underlying health issues in patients | £866 | Please give what you can to our medical | teams — they’ll give everything they can | in return. | THANK YOU | DONATE NOW | CALL 0800 055 7985 | or make your donation online at: | msf.org.uk/tigray | Scan to donate | Please give what you can to our medical teams — they’ll give everything they can in return | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | | Title ZBBEEE| | Surname | | | | | | | | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontieres UK | Address era et | OR CJ Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: | | | | | Cardholder name | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | | E} a | | | Postcode ne Et | Cadrumbers | | TT) Lltd Pee ei] Email QBEEREDZ | Expiry date ET / [yT¥] Today's date | l/| | l/| | | | 5 HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. | Signature | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? requests for donations. | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% more | at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | date JO/OB/OO | NB: Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | this declaration, so that we can update our records. | giftaid | C] | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations, | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which provides first-hand accounts of our work. | You will receive Frontline, event invitations and occasional emergency appeals with | [] Opt me in to email | RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand | accounts from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, | from combating epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | We won't allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing | purposes and we won’t bombard you with appeals. | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations, | and occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change | how you hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling | 100460 | 020 7404 6600. Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, | Chippenham SN14 6NG. Alternatively you can phone 0800 055 7985 or make your donation online at: msf.org.uk/tigray | Charity Registration Number 1026588",Newspaper,NA,NA
