099,"1) ZINAING Ol0yg | ‘A GIFT IN YOUR WILL | 9 MY PROTECTION AT SEA | Matt Church, Volunteer Crew Member, Penarth Lifeboat Station | You can help RNLI volunteers like Matt face the full force of the sea with a gift in your Will. | You can provide the kit and training that keeps them safe, day or night. | 6 in 10 launches are only possible thanks to gifts in Wills. And it could provide the training brave volunteers like Matt | Countless lives saved because of the generosity of people need to become a lifesaver. | like you. It's a gift that won't be forgotten - because your name will be | A gift in your Will could provide the equipment that protects added to the side of a lifeboat. So you'll always be a part of our | our volunteers from the elements. It could fuel the lifeboat lifesaving family. | so they can race to the rescue. | Find out how you can leave a lifesaving legacy. | Return the form below, visit RNLI.org/Express or call 0300 300 0062 | To receive a free no obligation ‘Gifts in Wills Guide’, fill in the form below and send to: ‘Freepost RNLI Wills’ | (no stamp or other address details required) | LLOLZV-W1 | Title: Full Name: Keep in touch | Your support saves lives, and we look forward to keeping in touch | es with you by post and phone, sharing our news, activities and appeals. | Would you like to receive our emails and text messages too? | Post code: Phone: LI Yes, !'m happy to hear from you by email | C] Yes, I’m happy to hear from you by text | Email: | Even if you have received our communications in the past, | Privacy Notice: Wewal always store your shinee we'll make sure we honour the preferences you express here. | and they will only be used by the RNLI, RNLI Shop and RNLI College. F | Stoarsita ray ees bn ink hi eheieh peels eetalo ta own the scarce If you would rather not hear from us, or would like to change | best service possible. We will only allow your information to be used by FUNDRAISING how we contact you, please get in touch. Just visit | suppliers working on our behalf and we'll only share it if required to do so REGULATOR RNLI.org/preferences or call 0300 300 9918. | by law. For full details see our Privacy Policy at RNLI.org/PrivacyPolicy or | contact our Supporter Experience Team on 0300 300 9918. | The RNLI is the charity that saves lives at sea. The Royal National Lifeboat Institution, a charity registered in England and Wales (209603), Scotland (SC037736), the Republic of Ireland | (CHY 2678 and 20003326), the Bailiwick of Jersey (14), the Isle of Man (1308 and 006329F), the Bailiwick of Guernsey and Alderney, of West Quay Road, Poole, Dorset, BH15 1HZ",Newspaper,NA,NA
