123,"YEMEN ON | THE BRINK | OF FAMINE | GIVE £143 NOW TO HELP DISPLACED | FAMILIES BUY THE FOOD AND ESSENTIALS | THAT CAN SAVE THEIR LIVES. | After more than six years of war, Yemen is Even before the coronavirus pandemic hit, | now heading towards the worst famine the Yemen was the world’s worst humanitarian | world has seen for decades. crisis, with 80% of the population dependent | on aid for their day-to-day survival. | The intensifying conflict, along with a | fuel embargo, has seen the economy | collapse with the prices of food and other | commodities skyrocketing. | Malnutrition rates are at record highs. | Thousands of children under-5 are severely | malnourished. They are children with distended | bellies, emaciated limbs and blank stares — | they are starving to death. | © UNHCR/Marie-Joélle Jeane | People who have lost their homes in the | conflict are the most vulnerable — they are | up to four times more likely to face hunger. | And 79% of those displaced are women and | children. Many parents are going without | food so their children can eat, others have no | But it’s not too late. If you act now, you can | help save lives. UK for UNHCR urgently needs | your support to give the most vulnerable | families lifesaving Emergency Payments, | so they can buy basic food like rice, flour and | cooking oil and essentials like medicine | income at all. Jean-Nicolas Beuze, UNHCR’s | and water. representative in Yemen, says: “Yemenis can’t £1 43 6 | With a gift of £143 today, you could provide afford to worry about coronavirus. They are can provide | an Emergency Payment and help save lives. too worried about not having any food to | The £143 payment is based on the cost of a feed their children.” an Emergency Payment | ‘Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of food This is happening right now. UNHCR teams on to help a displaced | and household essentials, and has proved the ground are doing everything in their power | the most effective way of helping families to help displaced people survive. But with family of six to buy | get enough food to sustain themselves. their work critically underfunded, they can’t e | For a family on the edge of starvation, save lives without you. Please give £143 or food Fy are | essentials. | it means survival. whatever you can afford today. | Give now at unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in the form below | Four-year-old Umaimah, whose family was displaced | 19 months ago. Her father collects tin cans to sell, | which barely brings in enough to pay for food. | I would like to give: [_]¢143. [_lothers__ : Please return this form along with your cheque to: | (_] | enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don't need a stamp) | [_] | would like to make a donation by debit/credit card Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate iftaid ite | Card no. Expiry date CI would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p 7 | pea | | Ss ] If Be [ | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | q J | | | | | hares J /| os it | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand | ———__—_—__—_— ; that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my | Signature Date donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax | it and VAT do not qualify. | =e ST ; eae ot l= tou eh If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | _] Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Title “Firstname 2 Last name Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | Address a= : donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | Postcode other events. You can read more ab