 McKean, Director of Programmes, Funding and Operations. to buy it. | _ ae | Yes, ‘I want to help prevent a child dying: from the | y | MERCY | effects of malnutrition. CORPS | There are three ways you can make your gift: | ) Go online: europe.mercycorps.org/ yemen-children | ) Speak to Supporter Care, Mon-Fri, 9am-—5Spm: 0131 662 2377 | ) Complete the form below, and return in the enclosed envelope or send to 96/3 Commercial Quay, Edinburgh, EH6 6LX | | would like to give O£100 OD£15 (£45 (My choice of amount: | Ol enclose a cheque/postal order/CAF voucher made out to Mercy Corps OR | CO Please debit my: (J Mastercard [) Visa ()CAF Card [1 Maestro | Card holder’s name: | Card number: | Start date: fi Expiry date: / Issue number: (Shaded boxes Maestro only) | 3-digit security number: Signature(s): Date: vf i | Title: First Name: Surname: | Address’: | Postcode: | “If you wish to Gift Aid your gift, please make sure to provide your address. V\ | Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. iftaid it | (Yes, | am a UK taxpayer and | would like Mercy Corps to claim the tax on all qualifying donations J | | have made in the past 4 years, as well as any future donations. | understand that if | pay less Income/Capital Gains Tax than | the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Gift Aid will be | used to fund Mercy Corps’ general work. | (1) No, | am not a tax payer. | Please notify Mercy Corps if: you want to cancel this declaration; your name or home address has changed; you no longer pay | sufficient income and/or capital gains tax. | Together, a better world is possible - Stay connected with Mercy Corps. | Our work is only possible because of the support and dedication of people like you. As part of our global community, we would like | to keep you up-to-date with our progress in the field, new fundraising activities and ways you can take action. Please read our privacy | statement available at europe.mercycorps.org/privacy for more information. | Please add your email and tick the box to confirm you'd like to hear about our work and fundraising activities. 1) | Email: | If you would prefer not to hear from Mercy Corps by post please tick here. (1) | Please remember you can update your preferences at any time by emailing fundraising-europe@mercycorps.org | or by calling 0131 662 2377. | coop | FUNDRAISING | Funds will be used wherever the need is greatest Registered Charity Number SCO30289 20210401-IG-ISTURRB | Yemen is vast and mountainous. Families can find | relative safety from conflict in more remote places but it is | challenging to get medical care. Travel is nearly impossible | for those who are very sick. | Our Mobile Health Clinics are a lifeline to many. Just one | clinic is able to serve 10 villages, giving invaluable support | to 3,000 - 4,000 people who would otherwise be left without | medical help. | It costs around £3,700 to run one Mobile Health Clinic for | a month. It is vital that these clinics remain staffed and | equipped so they can continue the important work of treating | children in Yemen who have no access to medical care. | Mothers and children wait at a Mercy | Corps clinic, 2018. | Together, people like you are making a difference. | could help | treat a child under five | who has severe acute | malnutrition for | up to eight weeks. | could go towards | a hygiene kit to help | children stay healthy | and stop disease. | could help | a family access food | for a week when Som | they cannot afford <es | to buy it. | | We are working to prevent disease from taking hold. Thanks | to our supporters, we are providing hygiene kits including | soap, clean water and washing powder to help families stay | clean. In remote areas we are rehabilitating and building | water points that give access to safe water for families in | nearby villages. | And for families that cannot afford to buy food we provide | vouchers for food baskets that they can use to buy their most | essential needs. 2018, children fill up water cans at o water | 5 station Mercy Corps built. | Last year we reached over one million people in Yemen. ‘seunmeswsssmmmsemm | People fleeing conflict, living in poverty or without access | to healthcare are especially vulnerable to the impacts | of the COVID-19 pandemic. | Your gift could help provide emergency supplies to help | communities protect themselves against the spread | of disease - items such as soap and clean water are more | important than ever before. Your support could help bring | much needed food and aid to vulnerable families and | communities - in Yemen and around the world. | COVID-19 is putting vulnerable people at more risk | than ever. Please help them today. | MERCY | CORPS | THANK YOU Z Lilt | Freepost RTZT-EJJC-CULS | Mercy Corps | 96/3 Commercial Street | Edinburgh | EH6 6LX",Newspaper,NA,NA
132,"YEMEN ON THE | BRINK OF FAMINE | GIVE £143 NOW TO HELP DISPLACED FAMILIES BUY THE. | FOOD AND ESSENTIALS THAT CAN SAVE THEIR LIVES. | After more than six years of war, Yemen is | now heading towards the worst famine the | world has seen for decades. Malnutrition | rates are at record highs. Thousands of | children under-5 are severely malnourished. | But it’s not too late. If you act now, you can help | save lives. UK for UNHCR urgently needs your | support to give the most vulnerable families | lifesaving Emergency Payments, so they can | buy basic food like rice, flour and cooking oil | and essentials like medicine and water. | With a gift of £143 today, you could provide | an Emergency Payment and help save lives. | The £143 payment is based on the cost of a | ‘Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of food and | household essentials. For a family on the sy | edge of starvation, it means survival. Four-year-old Umaimah, whose family was displaced | 19 months ago. Her father collects tin cans to sell, | Even before the coronavirus pandemic, which barely brings in enough to pay for food. | Yemen was the world’s worst humanitarian | crisis, with 80% of the population worried about not having any food to | dependent on aid for their day-to-day feed their children.” | survival. The intensifying conflict, along | with a fuel embargo, has seen the economy | collapse with the prices of food and other | commodities skyrocketing. | This is happening right now. UNHCR | teams on the ground are doing everything | in their power to help displaced people | survive. But with their work critically | Jean-Nicolas Beuze, UNHCR’s representative | underfunded, they can’t save lives without | in Yemen, says: “Yemenis can’t afford to you. Please give £143 or whatever you | worry about coronavirus. They are too can afford today. | £4 43 could provide an Emergency Payment to help a | displaced family of six to buy food and essentials. | Give now at | unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883 or fill in and return the form below | I would like to give: be £143 Pa Other 6 Se re | [_] 1 enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | [_] | would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. Expiry date | WE 2 Milo BS Lab Bs ka ge cl | eae | | / R? | CT Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title First name Last name | Address Sa A Ae took ooh Bo ee fk Ss Ac eee wor | pbsteode: | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR'’s work: CJ By email C By phone | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | (1 1 would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p for each Rie fas au | £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand that if! pay less | income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is | my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team on | 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | ras as contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | Registered with (() ) | “See (UNHCR | < iow. Scan this | : =~<— The UN Refugee Agency | QR code to United Kingdom for UNHCR | oh sie donate online | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415).