134,"£9L000-Wv) | 1u¥z O8S | dOSYYOM | yg aSLuduaj}UuyZ poomM uojUeW | au}ua) UOLZN}OS e}eG FYL | Ply uelysl4yy | XSNN-AVAV-GHLY SN}d Ysodaeau4 | Help a community like Rose’s build | a life-saving dam. | pair of taps E communal water point | cement | We have 7 days to make a huge | stand with families like Rose's, and | millions more people across Kenya | whose lives are threatened daily | by storms, flash floods and drought. | Let's stand together against climate | chaos. Let's work with communities | to help build reliable water systems | - and better futures. | Every drop of water that falls is | precious. So there needs to be a | simple, sustainable and ingenious | way to successfully collect it. Earth | dams do just that. And your gift | today can help build them. | These huge basins are dug in the | ground to collect and store rain | water. It’s then piped into taps | for people like Rose to draw from. | You only have to look at Florence | and her community in the image | opposite to see the difference | an earth dam can make. | Crops grow, land can be farmed, | and families no longer go hungry. | People stand strong and are | better prepared for whatever | life throws at them. | tire | ieee ut lol we | Will you stand against | climate chaos bebe | seople in Kenya: | : 2 he a , <> | Sag, ~~"" — ef : x | | Kitui County in Eastern Kenya was already in | the grip of a climate emergency. Severe drought | followed by extreme and unpredictable changes | in weather has destroyed crops, killed livestock, | and continues to threaten livelihoods. | Then the pandemic hit. | We know ourselves that water | and washing hands has been | vital in helping to save lives | during the pandemic. But what | if there isn’t any? What if the | nearest water source is miles | away, by foot? What then? This | climate crisis and the pandemic | impacts us all. But people living in | poverty, like Rose and her family, | get hit the hardest. Today, we | can make a stand with people | in Kenya. | The recent | pandemic has | made a lack of | water more critical | for people like Rose. | You may never meet a more | determined grandmother than | Rose. At 68 years old she makes | a six-hour round trip every other | day to collect water for her family | so they can farm, drink and wash. | She’s hungry and weary but she | goes on. Because she has to. Her | grandchildren’s lives depend on it. | However, she won't have the strength | to do this journey forever. | '‘RParates | Even before the pandemic hit, | unreliable and unpredictable rainfall | made life a struggle. Today we can | stand against this chaos. Together | we can work with communities like | Rose's to make sure everyone has | easy access to reliable water sources - | now and in the future. | Here’s my gift of | | e10 | |ea2 | |e335 | Jother £ | We will use your donations for pre such as those featured and where we consider the need is greatest | Title First Name Surname | Addre: Pos | | Please make your cheque postal order CAF voucher™ | payable to: Christian Aid. (Please do not send cash by post) *delete as appropriate | debit my Mastercard Visa Maestro CAF Charity Card | Card no. (Piease copy the long number along the middle of your card Start date Expiry date | ssue no Today’s date | Mae gnature | giftaid a | Gift Aid your donation to make it worth 25% more, at no extra cost to you. | want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | n the future or t | Christ | Christiar Please notify Christian Aid if you: | pay less *wantt ance! this ceciaratior | e address | amount of Gift Aid ¢ | tax year itism | We would love to tell you how your support is making a difference! | j are happy to hear from us by email or telephone, please provide those details below | We will keep you updated about our work and the dif : J: | lever to share your details with any other organisation for marketing purposes. For more information | please visit caid.org.uk/privacy | To save paper, if we have your email address we 