140,"Questions about smear tests? | We're here for you. | Coronavirus has changed a lot of things. | lf you've been invited for cervical screening (a | Smear test), you may have questions or | concerns about how your appointment will | work now. | Whether it's questions about going for a test, | or you want to talk about your results, we | offer free, confidential information and | Support. | No question is too big or too small.",Newspaper,NA,NA
141,"Do you know | the symptoms — | of ovarian | cancer? | » Persistent bloated tummy? | » Always feeling full? | » Tummy pain? | » Needing to wee more? | The sooner cancer is diagnosed, | the easier it is to treat. | If you regularly experience any of | these symptoms and they’re not | normal for you, it’s important | to see your GP. | Raise awareness. Fund research. Save lives. | Registered charity numbers 1125038 (England and Wales).and SCo42920 (Scotland). | Target Ovarian Cancer is a company limited by guarantee, registered in England and Wales (no. 6619983). | Registered office: 2 Angel Gate, London EC1V 2PT. | TARGET | OVARIAN | CANCER",Newspaper,NA,NA
142,"YEMEN ON | THE BRINK | OF FAMINE | GIVE £143 NOW TO HELP DISPLACED | FAMILIES BUY THE FOOD AND ESSENTIALS | THAT CAN SAVE THEIR LIVES. | After more than six years of war, Yemen is | now heading towards the worst famine the | world has seen for decades. | Malnutrition rates are at record highs. | Thousands of children under-5 are severely | malnourished. They are children with distended | bellies, emaciated limbs and blank stares — | they are starving to death. | But it’s not too late. If you act now, you can | help save lives. UK for UNHCR urgently needs | your support to give the most vulnerable | families lifesaving Emergency Payments, | so they can buy basic food like rice, flour and | cooking oil and essentials like medicine | and water. | With a gift of £143 today, you could provide . | an Emergency Payment and help save lives. | The £143 payment is based on the cost of a feed their children.” | ‘Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of food | and household essentials, and has proved | the most effective way of helping families | get enough food to sustain themselves. | For a family on the edge of starvation, | it means survival. | Even before the coronavirus pandemic hit, | Yemen was the world’s worst humanitarian | crisis, with 80% of the population dependent | on aid for their day-to-day survival. | The intensifying conflict, along with a | fuel embargo, has seen the economy | collapse with the prices of food and other | commodities skyrocketing. | People who have lost their homes in the , ) | conflict are the most vulnerable — they are | up to four times more likely to face hunger. | And 79% of those displaced are women and | children. Many parents are going without | food so their children can eat, others have no | income at all. Jean-Nicolas Beuze, UNHCR’s | representative in Yemen, says: “Yemenis can’t | afford to worry about coronavirus. They are | too worried about not having any food to | This is happening right now. UNHCR teams on | the ground are doing everything in their power | to help displaced people survive. But with | their work critically underfunded, they can’t | save lives without you. Please give £143 or | whatever you can afford today. | © UNHCR/Marie-Joélle Jean-Charles | Four-year-old Umaimah, whose family was displaced | 19 months ago. Her father collects tin cans to sell, | which barely brings in enough to pay for food. | £143 could provide | an Emergency Payment | to help a displaced | family of six to buy | food and essentials. | Give now at Unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in the form below | | would like to give: | £143 [ | Other € | [_] | enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | [_] | would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. ox | | Signature E | Date | CO Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title _ a Ee First name Last name in t=* a we | Address * cae ee es mee | Ste a: Postcode #5 | Email Z < Oke, eege SN eas | Phone | Please tell us if:you are happy to hear about UNHCR'’s work: C] By email ist By phone | Registered with ‘ | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate iftaid it | C1 would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p pe | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand | that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my | donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax | and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities.and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | (\) UNHCR | The UN Refugee Agency | United Kingdom for UNHCR | P21YEOBA2 | Scan this | QR code to | donate online",Newspaper,NA,NA
