145,"BritishRedCross | Observer readers, people =/ | in India need your help. | Please send to: Global Coronavirus Appeal; ref 175914, Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ, British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, | CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG % | | would like to make a donation of £20[] £40[] £60] £100[] Othere| | | (_]| enclose a cheque, made payable to British Red Cross OR [_]Please debit my Visa/Mastercard/CAF Charity card with the amount specified | card number! TT TILT TT ILET TELL] xin date [T/T] | Title Forename Surname | Address | Postcode | Phone number** **Please only give us your telephone number if you are happy for us to | call you about our work and how you can donate and help in other ways. | 9 iftaid uw Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. | Cl am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, as well as any future donations, until | notify them otherwise. | Please tick. | understand that if | pay less income/capital gains tax than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations in the tax year in which they are received, it is my responsibility | to pay any difference. Please remember to let us know of any changes to your tax’status, including changes to your name or address, or if you need to cancel this agreement. | Keeping in touch Your support makes a life-changing difference to people in crisis. We write to our supporters to update you about the work of the British Red Cross, and how you can help and donate in | other ways. You can change the way we contact you at any time by visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch or calling Freephone 0800 2800 491. | Privacy statement The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and will use personal data for the purpose it was collected or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for example, to provide | goods, services or information you have requested or to administer donations or services we provide. We may also analyse data we collect to better understand the people who support us or those who use or deliver our | services. Sometimes this means us combining that data with information from reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor communications and services in a more focused and cost-effective way, as well as better | meeting your needs and the needs of others like you. However, we will never do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with previously expressed privacy preferences. | For full details about how we use personal data, our legal basis for doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy. | The Global Coronavirus. Appeal covers countries currently affected and those potentially affected in the future by Covid-19. | At this current time we are directing donations to this appeal-to the Red Cross and Red Crescent coronavirus response in | India. In the very unlikely event that we raise more money than can be reasonably and efficiently spent, any surplus funds | will be used to prepare for and respond to other humanitarian disasters anywhere in the world. For more information visit Registered with a powe r | redcross.org.uk | “Texts cost £10 +1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile FU N DRAISING of ki Nn d n es Ss | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), REGULATOR | Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430).",Newspaper,NA,NA
146,"wd WaterAid MM till | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST | WaterAid For every £1 you give, we spend... | York House | Wetherby Road | Long Marston | YORK | YO26 7NH | 77p on clean water, decent | toilets and good hygiene | 23p on fundraising* | Thank you for | changing lives | It's a big ask It’s a big ask | Here goes. | We need your help to bring clean water to | everyone, everywhere within a generation. | I'm about to ask you to get behind something that will | change the world, forever. That may sound daunting but | I need you to carry on reading, because together we really | can bring clean water to everyone. | Gulp. I'll start at the beginning. | It starts with a child like Ibrahim, in Sierra Leone. The water | you see him collecting is filthy and makes him dangerously ill. | But he has no choice, it's the only water there is and every sip | could kill him. Just like it kills over 800 children every day. This | has to change. | But, here’s the good news. We've already worked in Ibrahim's | village, helping to bring the community clean water that can | save lives. But that’s not enough. We need to bring water | to many, many more children around the world. Just £2 a | month from you today could help make that happen. | Together we can help every child - until | we've helped them all. | It doesn’t stop there. There are 785 million people like Ibrahim in the world who still do not | have clean water. Reaching them all might seem impossible, but we have to think big. Because | if more people - like you - give £2 a month then, child by child, village by village, we know it’s | possible to get clean water, decent toilets and good hygiene to everyone in our lifetime. | If everyone, everywhere has clean | water, children like Ibrahim won't | risk their lives drinking filthy | deadly water. Please start giving | a small gift of £2 a month today. | How can I be so sure? Because I know how powerful we can be as a team - together. | We work with local experts and communities to install reliable, long-lasting pipes, pumps and | taps. In fact, we reach almost 1,000 people with clean water every single day. We do everything | we can to ensure governments around the world deliver on their clean water promises too. | So what do you say? | Just imagine that day, when a child like Ibrahim tastes clean water for the | first time. When his mother doesn’t have to worry that the next sip could kill | him. Then imagine the moment we reach every child, everywhere. | Let's bring clean water to the world within a generation. Please fill in the | donation form to start giving £2 a month today, every penny counts. | Thank you. | Johnty Gray, WaterAid UK. | Since we visited Ibrahim, WaterAid has delivered clean water to his community. However, millions of children | still face the terrible circumstances and choices highlighted above. | WaterAid | Call 0300 123 4341"" | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Visit wateraid.org/uk/gulp | **As of 2019/20 WaterAid Annual Report | Registered charity numbers 288701 (England and Wales) | and SC039479 (Scotland). | MOISTEN HERE | Yes, let’s bring clean water to the world, | starting with a child like Ibrahim. WaterAid | £10 a month could save | aha a big In just 1 | £5 a month could save | children’s lives. | | £2 a month could save | children’s lives. In just | 1OMN< | Here's my life-changing giftof: £2 £5 £10 Surprise us!£ a month fornernoxce | Startingonthe 1st 15th 25th Month Year peedalche eld | Title: First name: Last name: | Home address: | Postcode: | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid without your full name and address. | You can hear how you change lives. We hope you will fill out your contact details below | to hear more about children like Ibrahim, fundraising, and opportunities to get involved. If you | are happy to hear from us by phone and email, please let us know your details: | Tel no. (home/mobile): Email: | Many people love to receive postal updates. Tick if you'd prefer not to _ | * WaterAid and WaterAid Trading will use your personal details to communicate with you in the ways you have agreed to, and as | explained in our Privacy Policy. | + We may use the information you share with us and background information about you that we obtain from publicly available sources | to carry out analysis (sometimes using suppliers) to tailor our communications to be more appropriate and relevant to your interests. | * You can withdraw your consent at any time. For full details, including information about your privacy rights, see our Privacy Policy at | www.wateraid.org/privacy | To change your preferences, or request to stop receiving communications please contact us on | 020 7793 4594 or at supportercare@wateraid.org 211AE/01N | WaterAid Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by direct debit. | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST, WaterAid, York House, York YO26 7NH. (00 NOT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) Beet. | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society Service user number | 406789 | Reference (to be completed by WaterAid) | To the Manager: Bank/building society | Branch address: | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please pay WaterAid | Direct Debits from the account detailed in this erelethipen. to | the Gra etd assured by the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand | ede Instruction may remain with WaterAid and, if so, details will | be passed electronically to my bank/building society. | Postcode: | Name(s) of account holder(s): | Signature(s) | Bank/building society account number Branch sort code x | Date | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account. | JY¥JH N3LSIOW",Newspaper,NA,NA
147,"“i Humanists UK | SOCIETY | 100,000 members and | supporters | Will you join our movement too? | As we emerge from the pandemic, the world | around us seems more intolerant and divisive | than ever. Now, some of our most basic values | are under threat - free speech, compassion, | kindness, reason, and tolerance. | But there is something you can do to protect | | the values of the Enlightenment, fairness, and | rational thought. | For just £4 per month, you can promote rational and | positive changes, and join a community of | like-minded individuals. Together, we can make sure | everyone is treated equally, regardless of | their religion or belief. | ONLINE | BY PHONE | We are a voice for non-religious people in this | country. We support everybody who wants to lead | a good, fulfilling life without religious beliefs - and | what's more, we've been doing it for 125 years! | In that time, we've played a key role in major social | reforms, such as legalising same-sex marriage and | making abortions legal, safe, and accessible across | the UK. But we've still got a lot to do! | 53% of British adults now say they’re not | religious. We campaign on their behalf, fighting | unfair, religiously motivated bias -— in politics, the | “media, in education, and beyond. And you can | help us do that, by joining Humanists UK today. | 359 Moreland St, London | EC1V 8BB | 125 years of | Humanists UK",Newspaper,NA,NA
148,"PLEASE VISIT | WWW.HELPSTVINCENT.COM | ST VINCENT AND THE GRENADINES DISASTER RELIEF EFFORT | On 9th April 2021 | La Soufriere, the - | volcano on the | Caribbean island of | St Vincent erupted. | The eruption of the volcano has had devastating consequences | for thousands of people living nearby, who were evacuated | and are now in shelters. Whilst no injuries occurred, homes | and livelihoods have been destroyed and many people have | been left with nothing. | Caribbean countries and charities have been quick to offer | supplies and aid but you can help the people of St Vincent | and the Grenadines by donating via the Government National | Emergency Management Organisation (NEMO). | Thank You for Your Help. |",Newspaper,NA,NA
149,"> = pera ae > | Sightsavers : Sightsavers | 4 7) we | Nalukena geteeW x j N | cae | | SJ@ADS]YBIS | nowwn | zacc- | a+ 3 3 0 | -Fvuv0vTS | UO ® et | anor a8 | 2 aun ® | oz < | on=t oo | Soo 4 | I< OW | Will you Sian . | help protect | alukena | children fro wy bs | | Just £5 from you) | could save her sight. | could save her sight. | www.sightsavers.org/closer | | www.sightsavers.org/ p's www.sightsavers.org/closer | Trachoma steals sight with every blink... | Trachoma is an infection that's both agonising, and blinding. | At first, it makes your eyes itchy and sore. But if left | untreated, it develops into the more severe trichiasis - | which steals your sight blink by painful blink... | Nalukena had suffered from trachoma since birth - and | at just two years old, it was clear she was in real pain. | Her devastated parents did all they could to help their | little girl, but they didn't understand what was wrong. | They just knew it was getting worse. | Without help, | sight altogether. | You can save children from a life of pain | That’s why your support today is so vital. Together, we | can reach a whole class of children like Nalukena with | sight-saving treatment - and one day eliminate this cruel | infection for good. | From painful trachoma... | £5 could protect a class of children | Thankfully, we could help Nalukena with an antibiotic called | Zithromax* - which costs just 15p per treatment, and has the | power to stop trachoma in its tracks. | Now, Nalukena no longer has to live in pain, and can look forward | to a happy future. But there are still millions of children across | Africa who are moving closer to blindness each day. It's vital | we can treat them, before they lose their sight forever. | Your gift will save children’s sight | Just £5 from you is all it takes to provide Zithromax” for | a class of 33 children - saving them from blindness, and | moving us closer to our goal of eliminating trachoma by 2025. | To make a donation, simply complete the form | opposite and return it in the attached envelope, | give online, or call O800 298 2200 today. | little Nalukena was at risk of losing her | ...to blinding trichiasis | Trachoma starts with a | bite from an infected fly. @ | Will you send £5 today and save a class of children from blinding trachoma? | The eyes start to itch and weep, @ <p The eyelids then turn inwards, causing 4 <p> This condition is trichiasis, | and become very sore in sunlight. the eyelashes to scrape the eye. which eventually steals sight. | 4& DETACH HERE & | & DETACH HERE & | Yes, | want to give £5 to stop trachoma and save the sight of children like Nalukena | Title First name Surname | Full home address | Postcode | Phone number | Email | Are you happy to receive updates and find out how you can help by email or telephone? | If so, please fill in your details above. | We want you to be really proud of the work you're helping make ; | happen and will be in touch from time to time with updates about ThroughGiftAid,any dit | how your support is changing lives. To do this, we'll use the details donation you give will gifte | you've provided but promise never to sell or share your data. be worth 25% more. | If you'd rather not hear from us, please let us know by emailing tam a UK taxpayer and | would like | info@sightsavers.org or calling 01444 446600. Sightsavers to reclaim the tax paid on all my | past, present and future. | understand | [ 7 P : | | would like to make a donation of el [TT J-TT) that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains | Tax in the current tax year than the amount | Please make cheque/postal order payable to Sightsavers tase poner of Gift Aid claimed on my donations, it is my | Or debit my: O MasterCard OVisa 0 CAF SEND CASH responsibility to pay any difference. | SC LILI ET LICE Lt (CJ I'd like Sightsavers to claim | Gift Aid on my donations. | eC LIC) be CLC | [Name on card | s! | [Signature | Date | Your donation will be used to support our work whereve