168,"YEMEN EMERGENCY APPEAL 4 Serexozzz | vaesthetist Lenka Ce | tal in Ye | | ALISON CRIADO-PEREZ | IS AN MSF NURSE WHO | | WORKED IN MARIB | The conflict in Yemen is now in its sixth year. In Marib | in central Yemen, nearly three million people have been | displaced from their homes and are living in makeshift | camps close to the frontline. Pregnant women and | children are in desperate need of medical care. | “When we arrived in Marib, we found the local hospitals | overwhelmed by the sheer number of people and by an | influx of war-wounded. Around 2.7 million people are | in the province now, many of them displaced from their | homes elsewhere and looking for a safe haven. | People were living in makeshift shelters made of plastic | and metal sheets. There were no latrines, just pits dug in | the ground outside the tents. People were very worried | about their health, about the risk of disease, about not | having enough food. We were very concerned about the | health of mothers and children, and pregnant women | were a major worry too. | Over the next month, our small team worked around. | the clock to set up clinics providing basic healthcare | and to supply hospitals that were struggling. Getting | medicines to this part of Yemen wasn't easy. Supplies | often had to cross frontlines. One of our trucks carrying | antibiotics, medicines and other supplies was hijacked. | It was an incredibly difficult environment to work in. | Along with general healthcare, we provided routine | vaccinations for children and offered antenatal and | postnatal care. We saw a lot of pregnant women and | children and were able to refer pregnant women | with complications to larger hospitals for emergency | caesareans. It made a real difference. | A DESPERATE SITUATION | The day we started working in a rural hospital near the | frontline, a woman came in with a breech delivery who | was having real difficulty. Our midwife assisted and | everything went well. But who knows what would have | happened to that woman if the hospital wasn't there. | Since I left, many more people have come to the area. | But Marib is no longer a safe place to be. In recent | weeks, the frontlines have moved into the province, | causing large numbers of injuries and forcing thousands | more people to flee their homes. As the frontline | approaches Marib city, we are concerned that people | sheltering in the area may find themselves with no | place else to go. | After six years of conflict, the situation is desperate. | These people need our help now more than ever.” | WHAT IS HAPPENING IN YEMEN? | Yemen is the midst of civil war. After six years of conflict, the | medical and humanitarian situation in Yemen continues to | deteriorate. Poverty is widespread, malnutrition is on the rise | and people are confronted by the daily threat of violence. | Pregnant women struggle to access medical care. | Infant and maternal mortality are on the rise as | mothers and children bear the brunt of an increasingly | brutal conflict. | MSF teams are providing urgent medical care to people | caught up in this crisis. We work in 12 hospitals and health | centres and support more than 20 hospitals and health | facilities across the country. | We provide medical support in emergency rooms, | maternity wards and outpatient departments, conduct | surgeries, and run mobile clinics in rural towns and | villages. The situation remains desperate. We need | your help now more than ever | THANK YOU | could pay for three safe delivery kits | to assist women giving birth. | could provide an oxygen kit to help care for | premature babies with underdeveloped lungs. | could cover the cost of a midwife working | in a field hospital for three days. | could pay for a portable ultrasound device | to monitor the health of pregnant women | and their foetuses. | DONATE NOW | CALL 0800 055 79 84 | Or search ‘MSF NURSE’ | to make an online donation | YES, | would like to support MSF's medical teams in Yemen | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontiéres UK C] | OR C] Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: | cv ee CETTE EEE | Cardnumber|_| | | | | | | | | | | TT I | J oe LTE | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% | | | more at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | date O/O0/OO | NB; Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | giftaid | Signature Today's ai | / | | | / | | | this declaration, so that we can update our records. | Title | | Forename(s) | | _ RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand accounts | Surname from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, from combatting | epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | Address | al We won’t allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing purposes | and we won't bombard you with appeals. | | Postcode : ‘ , ; ; A ghee wo | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations,and ~ | Telephone | occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change how you 3 | P hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling 020 7404 6600. S | Email Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage | provides first-hand accounts of our work. You will receive Frontline, occasional i 0 a 7 free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, | emergency appeals, requests for donations and event invitations. ptmeintoemail Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, Chippenham SN14 6NG. Altematively — | Charity Registration Number 1026588 you can phone 0800 055 79 84. MSFRO0048",Newspaper,NA,NA
169,"£9L000-Wv) | 1u¥z O8S | dOSYYOM | yg aSLuduaj}UuyZ poomM uojUeW | au}ua) UOLZN}OS e}eG FYL | Ply uelysl4yy | XSNN-AVAV-GHLY SN}d Ysodaeau4 | Help a community like Rose’s build | a life-saving dam. | pair of taps E communal water point | cement | We have 7 days to make a huge | stand with families like Rose's, and | millions more people across Kenya | whose lives are threatened daily | by storms, flash floods and drought. | Let's stand together against climate | chaos. Let's work with communities | to help build reliable water systems | - and better futures. | Every drop of water that falls is | precious. So there needs to be a | simple, sustainable and ingenious | way to successfully collect it. Earth | dams do just that. And your gift | today can help build them. | These huge basins are dug in the | ground to collect and store rain | water. It’s then piped into taps | for people like Rose to draw from. | You only have to look at Florence | and her community in the image | opposite to see the difference | an earth dam can make. | Crops grow, land can be farmed, | and families no longer go hungry. | People stand strong and are | better prepared for whatever | life throws at them. | tire | ieee ut lol we | Will you stand against | climate chaos bebe | seople in Kenya: | : 2 he a , <> | Sag, ~~"" — ef : x | | Kitui County in Eastern Kenya was already in | the grip of a climate emergency. Severe drought | followed by extreme and unpredictable changes | in weather has destroyed crops, killed livestock, | and continues to threaten livelihoods. | Then the pandemic hit. | We know ourselves that water | and washing hands has been | vital in helping to save lives | during the pandemic. But what | if there isn’t any? What if the | nearest water source is miles | away, by foot? What then? This | climate crisis and the pandemic | impacts us all. But people living in | poverty, like Rose and her family, | get hit the hardest. Today, we | can make a stand with people | in Kenya. | The recent | pandemic has | made a lack of | water more critical | for people like Rose. | You may never meet a more | determined grandmother than | Rose. At 68 years old she makes | a six-hour round trip every other | day to collect water for her family | so they can farm, drink and wash. | She’s hungry and weary but she | goes on. Because she has to. Her | grandchildren’s lives depend on it. | However, she won't have the strength | to do this journey forever. | '‘RParates | Even before the pandemic hit, | unreliable and unpredictable rainfall | made life a struggle. Today we can | stand against this chaos. Together | we can work with communities like | Rose's to make sure everyone has | easy access to reliable water sources - | now and in the future. | Here’s my gift of | | e10 | |ea2 | |e335 | Jother £ | We will use your donations for pre such as those featured and where we consider the need is greatest | Title First Name Surname | Addre: Pos | | Please make your cheque postal order CAF voucher™ | payable to: Christian Aid. (Please do not send cash by post) *delete as appropriate | debit my Mastercard Visa Maestro CAF Charity Card | Card no. (Piease copy the long number along the middle of your card Start date Expiry date | ssue no Today’s date | Mae gnature | giftaid a | Gift Aid your donation to make it worth 25% more, at no extra cost to you. | want to Gift Aid my donation and any donations | n the future or t | Christ | Christiar Please notify Christian Aid if you: | pay less *wantt ance! this ceciaratior | e address | amount of Gift Aid ¢ | tax year itism | We would love to tell you how your support is making a difference! | j are happy to hear from us by email or telephone, please provide those details below | We will keep you updated about our work and the dif : J: | lever to share your details with any other organisation for marketing purposes. For more information | please visit caid.org.uk/privacy | To save paper, if we have your email address we will send you a thank you by email. | I'd like to know more about leaving a gift in my Will to safeguard this vital work for the future. | Please fold and seal your completed form and send it t | Freepost Plus RTHB-AKAE-UUSX, Christian Aid, The Data Solution | Centre, Manton Wood Enterprise Park, WORKSOP S80 2RT. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | (FR) REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
170,"> = pera ae > | Sightsavers : Sightsavers | 4 7) we | Nalukena geteeW x j N | cae | | SJ@ADS]YBIS | nowwn | zacc- | a+ 3 3 0 | -Fvuv0vTS | UO ® et | anor a8 | 2 aun ® | oz < | on=t oo | Soo 4 | I< OW | Will you Sian . | help protect | alukena | children fro wy bs | | Just £5 from you) | could save her sight. | could save her sight. | www.sightsavers.org/closer | | www.sightsavers.org/ p's www.sightsavers.org/closer | Trachoma steals sight with every blink... | Trachoma is an infection that's both agonising, and blinding. | At first, it makes your eyes itchy and sore. But if left | untreated, it develops into the more severe trichiasis - | which steals your sight blink by painful blink... | Nalukena had suffered from trachoma since birth - and | at just two years old, it was clear she was in real pain. | Her devastated parents did all they could to help their | little girl, but they didn't understand what was wrong. | They just knew it was getting worse. | Without help, | sight altogether. | You can save children from a life of pain | That’s why your support today is so vital. Together, we | can reach a whole class of children like Nalukena with | sight-saving treatment - and one day eliminate this cruel | infection for good. | From painful trachoma... | £5 could protect a class of children | Thankfully, we could help Nalukena with an antibiotic called | Zithromax* - which costs just 15p per treatment, and has the | power to stop trachoma in its tracks. | Now, Nalukena no longer has to live in pain, and can look forward | to a happy future. But there are still millions of children across | Africa who are moving closer to blindness each day. It's vital | we can treat them, before they lose their sight forever. | Your gift will save children’s sight | Just £5 from you is all it takes to provide Zithromax” for | a class of 33 children - saving them from blindness, and | moving us closer to our goal of eliminating trachoma by 2025. | To make a donation, simply complete the form | opposite and return it in the attached envelope, | give online, or call O800 298 2200 today. | little Nalukena was at risk of losing her | ...to blinding trichiasis | Trachoma starts with a | bite from an infected fly. @ | Will you send £5 today and save a class of children from blinding trachoma? | The eyes start to itch and weep, @ <p The eyelids then turn inwards, causing 4 <p> This condition is trichiasis, | and become very sore in sunlight. the eyelashes to scrape the eye. which eventually steals sight. | 4& DETACH HERE & | & DETACH HERE & | Yes, | want to give £5 to stop trachoma and save the sight of children like Nalukena | Title First name Surname | Full home address | Postcode | Phone number | Email | Are you happy to receive updates and find out how you can help by email or telephone? | If so, please fill in your details above. | We want you to be really proud of the work you're helping make ; | happen and will be in touch from time to time with updates about ThroughGiftAid,any dit | how your support is changing lives. To do this, we'll use the details donation you give will gifte | you've provided but promise never to sell or share your data. be worth 25% more. | If you'd rather not hear from us, please let us know by emailing tam a UK taxpayer and | would like | info@sightsavers.org or calling 01444 446600. Sightsavers to reclaim the tax paid on all my | past, present and future. | understand | [ 7 P : | | would like to make a donation of el [TT J-TT) that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains | Tax in the current tax year than the amount | Please make cheque/postal order payable to Sightsavers tase poner of Gift Aid claimed on my donations, it is my | Or debit my: O MasterCard OVisa 0 CAF SEND CASH responsibility to pay any difference. | SC LILI ET LICE Lt (CJ I'd like Sightsavers to claim | Gift Aid on my donations. | eC LIC) be CLC | [Name on card | s! | [Signature | Date | Your donation will be used to support our work whereve