173,"Dad? | dementia | killing | _ Feelings of confusion, desperation and | isolation dont just affect people with | dementia, theyre symptoms the people | closest to them experience too. | Right now, the broken social care system | means that in the UK, nearly 1 million | people with dementia and their families | are Struggling to get the support and | care that they need. Until things change, | adementia diagnosis will continue to | claim more than one life. Make a stand | this Dementia Action Week, 17-23 May. | Because while dementia isn't curable | “yet, the care system is. | Sign the petition to reform social! care. | Search: Cure the Care System | Giheinert Dementia Action Week | Supported by «> Santander",Newspaper,NA,NA
