175,"oe ow | — ae ee 8 ee ee | tusel FREE | Ste ktm, FUTURE | Registered charity in England & Wales (1110522) and Scotland (SC044246). | $i HUNGER C¥recycle , | IT’S TIME TO COME TOGETHER | TO BUILD A BETTER FUTURE - A STRONGER, | MORE JUST SOCIETY, WHERE NO ONE GOES HUNGRY. | IT’S TIME TO COME TOGETHER TO | BUILD A HUNGER FREE FUTURE. | | Across the UK, more people than ever are facing extreme a | poverty, unable to afford the basics or put food on the table. | At the start of the pandemic, the need for emergency food parcels from | our food bank network rose by 47%, with 2,600 food parcels provided for | children every day. We can’t allow food banks to become part of the fabric | of our communities. It’s time for change. | | FRE | FUTURE | SPEAK UP FOR STOP FAMILIES SUPPORT YOUR | A BETTER FUTURE GOING HUNGRY COMMUNITY | | Together our voices Donations are vital in Volunteering, | are powerful. Join | our movement and | speak up for justice, | compassion, and | positive change. | Stand alongside people facing hunger and | take action now to end the need for food banks. | #HUNGERFREEFUTURE | The Trussell Trust | making sure the food | banks in our network | can provide emergency | parcels for people | who cannot afford | the basics. | Unit 9, Ashfield Trading Estate, Ashfield Road, Salisbury SP2 7HL | Registered charity in England & Wales (1110522) and Scotland ($C044246). | fundraising, getting ce | involved - you can a | make a real difference | in your area by | working with us to | build a better future. — | Registered with | (FR FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | ~~ YE S | WANT TO HELP CREATE A | wv HUNGER FREE FUTURE FOR EVERYONE | 1. MY GIFT FOR A HUNGER FREE FUTURE | I'd like to give: [ £25 [_ £50 [ £75 -OR- my choice of:| £ | [| | enclose a cheque/postal order or CAF voucher (payable to The Trussell Trust) - OR - | Please debit my: & Visa [ MasterCard [ Maestro | Card No. (Maestro only) Issue No. (Maestro only) | Start date: / Expiry date: / CVV: (3 digit security code) | Name on card: Date: | [ ] If you do not require an acknowledgement of your generous gift, please tick this box. Alt | As a supporter of the Trussell Trust, you’re as much a part of our community as our food banks are a part of theirs. By keeping | you informed about our campaigning, research, and fundraising work; our community, and our ability to fight poverty is | strengthened. Let us know below how you would like to be contacted in the future. | 2. MY DETAILS 3. BOOST MY GIFT | Stay up to date with our campaign for a hunger free future today: gifted wn | Please do contact me via: P Email [ Telephone [_] SMS ; | ; Boost your donation by 25p for | Please do NOT contact me via post|_| every £1 you donate. In order to | Gift Aid your donation you must | Mobite: tick the box below. | ; [J | want to Gift Aid my donation and any | Email: donations | make in the future or have made | in the past four years. | Add your details here so we can process your payment | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | and claim Gift Aid if you qualify. | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains | d aca fy: Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my | responsibility to pay any difference. | Title: Name: | Address: Signature: | Postcode: Date: | You're in control. If you’d like to change your choices at any time, all you have to do is call our Supporter Care Team on 01722 580 178 (calls | charged at standard rate, Monday to Friday, 9am to Spm) or email supportercare @trusselltrust.org. | The Trussell Trust will use the personal information that you provide in accordance with the Data Protection Act 2018. The Trussell Trust | is registered as a data controller with the UK Information Commissioner’s Office under registration number Z279027X. Your details will | be kept safe and secure, only used by us, or those who work for us, and will not be shared, sold or rented to third parties for marketing | purposes. We may use information and data you provide for analysis, research, or screening purposes in order to help us understand our | supporters so we can save resources and deliver the best possible service. If you would like to know more about your data protection | rights, or how we use and look after your data, please take a look at our Privacy Policy at trusselltrust.org/privacy. | PLEASE RETURN USING THE ENVELOPE PROVIDED, the HUNGER | VISIT TRUSSELLTRUST.ORG /HUNGERFREE trussell ae | OR CALL 01722 580 178 (Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm) trust | Thank you for your generosity. Your donation will be used wherever the need is the greatest. Stop UK Hunger FUTURE | DONATE £25 | HUNGER AND JOIN OUR | CAMPAIGN To £ | trussel EEE THE INJUSTICg | trust OF HUNG ER AND | Stop UK Hunger FUTURE POVERTY IN THE | UK FoR GOOD | ACROSS THE UK, MORE PEOPLE THAN EVER ARE FACING | EXTREME POVERTY, UNABLE TO PUT FOOD ON THE TABLE. | THIS ISN’T RIGHT. IT’S TIME TO COME TOGETHER TO BUILD | A HUNGER FREE FUTURE. | March 2021 | Dear Friend, | After 10 years of cuts and as we face the economic fall-out of the Covid-19 pandemic, more people than ever | are unable to afford the basics, forced to turn to charity to put food on the table. Every day, food banks across | the UK are meeting this unprecedented challenge with compassion and care, but we can’t allow food banks to | become part of the fabric of our communities. It’s time for change. | You can be part of building a hunger free future. Donate £25 and join our | movement for change. Together, we can end the need for food banks and | build a stronger society - one where no one goes hungry. | Even before Covid-19 hit, need for food banks was growing and had reached record levels. And at the start | of the pandemic, that need increased by a further 47%, with a shocking 2,600 food parcels given to children | every day. More people than ever are existing, not living. More people than ever can’t afford to put food on | the table. | “We’re the fifth richest country in the world, it’s just not good enough! There’s too many people that fall | through the cracks.” - Caroline | Alongside the food banks in our network, we’re continuing to do whatever it takes to make sure everyone can | access emergency support when they need it. But when one person goes hungry, our whole society is weaker. | No one should need to turn to charity because they can’t afford the basics. For Jeanette, who has faced | poverty throughout her life, a sudden change in circumstances meant her family was unable to put food on | the table. | “We were always on the cusp of not having enough for the basics. You’re only ever one problem | away from a real crisis. For us, an injury resulted in our main form of family income grinding to a | halt. Without a steady stream of income, we had to get food from a food bank. At the time, it was | mortifying. But it pretty much saved our lives.” | And now, the pandemic has meant “everything’s tipped upside down” once again. | “Because of underlying health problems that | have, I’ve been shielding since March and surviving on | £800 a month from Universal Credit. My rent is £520, so that shows you how much money there is. | “Even though I’ve got excellent qualifications, you know, life should be good and dandy, just one | little thing can throw you back down that path.” | Please turn over... | On average, people who need to use a food bank have just £50 a week left after housing costs to cover the | essentials like bills, transport, and food. | This isn’t right. The UK’s support system is meant to be there for any of us when we need it, but for Jeanette | and thousands more of us it isn’t working as it should. It’s time to build a better future. | Together, we can create a better future. Your £25 donation will help food | banks provide emergency food now, and support our campaign for a fairer, | more just future. | It’s time to come together to build a better future. The challenge is big, and we need your help. Join us now | and together, we can end the need for food banks. | Simon Maltz | Hunger Free Future Project Manager | PS. During the first six months of the pandemic, food banks in our network gave out a staggering 1.2 million | food parcels to people in crisis. We can’t let this happen again. Your gift of £25 can provide help now and | support the #HungerFreeFuture movement. | CAROLINE’S STORY | Caroline, who has needed to use a food bank in the past, is one of the thousands of people who’ve signed | up to help us build a hunger free future. | “I’ve had a lot to deal with in my life. I’ve had mental health issues from | my early twenties. | have a severely disabled child. | lost both my parents “| think there’s that feeling | quite young iy marrige fed ads made amass finan APO of fara, va way, where | » oe SSG are I’m thinking, why am | | “| just didn’t have enough money to live on. | always think when people having to go and get free | talk about food poverty — it’s poverty. It’s not food poverty. It’s the lack food? But I’m not ashamed | of money. | didn’t want to go to a food bank. | think most people don’t because it’s not my fault.” | expect somebody like me to need a food bank, but | did. I’m not ashamed | though because it’s not my fault. And it’s not of my making. | “My depression could happen to anyone. Having a disabled child could happen to anyone. You cannot | guarantee at any stage of life that something isn’t going to happen that stops you from being part of | mainstream society. We’re the fifth richest country in the world, it’s just not good enough! There’s too many | people that fall through the cracks.” | Caroline’s right. It’s time for us to stand together to build a stronger, more just society, | one where the right support exists to make sure no one goes hungry. | By donating £25 today, you can help create a better future. | The Trussell Trust | Unit 9, Ashfield Trading Estate, Ashfield Road, Salisbury SP2 7HL. Registered charity in England & Wales (1110522) and Scotland (SC044246). | Freepost Plus RIGG-AUTH-KUGH | The Trussell Trust | 9 Ashfield Road Trading Estate | Salisbury | SP2 7HL | the FIUNGER | hee! FREE | Stop Kiger FUTURE | THANK YOU FOR HELPING BUILD | A BHUNGER FREE FUTURE",Newspaper,NA,NA
177,"MSF anaesthetist Lenka Cerver | )hi As-Sufal hospital in Yemer | ALISON CRIADO-PEREZ | IS AN MSF NURSE WHO | WORKED IN MARIB | The conffict in Yemen is now in its sixth year. In Marib | in central Yemen, néarly thrée million people have been | displaced from their homes and are living in makeshift | camps close to the frontline. Pregnant women and | children are in desperate need of medical care. | “When we arrived in Marib, we found the local hospitals | overwhelmed by the sheer number of people and by an | influx of war-wounded. Around 2.7 million people are | in the province now, many of them displaced from their | homes elsewhere and looking for a safe haven. | People were living in makeshift shelters made of plastic | and metal sheets. There were no latrines, just pits dug in | the ground outside the tents. People were very worried | about their health, about the risk of disease, about not | having enough food. We were very concerned about the | health of mothers and children, and pregnant women | were a major worry too. | Over the next month, our small team worked around | the clock to set up clinics providing basic healthcare | and to supply hospitals that were struggling. Getting | medicines to this part of Yemen wasn't easy. Supplies | often had to cross frontlines. One of our trucks carrying | antibiotics, medicines and other supplies was hijacked. | It was an incredibly difficult environment to work in. | Along with general healthcare, we provided routine | vaccinations for children and offered antenatal and | postnatal care. We saw a lot of pregnant women and | children and were able to refer pregnant women | with complications to larger hospitals for emergency | caesareans. It made a real difference. | A DESPERATE SITUATION | The day we started working in a rural hospital near the | frontline, a woman came in with a breech delivery who | was having real difficulty. Our midwife assisted and | everything went well. But who knows what would have | happened to that woman if the hospital wasn't there. | Since I left, many more people have come to the area. | But Marib is no longer a safe place to be. In recent | weeks, the frontlines have moved into the province, | causing large numbers of injuries and forcing thousands | more people to flee their homes. As the frontline | approaches Marib city, we are concerned that people | sheltering in the area may find themselves with no | place else to go. , | After six years of conflict, the situation is desperate. | These people need our help now more than ever.” | WHAT IS HAPPENING IN YEMEN? | Yemen is in the midst of civil war. After six years of conflict, | the medical and humanitarian situation in Yemen continues to | deteriorate. Poverty is widespread, malnutrition is on the rise | and people are confronted by the daily threat of violence. | Pregnant women struggle to access medical care. | Infant and maternal mortality are on the rise as | mothers and children bear the brunt of an increasingly | brutal conflict. | MSF teams are providing urgent medical care to people | caught up in this crisis. We work in 12 hospitals and health | centres and support more than 20 hospitals and health | facilities across the country. | We provide medical support in emergency rooms, | maternity wards and outpatient departments, conduct | surgeries, and run mobile clinics in rural towns and | villages. The situation remains desperate. We need | your help now more than ever. | THANK YOU | could pay for three safe delivery kits | to assist women giving birth. | could provide an oxygen kit to help care for | premature babies with underdeveloped lungs. | could cover the cost of a midwife working | in a field hospital for three days. | £866 could pay for a portable ultrasound device | to monitor the health of pregnant women | and their foetuses. | CALL 0800 055 79 84 | Or search ‘MSF NURSE’ | to make an online donation | YES, | would like to support MSF's medical teams in Yemen | | WOULD LIKE TO MAKE A DONATION OF £ | | Please make your cheque/charity voucher payable to Médecins Sans Frontiéres UK c | OR C] Please charge my VISA/Mastercard/Amex/CAF card: | CardholdernameL_| {| [ [| | | | {tt tt ttt tt tt ttt | | Cardnumber|_{ | | | | | | | | tt tt td | | ARE YOU A UK TAXPAYER? | If so, you can make your gift worth 25% | | | more at no extra cost. Please tick the box below. | | wish Médecins Sans Frontiéres (MSF) to treat all gifts in the last 4 years, this gift | and all future gifts as Gift Aid donations. | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed | on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | pate O/OO/O0 | NB: Please let us know if your name, address or tax status changes, or if you would like to cancel | giftaid it | Signature Today's date | | | Vd rey i P eS this declaration, so that we can update our records. | Title | | Forename(s) | | RESPECTING YOU AND YOUR PERSONAL DATA | Your support is vital to our work and we would like to keep you informed with first-hand accounts | Surname | from our staff and patients about the lifesaving impact your support is having, from combatting | epidemics to providing emergency surgery. | Address | We won't allow other organisations to have access to your personal data for marketing purposes | and we won't bombard you with appeals. | | Postcode ine Di itati 8 | By supporting MSF, you will receive our quarterly magazine Dispatches, event invitations,and i) | Telephone | occasional emergency appeals with requests for donations by post. You can change how you 3 | P hear from MSF UK by emailing uk.fundraising@london.msf.org or calling 020 7404 6600. a | Email | Visit our privacy notice for more: msf.org.uk/privacy. | HEAR FROM MSF BY EMAIL. Sign up to our monthly email, Frontline, which Please fill in this form, place in an envelope and return postage | provides first-hand accounts of our work. You will receive Frontline, occasional [] Ont ahi 1 free to: FREEPOST RUBA-GYZY-YXST, Médecins Sans Frontiéres, | emergency appeals, requests for donations and event invitations. pt me in to emai Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, Chippenham SN14 6NG. Alternatively ‘sess | Charity Registration Number 1026588 | you can phone 0800 055 79 84.",Newspaper,NA,NA
178,"YEMEN ON | THE BRINK | OF FAMINE | GIVE £143 NOW TO HELP DISPLACED | FAMILIES BUY THE FOOD AND ESSENTIALS | THAT CAN SAVE THEIR LIVES. | After more than six years of war, Yemen is | now heading towards the worst famine the | world has seen for decades. | Malnutrition rates are at record highs. | Thousands of children under-5 are severely | malnourished. They are children with distended | bellies, emaciated limbs and blank stares — | they are starving to death. | But it’s not too late. If you act now, you can | help save lives. UK for UNHCR urgently needs | your support to give the most vulnerable | families lifesaving Emergency Payments, | so they can buy basic food like rice, flour and | cooking oil and essentials like medicine | and water. | With a gift of £143 today, you could provide . | an Emergency Payment and help save lives. | The £143 payment is based on the cost of a feed their children.” | ‘Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of food | and household essentials, and has proved | the most effective way of helping families | get enough food to sustain themselves. | For a family on the edge of starvation, | it means survival. | Even before the coronavirus pandemic hit, | Yemen was the world’s worst humanitarian | crisis, with 80% of the population dependent | on aid for their day-to-day survival. | The intensifying conflict, along with a | fuel embargo, has seen the economy | collapse with the prices of food and other | commodities skyrocketing. | People who have lost their homes in the | conflict are the most vulnerable — they are | up to four times more likely to face hunger. | And 79% of those displaced are women and | children. Many parents are going without | food so their children can eat, others have no | income at all. Jean-Nicolas Beuze, UNHCR’s | representative in Yemen, says: “Yemenis can’t | afford to worry about coronavirus. They are | too worried about not having any food to | This is happening right now. UNHCR teams on | the ground are doing everything in their power | to help displaced people survive. But with | their work critically underfunded, they can’t | save lives without you. Please give £143 or | whatever you can afford today. | © UNHCR/Marie-Joélle Jean-Charles | Four-year-old Umaimah, whose family was displaced | 19 months ago. Her father collects tin cans to sell, | which barely brings in enough to pay for food. | £143 could provide | an Emergency Payment | to help a displaced | family of six to buy | food and essentials. | Give now at unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in the form below | | would like to give: | £143 ] Other £ | [_] | enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | (_] | would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. Expiry date _ | 5 se A ads | | Signature c | Date | LJ Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title | ___ First name Last hana: 2-2 eee | Addresss iene ae ies es | ae Te ee Postcode 2 | Email ete. “hy 2. tt eS, | Phone | Please tell us if-you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: C] By email Sst By phone | Registered with ‘ | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | giftaid it | Ci would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand | that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my | donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax | and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities.and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | () UNHCR | The UN Refugee Agency | United Kingdom for UNHCR | P21YEOBA2 | Scan this | QR code to | donate online",Newspaper,NA,NA
