197,"(Ee Ga 2 is | , EMERGENCY APPEAL FOR’ | THE PEOPLE OF | PALESTINE | Following 11 days of heavy shelling and airstrikes on Gaza, the | Palestinian health service is under impossible strain. Before Israel's | military offensive, 50% of essential medicines were already in | dangerously short supply. Now, hospitals are overwhelmed with the | huge numbers of casualties - many need ri: treatments for crush | injuries, burns and limb wounds. | Medical Aid for Palestinians (MAP) is on the ground continuing to respond | to the huge number of casualties. Our teams in Gaza and the West Bank are | working directly with local healthcare partners to ensure that Palestinians get | the medical aid they need during this critical time. | Right now, our immediate priority is getting vital medicines and equipment | into the hands of medical teams as quickly as possible. We have released | emergency funding to provide the items desperately needed by hospitals | . ae 1, 4 | _ Bent : | ""* ° | ‘ After nearly two weeks | of bombing in occupied | Palestine, the health service | is in a state of emergency — | and many lives are at risk. | ¢ In Gaza, more than 230 Palestinians | have been killed, including at least | 65 children, and over 1,760 injured. | ¢ Hospitals are struggling to cope | with the heavy influx of casualties | amid a pandemic. | ¢ Hospitals, clinics and COVID testing | centres across Gaza have been | damaged by bombing. | e Essential medicines are at critically | low levels. | and emergency services in both Gaza and East Jerusalem. | MAP has been working for the health and dignity of Palestinians living under | occupation and as refugees for over 30 years. In times of crisis, we are ready | to respond quickly with aid and assistance, but your support is vital. Thank you. | A donation from you today could help provide: | ¢ Hygiene kits containing soap, bandages and antiseptics for | people who have been forced to flee from their bombed homes. | ¢ Emergency supplies such as antibiotics, anaesthetics, dressings and | fluids to stabilise and operate safely on those with severe injuries. | ¢ Specialist lifesaving treatments, such as those used for a child | with severe crush injuries or burns. | The people of Palestine urgently need your help. Please donate now and | save lives. Call 020 7226 4114 or go to WWW.MAP.ORG.UK/OBSERVER | Here is my urgent gift of: £25 [)£50 [)£100 OR my own choice of £ | (_]'ll send a cheque/postal order made payable to Medical Aid for Palestinians OR | LJ Please charge my Visa / MasterCard / Amex / CAF card (delete as applicable) | Card no| {=o} es fe a eee ote | Valid from u Expiry Date / | Signature(s) Date / / | We'd like to keep you informed about how your support is helping Palestinians. To hear from | us, please provide your details below: | Name: | Address: | Postcode: | (_] Yes, you can contact me by email. Email: | (J Yes, you can contact me by telephone. Telephone number: | We will keep you updated by post with information about your donation. If you do not want us to write to | you about our work, please tick this box: (1) No, please don’t contact me by post. You are always in control | of how you hear from us and you can change your mind at any time by calling us on 020 7226 4114. | We'll always protect your privacy and will never sell or swap your data with any third party. To find out | more about how we safeguard your data, visit: map.org.uk | MEDICAL AID FOR PALESTINIANS | Boost your donation by 25p for be peat | every £1 you donate with Gift Aid giftaid ad | Ol am a UK taxpayer and would like to Gift Aid this donation and any donations | | have made in the past four years, or | make in the future, to Medical Aid for Palestinians. | | understand that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax each tax year (6 April to | 5 April), than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all of my donations, it is my responsibility | to pay any difference. | Date: / / | D Sorry, | am not a UK taxpayer, and therefore cannot take part in Gift Aid. | Please notify the charity if you: want to cancel this declaration, change your | name or home address, or no longer pay sufficient tax on your income and/or capital | gains. If you pay Income Tax at the higher or additional rate and want to receive the | additional tax relief due to you, you must include all your Gift Aid donations on your | Self-Assessment tax return or ask HM Revenue and Customs to adjust your tax code. | We promise to use your donation to | support the medical and health needs | of the Palestinian people, wherever the | need is the greatest. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Please complete and return | this form in an envelope to: | Freepost MAP | (no stamp is required). | You can also donate online: | www.map.org.uk/observer | Scan this QR | code, donate | online and | support the | people of Gaza | in seconds. | 2105EAP | SLESPOL JeQUINN Auey> pasaysibay",Newspaper,NA,NA
198,"— ee One | Saving our planet — | begins with you opening this envelope. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Friends of | the Earth | | Qrrecycle | ee Become partof | something bigg | Friends of the Earth Limited; Company number 1012357. | Registered in England and Wales. | Our registered office is: lst Floor, The Printworks, 139 Clapham Road, SW9 OHP. | To view our Privacy Policy please visit: | friendsoftheearth.uk/about-us/privacy-policy. | Our paper is totally recycled and our printers hold 1S014001 | which means they care about the environment. May 2021. | If we stand together today, we can make Friends of | the government act tosavethisplanet. -  ~ the Earth © | Dear friend. | Thank you for opening this letter. The fact you’ve done so proves we have something in common - we | both want to save our planet. Today, I’m hoping you'll join me and thousands of others to do just that. | The undeniable impact of climate change can be seen all around us - extreme flooding, heatwaves and | storms. It’s getting worse all the time. Climate change has become a climate crisis. | And while people like you and | watch in frustration and horror, the government is failing to do what's | needed to protect our planet and those of us who call it home. | We're running out of time to prevent the worst impacts of this climate crisis. | But it can be done. And it will be done by people like us. | By working together, we can be a movement with the passion, expertise and sheer numbers to show | the government they have no choice but to act. | Will you pl r part, and help protect n r planet oming a Frien f the Earth | member for £5 a month? | The government has made many positive statements | about leading the world in tackling the climate crisis. But | behind closed doors they’re still making harmful decisions. | Recently they have given the green light to more oil and | gas wells in the North Sea. They’ve also cancelled the | Green Homes Grant - an important solution to help people | improve energy efficiency in their homes, like better | insulation or double glazing. We’re members | That’s why we must each take action right now, to demand “I donate to Friends of the | they change h th they’re | in wn. If w that Earth because they hold | we'll each be able to look back in 5 or 10 years and say with the government to | pride that we were on the right side of history. account over the | It’s easy to feel powerless as an individual, but nothing could climate crisis. | be further from the truth. Jan, Friends of the | Earth Member | By becoming a Friends of the Earth member today you | Please turn over... | can join a growing network of people around the globe, | determined to stand up and make those who have the | power to protect people and planet, act. | What makes us different is that we’re not simply | demanding change, we’re actively working to make | change h nand holding the government to ac | We're campaigners, lawyers, and climate experts. We’re | members, volunteers and local activists too. And the work | we do is making a real difference. | Recent successes include helping to get a planned | opencast coal mine in Northumberland stopped, and | launching a legal challenge against the government’s | investment in a huge gas plant in Mozambique. | Our members give us the strength and funding to | challenge the government on cases like these on the | streets, in courtrooms and in the corridors of power. | If you become a member too, you'll make our movement | stronger until we’re simply impossible to ignore. | You could look back in 5 or 10 years and say you were on | the right side of history, you took action for the planet. | Will you become a member today? | Thank you. | “DAWES Femaudo | Denis Fernando | Friends of the Earth Campaigner | PS Stand with us today and you can look back | 5 or 10 years and say you took action for the | planet, you were on the right side of history. | Please become a member for £5 a month now, | or anything you can afford. io io | Use the form enclosed, visit “ | foe.uk/climate-member-21, | or scan the QR code. [=] Pa | Friends of the Earth Limited; Company number 1012357. Registered in England and Wales. | Our registered office is: lst Floor, The Printworks, 139 Clapham Road, SW9 OHP. | To view our Privacy Policy please visit: friendsoftheearth.uk/about-us/privacy-policy. | May 2021. | Our paper is totally recycled and our printers hold 1SO14001 | which means they care about the environment. | C¥recycle | We’re campaigners | “I support community groups | across the UK to secure | ambitious Climate | Action Plans | from their | local leaders.” | Catriona Currie, | Friends of the Earth | Campaigner | We’re lawyers | “I’m fighting for climate justice | on high-profile cases like | Heathrow airport expansion, | and supporting | communities | in challenging | fossil fuel | developments | in the UK.” | Katie de Kauwe, Friends | of the Earth Lawyer | We’re experts | “We find the evidence | and solutions to show the | government what can be | done to stop the | impacts of the | climate crisis.” | Mike Childs, Friends | of the Earth Head of | Science, Policy and | Research | Here’s what we can achieve Friends of | the Earth | when we stand together. 3 | 1971 | Glass | < bottle | recycling | action | 11976 | Protecting 7% ys aki . 2 Recycling | endangered Vf /-#4_. = bins reach | species ’ gon Oe, front doors | We helped draft a across the UK | the Endangered Species We helped write the | Act 1976 to protect 5,800 legislation that put that | species of animals across recycling bin on your — ; | the globe. doorstep. Huge wins like this | are only possible with the | support of people like you. | In our founding year we | , returned thousands of | used glass bottles outside | the Schweppes HQ to | promote reuse. | SERS REE EHH EERE EEE EERE EE EEE TEE EEE ETHOS ESOS EHEEEEEEH ESE SEEEEEEHEE EEE HERES EEEEEEEEHE SESH EEEOEEEEEHEEEHESEEEEEEEEEEEE ETE HEHEHE DEEE® | ‘. | 200