G.UK/DONATE YOUR SUPPORT MAKES OUR WORK POSSIBLE PLEASE HELP US SAVE LIVES AND DONATE AT MSF.ORG.UK/DONATE | Bentiu | Protection | = = 9 eee ee | ‘| The hospital is run by more than | 500 MSF staff, most of whom | a are residents of the camp. | of Civili | ivilians | | camp | Bentiu Protection of Civilians camp | in South Sudan is home to some | 100,000 people who have sought | refuge from conflict. Residents live in | temporary shelters made of corrugated | metal, plant stalks, mud and plastic | sheeting. These offer limited protection | from the elements, especially during | the rainy season when walkways | become lanes of mud. People's medical | needs are enormous. | MSF operates the main hospital in the | UN-run camp, which provides general | medical care, surgery, treatment for malaria, | malnutrition and diseases | water and | FB | \ EA WB | linked to poor | for tuberculosis and HIV. | “MSF is operating one of the only hospitals | thar has surgical services — not only in Bentiu, | but in the wider region,” says MSF surgeon | John Buckles, who has recurned to Bentiu | five times to conduct surgeries. “Working | here, you're faced with a broad spectrum | of conditions, ranging from tropical diseases | to surgical conditions that occur in any | society where there are abdominal issues, | igh to cy | along with | ie: har: ig | pleased that you've been able to help, | while also knowing that, ifitwasn't | All of | these conditions have continued during | the COVID-19 pandemic.” | Bustration Jere Raceey | YOUR SUPPORT MAKES OUR WORK POSSIBLE PLEASE HELP US SAVE LIVES AND DONATE AT MSF.ORG.UK/DONATE | | the medical care and lifesaving | Each ward of the 120-bed Surgery that they need. | hospital is housed in a white “A Wi money | tent connected by covered q Water tanks i ea sont 8 lene | walkways. “I was working sa | 12 to 15 hours a day for seven < | weeks, doing an average of “LE | | eight surgeries every day, — 7 oad | along with a range of local Er gh Bentiu and 