228,"=) WaterAid UN tal | Pir | hanes ee Loa Wb | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST | WaterAid For > we | York House 77p on clean water, decent | Wetherby Road toilets and good hygiene | Long Marston 23p on fundraising* | YORK For very £1 we spend on ft ndraising, | YO26 7NH vacate Arie Rapa | It's a big ask | It's a big ask | Here goes. | We need your help to bring clean water to | everyone, everywhere within a generation. | I'm about to ask you to get behind something that will | change the world, forever. That may sound daunting but | I need you to carry on reading, because together we really | can bring clean water to everyone. | Gulp. I'll start at the beginning. | It starts with a child like Ibrahim, in Sierra Leone. The water | you see him collecting is filthy and makes him dangerously ill. | But he has no choice, it's the only water there is and every sip | could kill him. Just like it kills over 800 children every day. This | has to change. | But, here’s the good news. We've already worked in Ibrahim's | village, helping to bring the community clean water that can | save lives. But that’s not enough. We need to bring water | to many, many more children around the world. Just £2 a | month from you today could help make that happen. | Together we can help every child - until | we've helped them all. | It doesn’t stop there. There are 785 million people like Ibrahim in the world who still do not | have clean water. Reaching them all might seem impossible, but we have to think big. Because | if more people - like you - give £2 a month then, child by child, village by village, we know it’s | possible to get clean water, decent toilets and good hygiene to everyone in our lifetime. | If everyone, everywhere has clean | water, children like Ibrahim won't | risk their lives drinking filthy | deadly water. Please start giving | a small gift of £2 a month today. | How can I be so sure? Because I know how powerful we can be as a team - together. | We work with local experts and communities to install reliable, long-lasting pipes, pumps and | taps. In fact, we reach almost 1,000 people with clean water every single day. We do everything | we can to ensure governments around the world deliver on their clean water promises too. | So what do you say? | Just imagine that day, when a child like Ibrahim tastes clean water for the | first time. When his mother doesn’t have to worry that the next sip could kill | him. Then imagine the moment we reach every child, everywhere. | Let's bring clean water to the world within a generation. Please fill in the | donation form to start giving £2 a month today, every penny counts. | Thank you. | Johnty Gray, WaterAid UK. | Since we visited Ibrahim, WaterAid has delivered clean water to his community. However, millions of children | still face the terrible circumstances and choices highlighted above. | WaterAid | Call 0300 123 4341"" | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Visit wateraid.org/uk/gulp | **As of 2019/20 WaterAid Annual Report | Registered charity numbers 288701 (England and Wales) | and SC039479 (Scotland). | MOISTEN HERE | Yes, let’s bring clean water to the world, | starting with a child like Ibrahim. WaterAid | £10 a month could save | aha a big In just 1 | £5 a month could save | children’s lives. | | £2 a month could save | children’s lives. In just | 1OMN< | Here's my life-changing giftof: £2 £5 £10 Surprise us!£ a month fornernoxce | Startingonthe 1st 15th 25th Month Year peedalche eld | Title: First name: Last name: | Home address: | Postcode: | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid without your full name and address. | You can hear how you change lives. We hope you will fill out your contact details below | to hear more about children like Ibrahim, fundraising, and opportunities to get involved. If you | are happy to hear from us by phone and email, please let us know your details: | Tel no. (home/mobile): Email: | Many people love to receive postal updates. Tick if you'd prefer not to _ | * WaterAid and WaterAid Trading will use your personal details to communicate with you in the ways you have agreed to, and as | explained in our Privacy Policy. | + We may use the information you share with us and background information about you that we obtain from publicly available sources | to carry out analysis (sometimes using suppliers) to tailor our communications to be more appropriate and relevant to your interests. | * You can withdraw your consent at any time. For full details, including information about your privacy rights, see our Privacy Policy at | www.wateraid.org/privacy | To change your preferences, or request to stop receiving communications please contact us on | 020 7793 4594 or at supportercare@wateraid.org 211AE/01N | WaterAid Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by direct debit. | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST, WaterAid, York House, York YO26 7NH. (00 NOT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) Beet. | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society Service user number | 406789 | Reference (to be completed by WaterAid) | To the Manager: Bank/building society | Branch address: | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please pay WaterAid | Direct Debits from the account detailed in this erelethipen. to | the Gra etd assured by the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand | ede Instruction may remain with WaterAid and, if so, details will | be passed electronically to my bank/building society. | Postcode: | Name(s) of account holder(s): | Signature(s) | Bank/building society account number Branch sort code x | Date | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account. | JY¥JH N3LSIOW",Newspaper,NA,NA
