237,"Create a kinder | future for | people living | with dementia | Will you consider leaving a gift in your Will to | Alzheimer’s Society? | Your gift will help fund research into a cure. And until | we get there, you'll help tackle the injustices in the | system to ensure people living with dementia are | not forgotten. | For too long, the UK’s unjust and underfunded social | care system has let people living with dementia | down, failing to recognise their needs, or the impact | their condition has on those who love them. | Thanks to income from gifts in Wills, we were able | to react quickly during the pandemic, stepping | in to provide invaluable support for people | struggling to cope with isolation, anxiety and | fear under lockdown. | A gift in your Will can ensure people affected by | sy wwe | L] Please send me my free guide to leaving a gift in my Will | Izheimer’s | Socie | / \ United | Against | ~ Dementia | dementia always have somebody to turn to. | For over 30 years, investing in research has been | central to Alzheimer’s Society’s mission. We now | Know so much more about the potential of fields like | genetics and immunology. The only thing holding us | back from pushing forwards is lack of funding. | Your legacy can be the investment in research that | speeds up the search for a cure. | Agift in your Will, of even just 1% of your estate, could | help achieve the step-change we desperately need. | Because if we in the dementia community don’t look | out for each other, who will? | You can help us improve dementia care and | support at the same time as we develop new | treatments — ensuring people living with dementia | are not forgotten. | Request your free guide to leaving a gift in your Will today. | Visit alzheimers.org.uk/notforgotten, | call 0370 011 0290 or fill out and return the form below. | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode | Email Phone | We’d love to send you updates on our life-changing services and research, | as well as our fundraising, campaigning and volunteering activities. | Please tick below to let us Know you're happy for us to stay in touch. | CF Byemail 0 Byphone OC Please don’t contact me via post | Post in your own envelope to: Freepost NOT FORGOTTEN | You do not need a stamp or any other address details. | Please follow Government isolation and distancing guidelines if posting. | Registered charity no. 296645. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, | Wales and Northern Ireland. | We will never sell your details to any third parties. | Please see alzheimers.org.uk/privacy for more | information. If you’d like to change what you receive | from us at any time, please call our friendly | team on 0330 333 0804. | Registered with | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | LGPRAQ421M Posed by models",Newspaper,NA,NA
238,"A gift in your Will helps the dogs | and cats who deserve it most | For over 160 years, Battersea has been here | for every dog and cat, taking them in without | question and caring for them without judgement | until we find them the homes where they truly | belong. One in three of these animals is cared for | thanks to gifts in Wills. | By remembering Battersea.in your Will, you help | ensure that we can continue to be here for every | dog and cat who needs us. Gifts in Wills are | vital to all areas of our work, So any gift you give, | whatever size, will make a big difference to the | animals in our care. oc | A gift in your Will costs you nothing today but | will help ensure that Battersea can continue to | support the animals who need us tomorrow. | Together, we will be here for every dog and cat. | i BATTERSEA | Battersea Dogs & Cats Home is acharity | _ fegistered in England and Wales (206394). s | To find out more about ere. : | leaving a gift in your Will ipsa iak ak | to Battersea, please call 020 7627 9300, email | pbeeialeyCPatlgr*s: org.uk or return this form | Title | | Name | Address | Postcode | The data you've provided will be used by Battersea Dogs & | Cats Home to send you a gifts in Wills information pack. | For more information about how we use your data, visit | battersea.org.uk/privacy ; | "" Return form to the Special Gifts Team: | z Freepost RTLJ- -ETCZ-SCCZ, Battersea Dogs & Cats Home, | gt Battersea Park Roe, London SW8 aBR: § | : pacitnend int | (FR) EUNDRAISING: | “REGULATOR =",Newspaper,NA,NA
239,"British Heart | Foundation | BHF-funded researcher | Dr Joseph Boyle is | studying how to protect | blood vessels from | damage that could lead | to a heart attack. | Gifts left to the British Heart Foundation to fund £100m of life saving research into | (BHF) have helped researchers to restart these conditions every year. We simply can’t | hearts, fix arteries in newborn babies, prove do that without gifts in Wills, because they | statins could protect millions, and give people make over half of all our research possible — | hearts they weren't born with. so you can be sure that, if you leave a gift, | You have the power to help make more we'll make every pound count. | breakthroughs possible — by remembering A gift in your Will could beat | the BHF in your Will. | Heart and circulatory diseases still kill one in | four of us in the UK. That’s why we’re aiming We call it Will Power. | heartbreak forever. | Find out more: search online | for ‘BHF Gifts in Wills’ Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | © British Heart Foundation 202] registered charity in England and Wales (225971 and Scotland (SC039426) 21LA01",Newspaper,NA,NA
