252,"Questions about smear tests? | We're here for you. | Coronavirus has changed a lot of things. | If you've been invited for cervical screening (a | smear test), you may have questions or | concerns about how your appointment will | work now. | Whether it's questions about going for a test, | or you want to talk about your results, we | offer free, confidential information and | support. | No question is too big or too small.",Newspaper,NA,NA
253,"DogsTrust | Make sure your dog is cared for with | a Canine Care Card from Dogs Trust | You’ve always done what you can to protect your four- | legged friend, and that shouldn’t change when life does. | With a Canine Care Card, you won’t have to worry about | what’s next for them, because Dogs Trust will look after | and rehome them at one of our 20 rehoming centres across the UK. | Apply online now to get your FREE Canine Care Card at: dogstrust.org.uk/ccc | 020 7837 0006 | DogsTrust | Please call | Email: ccc@dogstrust.org.uk Call us directly: O20 7837 0006 | Please quote “334776”, or complete the coupon below: | |_| Please send me a Dogs Trust Canine Care Card application form | (Please fill out in block capitals) | Title First Name | Surname | Address | Postcode 334776 | From time to time we would like to send you exciting updates about our work, products, services and how you can support | us, including fundraising activities and research by post. If you’d rather not receive these mailings, please tick here [_] | In order to communicate with you more effectively, better understand your preferences and ability to support our work, we | may analyse your data. We do share your information within the Dogs Trust Group; currently Dogs Trust Worldwide, Dogs Trust | Ireland and Dogs Trust Promotions. To read our full privacy policy visit dogstrust.org.uk/privacy. | Please send this coupon to: Freepost RTJE-SXGL-BEEJ, Dogs Trust, Moulton House, 10 Pond Wood Close, Northampton, | NN3 6DF (No stamp required.) N.B. Service only available for residents of the UK, Ireland, Channel Islands & Isle of Man. | DogsTrust | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | A dog is for life® | dogstrust.org.uk | © Dogs Trust 2021 | Registered charity numbers: 227523 & SC037843 | DGend | ~ - a | TL BA SS Se TR",Newspaper,NA,NA
254,"Leaving a gift in your Will can be life-changing. | Get your free RNIB Will Guide today and see how you | can help someone with sight loss build new skills, | confidence and greater independence — to create | their best possible future. | Yes, send me a free Will Guide today: | § Call 0303 123 9999 | (Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm) | Go online to rnib.org.uk/willguide | © RNIB registered charity in England and Wales | (226227), Scotland (SCO039316), Isle of Man (1226). Re N i B | Also operating in Northern Ireland. | Registered with s : | FUNDRAISING : | rR) REGULATOR 3 See differently",Newspaper,NA,NA
255,"Ethiopia-Tigray Emergency Appeal | GIVE SHELTER | £159 could provide a shelter kit — giving safety to families | fleeing the dreadful conflict. | Violence in Ethiopia’s Tigray region has seen more than two million people forced to flee their homes since the conflict started in | November 2020. Over 63,000 have fled into neighbouring Sudan, while those displaced inside Ethiopia include around 100,000 | refugees from Eritrea. | The region remains a tinderbox. There have been reports | of hundreds of people killed, of atrocities, including forced | military recruitment of men and boys, and of widespread | sexual violence against women. | Displaced families urgently need shelter. People have been | sleeping in the open air, with no access to water or food. | UNHCR teams on the ground are doing all they can to protect | people, but with funds running desperately low, they urgently | need your support. | £159 could pay for a shelter kit. As the diagram shows, each | kit contains bamboo poles, a bamboo floor mat, roof beams, | and other local building materials with which a family shelter | can be built. With the rainy season fast approaching, the shelter | you help provide could be lifesaving. And it will do more than | protect families from the elements; it will allow people to socially | distance to protect themselves from COVID-19, and give women | and girls a safe haven. | Without shelter, they are intensely vulnerable. UNHCR’s Country | Representative, Ann Encontre, said: “/ am deeply concerned by | WOODEN GABLE FRAME SHELTER | e The kit you can help provide builds a shelter like | this, using locally available materials. | e Each kit contains a roof beam, wall beams, bamboo | poles and sticks, rope, a bamboo mat for flooring | and straw mesh to line the walls. | Example shelter kit from Sudan. Content and structure vary depending on | location and materials available. | the widespread allegations of sexual violence against women and girls. The level of cruelty being reported defies belief.” | RIGHT NOW, SHELTER WILL SAVE PEOPLE’S LIVES. | Families have been forced to flee the terrifying violence and sought safety in other parts of Ethiopia’s Tigray region or in Sudan. | And every day a family spends without shelter, is a day when they are more at risk of contracting COVID-19, and a day when | women and girls remain more vulnerable to sexual violence. Please give £159, or whatever you can afford, today — there is not a | moment to lose. | £159 COULD PROVIDE A SHELTER KIT | Give now at UNrefugees.org.uk/tigraycrisis | Call 0800 029 3883. or fill in and return the form below | I would like to give: [_| £79 [_| £159 [_| £318 [_] others | Cit enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | [| would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | a a 2 a | Date | Card no. | Pe ae ear | Signature | Expiry date | Perarielc] | C Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: oO By email O By phone | Registered with | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Your gift will help families displaced by the Ethiopia Emergency, | funding shelter and other interventions, depending on greatest need. | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | gifvaid “we | [11 would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and I understand | that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my | donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax | and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | Scan this ‘() U Be El] Cc R | =-~> The UN Refugee Agency | QR code to United Kingdom for UNHCR | donate online | P21ETOBA2",Newspaper,NA,NA
256,"Or Druha examines two-month-old | Muhammad Jamal, admitted tothe | paediatric ward of Ad-Dahi rural hospital | after suffering diarrhoea and vomiting. | tographé | MEDECINS SANS FRONTIERES | ORS WITHOUT BORDERS | 2/e@ | YEMEN EMERGENCY APPEA | “After six years of conflict, the situation is desperate. Yemeni women | and children need our help now more than ever.’ | ALISON CRIADO-PEREZ | MSF NURSE | The conflict in Yemen is now | in its sixth year. In Marib, in | '_ central Yemen, nearly three | million people have been | displaced from their homes | - and are living in makeshift | camps close to the frontline. Pregnant women and | children are in desperate need of medical care. | “When we arrived in Marib, we found the local | hospitals overwhelmed by the sheer number of | people and by an influx of war-wounded. Nearly | 3 million people are in the province now, many | of them displaced from elsewhere. | People were living in makeshift shelters made | of plastic and metal sheets. There were no latrines, | just pits dug in the ground. People were worried | about their health, about the risk of disease, | about not having enough food. We were very | concerned about the health of mothers and children, | and pregnant women were also a major worry. | Over the next month, our small team worked | around the clock to set up clinics providing basic | healthcare and to supply hospitals that were | struggling. Getting medicines to this part of | ‘Pregnant women and | children are in desperate | need of medical care’ | Yemen wasn’t easy: Supplies often had to cross | frontlines. One of our trucks carrying antibiotics, | medicines and other supplies was hijacked. It was | an incredibly difficult environment to work in. | Along with general healthcare, we provided | routine vaccinations for children and offered | antenatal and postnatal care. We saw a lot of | pregnant women and children and were able | to refer pregnant women with complications | to larger hospitals for emergency caesareans. | It made a real difference. | The day we started working in a rural hospital | near the frontline, a woman came in with a | breech delivery who was having real difficulty. | Our midwife assisted and everything went well. | But who. knows what would have happened if | the hospital wasn’t there. | AN URGENT SITUATION | Since I left, many.more people have come to the | area. But Marib is no longer a safe place to be. In | recent weeks, the frontlines have moved into the | province, causing large numbers of injuries and | forcing thousands more people to flee their homes. | After six years of conflict, the situation is | desperate. These people need our help now | more than ever. | Thank you.” | DONATE TO SUPPORT OUR MEDICAL TEAMS | £44 COULD PAY FOR THREE SAFE DELIVERY | KITS TO ASSIST WOMEN GIVING BIRTH | CALLO8000557985 . Qi430 | SEARCH MSF CRISIS | _ ORSCANTO DONATE",Newspaper,NA,NA
257,"British Heart | Foundation | BHF-funded researcher | Dr Joseph Boyle is | studying how to protect | blood vessels from | damage that could lead | to a heart attack. | a ol | Gifts left to the British Heart Foundation to fund £100m of life saving research into | (BHF) have helped researchers to restart these conditions every year. We simply can’t | hearts, fix arteries in newborn babies, prove do that without gifts in Wills, because they | statins could protect millions, and give people make over half of all our research possible | hearts they weren’t born with. — so you can be sure that, if you leave a gift, | You have the power to help make more we'll make every pound count. | breakthroughs possible — by remembering A gift in your Will could beat ee | the BHF i Will. | 3 pacar heartbreak forever. | Heart and circulatory diseases still kill one in | four of us in the UK. That’s why we’re aiming We call it Will Power. ’ | Find out more: search online | for ‘BHF Gifts in Wills’ FR Resistered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | © British Heart Foundation 2021 registered charity in England and Wales (225971 and Scotland (SC039426) 2I1LAQ1",Newspaper,NA,NA
258,"ll you show your | support for people | affected by dementia? | Registered charity no. 296645. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, Wales and Northern Ireland. FMNOU04 | Thank you so much if you already Forget Me Not Appeal | support Alzheimer’s Society, and please | feel free to pass on this letter to a friend. C | Alzheime recycle | Give today and you'll — | receive a limited | edition Forget Me | Not pin badge. | Who will you wear | yours for? | Your Forget Me Not | stickers are inside | ks o ae | 3 3 ee | : SNe Me scenes | PH 1 xg e | eal ee : | $ NG, ee | gS 3 on F | x Cl. | ay Rosco | _g Dementia | DMC2 1051AN | Fo r g eT , Please affix | postage | stamp here to | help reduce | our costs. | Freepost Plus RUAT-CJJT-TEJB | Forget Me Not Appeal | Alzheimer's Society | Bumpers Way | Bumpers Farm | Chippenham | SN14 6NG | From: | From: | You can wear the | Forget Me Not | stickers (below) | or stick one to | your donation ' | form to symbolise — | your support. | Registered charity no. 296645. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, | Wales and Northern Ireland. | our gift will mean compassion, empathy | and support when people need it most. | Please give what you can to the Forget Me Not Appeal | £20 could pay for over an hour’s support | from a Dementia Adviser. _ | In that hour they could help people cope with | their condition on a day-to-day basis, understand | the benefits they’re entitled to, or look after their | mental health if they’re still isolating at home. | £40 means 250 people can access talking: | Point, our online community. | a | With Talking Point a trouble shared can become Si | a trouble halved — people can learn from each | other’s experiences, share their frustrations and | their knowledge of local services. | £105 supports a Dementia Adviser for | one day. | Dementia Advisers are dementia experts. They | provide information, offer guidance and directly | support people affected by dementia, day in, and | day out. | Please turn over to make your gift, and to tell us more about who you | will be thinking of for the Forget Me Not Appeal. Thank you so much. | Will you choose to change the future of dementia? | You’re doing something incredible to help thousands | of families affected by dementia. We'd love to | keep in touch with you about our amazing services | LJ Yes, I’d like to receive updates by email, | contact me at: | and research, and how you can get involved with LI Yes, rd be happy to speak to someone on the | fundraising, campaigning, or volunteering. It’s totally phone, contact me on: | up to you — you can update what you get at any time | and we'll never sell your details to third parties. L_] Yes, I'd like to receive updates via SMS, | Our work can’t continue without people like you, so contact me on: | please choose to stay in touch using these boxes | and help us beat dementia. If you’d like to change | what you receive from us at any time, please call | LJ Please do NOT contact me with updates | through the post | | Customer Care on 0330 333 0804. | | | Dear friend, | Your gift to the Forget Me Not Appeal will help change the lives of people | affected by dementia. Your kindness will mean more people living with | dementia and their carers get the practical and emotional support they Alz eimer | desperately need. Thank you. ocie | Kate Lee, Chief Executive Officer “ ~) | Eeeuse i Again | ce a: Dementia | ; Yes, I'll join the Forget Me Not Appeal to | / Attachyour ‘\ . | | ForgetMeNot } SUpport people affected by dementia. | sticker here | Don’t forget to ave us your cle tails $0 We can Send | — rok your Forget Me Not Pun badge. ) | i My details: Please complete all fields to make a valid Gift Aid claim. | Titlee___——C-~First Name Surname | Address | Postcode | 2 | will give: L] £20 tohelp pay for urgently needed support services ALZH0230 | LJ OR my choice of £ | L_] enclose a cheque/postal order made payable to Alzheimer’s Society OR | Please debit my Llvisa LlMastercard LICAF Card with the amount specified. | Card Start Expiry | no. date - date = | Signature Today’s | date ~ Z | All donations will go to where they are needed most: to support services, research and campaigning on behalf of people with dementia. | Pll be wearing my pin badge in tribute to | Please use this space to tell us why you want to support people affected by dementia. | Sharing real stories is a powerful way to demonstrate the value of supporting people affected by dementia. | By filling in this box you are consenting to us potentially using your story in future updates or appeals. | Olam happy for all gifts of money that | have made to Alzheimer’s Society in the | past four years, and all future gifts of money that | make, to be Gift Aid donations. | lam aUK taxpayer and understand that if | pay less Income Tax & Capital Gains Tax in the current | tax year than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all of my donations across all charities, it is my | responsibility to pay any difference. Alzheimer’s Society reclaims 25p for every £1 you donate from the | tax you pay for the current tax year. If you change your name, address or tax status, do let us know. | Please turn every £10 you donate into £12.50 at no extra cost to you . . it | i) | fea d | Please return this form in the Freepost envelope provided or post it to: | Freepost Plus RUAT—CJJT-—TEJB, Forget Me Not Appeal, Alzheimer’s Hover your | Society, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, Chippenham SN14 6NG hone camera | You can also donate online at alzheimers.org.uk/forgetmenotappeal over thes anne Oe ia i | | Registered charity no. 296645. A company limited by guarantee and registered in England no. 2115499. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, Wales and Northern Ireland. FMNDFO4 | | Forget | me not | Appeal | Dementia | Alzheimer’s Society | This summer, will you Show your —siairrced’ | Plymouth | love for somebody affected by = 2x0 | T 0330 333 0804 | dementia and support our ean | Forget Me Not Appeal? alzheimers.org.uk | alzheimers.org.uk | Dear friend, | This last year hasn’t been an easy time for any of us, and if you or someone you know is affected | by dementia, you'll understand just how isolating lockdowns and social distancing have been. | But we've got through it by pulling together, by acting as a community even when we've been | physically apart. | Alzheimer’s Society has been supporting people living with | dementia and their loved ones for over 40 years. And since | March 2020 our vital services; providing advice, guidance | and emotional support to people affected by dementia, | have been needed like never before. People have been | through so much and told us they’ve been feeling | forgotten, and that they want an opportunity to remember | and pay tribute to their loved ones. That’s why we have | launched our new Forget Me Not Appeal and why I’m | asking you to be part of it. It would be wonderful if you | could give a gift, to help fund vital support services for | people affected by dementia. | Please, will you give £20 to our Forget Me Not Appeal in | honour of someone you know affected by dementia? | To give now, you can fillin and return the enclosed form, visit alzheimers.org.uk/forgetmenotappeal | or call 0330 333 0804. | If you do give, we’ll send you a Forget Me Not pin badge. Do you know who you will wear it for? |’! be | wearing my badge and supporting the appeal for my mum, who has late-stage dementia and is | currently in a care home. She doesn’t know me now, but | Know she doesn’t love me any less. | As you can imagine, the visiting restrictions this past year have been really tough. | can only | hope Mum found comfort as Dad and me waved and shouted that we loved her through | her window. | | hope you'll join me and support the appeal in solidarity with | somebody you know who's affected by dementia, and all the | challenges they face. Even though dementia is so common | across the UK, it’s widely misunderstood and people still face | alot of stigma. So if we all support the appeal and wear a | Please turn over... | FMNLETO3 | badge it will be a way of raising our voices — of telling the UK | that people living with dementia matter. | But the Forget Me Not Appeal is about more than raising | awareness — it’s about raising funds to give people living with | dementia, and their carers, the practical support they need | right now. | That’s why I hope you’ll give £20 so Alzheimer’s Society | can be here for someone like Christine, who cares for her | husband Roy. | Perhaps Christine’s experiences resonate with your own? | ‘The man | love had changed and life seemed upside-down. | | didn’t know how to approach it. He would forget words. Now he can’t communicate with me, and | | have carers to help shower him. They talk about lockdown, but I’ve been in permanent lockdown | since Roy became ill as we're so isolated. Friends don’t come any more as they don’t know what to | say. The man | love is disappearing.’ | If someone you know is affected by dementia, you'll probably recognise the sense of isolation that | Christine mentions. Even in the best of times, isolation has a massive impact on the mental and | physical health of people living with dementia — and this last 15 or 16 months it’s been so much | harder. That’s why the Forget Me Not Appeal is so important — it will fund services like our | Dementia Advisers and Companion Calls, to make sure nobody has to face dementia alone. | For Christine, the Companion Calls service was a lifeline. I’m so grateful that the past kindness | of people like you made it possible to be there for her: | ‘My Companion Caller Mel rings every week and never misses — we have such a laugh. I’m so | involved with Roy’s dementia every day — but Mel makes me feel human again. | | don’t think there’s any way to overstate how vital that is — to help someone feel like a person, a | wife, husband, daughter, friend — and not just a carer. So when you send in your gift and then wear | your Forget Me Not badge this summer, | hope you'll think not just of someone who's special to | you, but also of all the people like Christine, who can feel a bit more human thanks to your support. | Thank you so much for getting behind our Forget Me Not Appeal. | Kate Lee | Alzheimer’s Society CEO | Tos hope you'll Support the Forget Me Not Appeal to help | provicle much-neeclecl emotional anck practical Support to people | aSSe ctecl by clementia. And also hope you'll wear your baclge When | you receive tt, in honour of someone Speccal to you: thank you So mach. | Alzheimer’s Society respects the confidentiality of everyone who uses our services and keeps that | information strictly private. Should this letter reach you at a difficult time, please accept our apologies. | lf you or your family have been affected by dementia we would like to Support you in every way we Can; | please contact our Dementia Connect support line on 0333 150 3456 or visit our website at | alzheimers.org.uk You can also find out about services available near you at | alzheimers.org.uk/dementiaconnect | Alzheimer’s Society is a registered charity in England and Wales (296645) and the Isle of Man (1128). A company limited by guarantee, | registered in England and Wales (2115499) and the Isle of Man (5730F). Registered office: 43-44 Crutched Friars, London EC3N 2AE.",Newspaper,NA,NA
259,"No one should feel held back in life. That's why a gift in your Will to RNIB is so powerful. | Large or small, it can help people whose possibilities often feel limited to learn new skills, | gain greater confidence and feel more independent every day. | Get your free RNIB Will Guide today and discover how your amazing gift could create a | fairer future for us all. | Get your free Will Guide to find out more: | Call 0303 123 9999 +e Ni i 3 | (Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm) | Go online to rnib.org.uk/willguide | Or, fill in and return this form to | Freepost SKILLS FOR LIFE See differently | We are committed to protecting your privacy and want to assure you that your personal | information is safe with us. For more information, please see www.rnib.org.uk/privacy | 1} FMR CTO ATO TENORS | ie etme cence | STONMONN IRIN |e tS ak a i | Yes, please send me a free Will Guide LAMAA2161R:02 | Title First Name Last Name | Address | Postcode | © RNIB registered charity in England and Wales (226227), Scotland (FR) FUNDRAISING | (SC039316), Isle of Man (1226). Also operating in Northern Ireland. REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
260,"So ——S< | =— s SSS SIS | = — —— | Se SSS SaaS SSS | 2s Soe, | ""Aeme il | MOJU} isnl },UOp | @SP9Id “@pisul | 49}}9] TORTTOUUH | U L ae - . | SSS os eee ><—S SS | XX) N | ""i ) | wi Hi | W +, | SSOADPOHUSII | Return address: British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM SN14 6NG | The power | of kindne | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | (, Call: 0300 0230827 LJ Visit: redcross.org.uk/newfund | [] Text FUND to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text FUND NO to give £10 without consenting to | calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). | For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). | Please affix | postage stamp | | vie BritishRedCross ion | oe Bh | Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ | ROOM Q2SI21 | British Red Cross | Bumpers Way | Bumpers Farm | CHIPPENHAM | SN14 6NG | | MTT lw eo ea La TT | UK Office | 44 Moorfields | BritishRedCross SARL | 0300 456 11 55 | redcross.org.uk | The British Red Cross Society, | incorporated by Royal Charter | 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), | People are in danger. of Man (0752) and Josey (490) | But we have a plan. | This is the response of our lifetime. | Dear reader, | I’m sure you’ll agree that the recent news coverage from around the world has been bleak. My teams and | are | deeply concerned by what we’re hearing from our colleagues across the global Red Cross movement, too. | Today | wanted to tell you about the new international fund we’ve launched, dedicated to supporting | people overseas, and ask if you can help. | Every year since 1999, extreme poverty levels globally have fallen — but that changed last year. The World Bank | estimates that somewhere between 119-124 million people fell into extreme poverty last year. | That’s 20 years of progress, of communities lifting themselves out of poverty, damaged by the pandemic. It’s clear to | us that we need to act, now. | We've set up a new international fund specifically to reach people whose lives have changed for the worse. Their | reality is a stark contrast to ours here in the UK — because despite the pain of last year, our nation’s vaccine rollout is | going well, and things are opening up. | However, that’s not the case for millions of people worldwide. It’s far from it. That’s why we’re asking if you can | support our new fund with a donation today. | Take the communities we work with in Cox’s Bazar in Bangladesh, for example, who rely on busy trading to earn | money and provide for their families. Worryingly, there’s been more than a 60% drop in income for people there, | due to factors out of their control (travel restrictions, supply chain disruptions, and limited buyers in the market, to | name a few). | For them, there is no plan B. Their livelihoods have been crushed by Covid-19 — causing a spike in food insecurity | (which could turn into a food crisis, if nothing changes). | continued overleaf | Please pledge whatever you can. | | would like to make a donation of: | Gift Aid allows us to claim back ‘ . d iw | [ ] £5 [] £10 [ | £25 [ | £50  Mychoice 2 25p of tax for every £1 you give, J (7UM | making your donation go further | [ ] | enclose a cheque or postal order, made payable to ‘British Red Cross’ OR am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross | to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, | [ ] Please debit my Credit / Debit or CAF Card with the amount specified as well as any future donations, until | notify them | otherwise. Please tick to confirm [_] | | understand that if | pay less income / capital gains tax | caso! | | | JEP TT ILLT TILE | Suerte Stee a te pele | ; responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to ow | as [TL] 4 [ [| let us know of any changes to your tax status including 3 | ate changes to your name or address or if you need to Ps | Title (please tick): MrL_] mrsL_] missL_] msL_] other[ , ili ca - | Name Surname Keeping in touch | hdchoss We're so grateful for your support, thank you. As part | of the Red Cross, we write to you to tell you about Q | Postcode how your gifts help transform lives and how you can # | donate and help in other ways, as well as to update = | Telephone* you about our news and services. If you would rather | 8 | Email"" we didn’t communicate with you in this way, you = | can change the way we contact you at any time by BY | “Please only give us your teleohone number/email address if you are happy for us to visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch, e-mailing @ | contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and how you can mailenquiries@redcross.org.uk writing to FREEPOST = | donate and help in other ways. RED CROSS or calling Freephone 0800 2 800 491. : | We’re seeing a similar dangerous pattern across the world. So that’s why we created this fund - to reach | individuals, families and communities who urgently need help, wherever they are. | Our resilience project in Rakhine, Myanmar, has been running since 2017, and | think it’s another example worth | sharing with you. People face crises on top of crises - climate change and ongoing conflict has led to more frequent | cyclones and floods, household providers losing livelihoods, displacement, and limited access to healthcare. | As |’m sure you'd expect, adding Covid-19 to that list has hugely intensified the situation. People who were | vulnerable before the pandemic are now in an even more fragile position, and our help has never been more critical. | Communities like those in Rakhine need support that’s tailored to these intense, complex needs — that takes into | account every dimension of each crisis they’re facing. | The Red Cross is the organisation that can give that support. But we need your help to deliver it. | We were made for times like these. For context, in 191 countries, you’ll see a Red Cross — a team of dedicated staff | and volunteers, who work alongside vulnerable communities and know exactly what they need. | That’s why our programmes really do work. We’re already part of the communities we help. | To take you back to Cox’s Bazar — before the pandemic, we’d been working with some particularly vulnerable | groups there, to help them become more financially resilient. And in the wake of coronavirus, our reports show that | those groups’ income had dropped less than others who hadn’t had that vital training. Ultimately, they were | more prepared for the worst. | With your help, we can continue to make a real impact and strengthen our programmes around the world, to reach | people whose lives depend on it. | These are people who have no safety net, nothing to fall back on, no savings to see them through. People who may | care for children or elderly relatives, who have no idea how they’ll get through the week, who need a lifeline more | than ever right now. | So please donate to our international fund if you can. | | Know you might not have expected my letter to (quite literally) fall into your lap today. | know how easy it is to feel | small when the problem is so big. | know you might be thinking: “there’s no way | can make a difference.” | But, if you're still reading this letter, | also know that’s simply not true. | The only way we can tackle this is by coming together, taking action, and doing all we can to show that we are not | willing to leave anyone behind, no matter where they are. | It’ll be the response of our lifetime. But it’s what we do, and | hope you’ll be a part of it. | Thank you for reading, | Jams U4 | Inmaculada Lopez De La Cova Pena | Director of Programmes and Partnerships, British Red Cross | The power | of kindness | P.S. | recognise that my letter may have landed at a hard time for you. If you need help from a friendly Red Crosser, | call our support line on 0808 196 3651. It’s open every day between 10am and 6pm. | ie BritishRedCross | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | \, Call: 0300 0230827 [J Visit: redcross.org.uk/newfund | 0 Text FUND to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text FUND NO to give £10 without consenting | to calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message | (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross will use your donation to support our work overseas, wherever the | need is greatest. | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). | Registered with | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Your Privacy | The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and | will use personal data for the purpose it was collected | or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for | example, to provide goods, services or information you | have requested or to administer donations or services | we provide. We may also analyse data we collect | to better understand the people who support us or | those who use or deliver our services. Sometimes this | means us combining that data with information from | reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor | communications and services in a more focused and | cost effective way, as well as better meeting your needs | and the needs of others like you. However, we will never | do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and | will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with | previously expressed privacy preferences. For full details | about how we use personal data, our legal basis for | doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy | notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy",Newspaper,NA,NA
