265,"BritishRedCross | FHumanity | triumphs | when good people | do something | Around the world, Covid-19 has | had a catastrophic impact on | lives and livelihoods. The World | Bank estimates that the pandemic | pushed a further 119-124 million | people into extreme poverty | last year — putting two decades | of progress into reverse. | Millions of people in the areas | worst affected were already reeling | from the effects of climate change | and ongoing conflict, and are now | in an even more fragile position. The | scale of the challenge is immense. | But it is not insurmountable. | The Red Cross Movement | was created for times like these. | With dedicated teams of staff and | volunteers on the ground in almost | every country, we know how to | get help to people in a crisis. | Our new _ International Relief | Fund has been set up in response | to this urgent unfolding disaster. | Vital projects are already | underway in Myanmar, Nepal, | Bangladesh, Sierra Leone, Nigeria, | Namibia, Kenya and Sudan. | From helping people to grow | sustainable livelihoods, to providing | communities with life-saving | health awareness sessions and | first aid training, we focus on | building resilience for the future. | Every donation to the British Red | Cross empowers us to reach people | wherever the need is greatest — to | help communities lift themselves | out of hardship and restore hope | where it has been all but destroyed. | Please help us today. Your support | has never been more critical. | The power | of kindness | Guardian readers, | we need you | Families and communities across | the world are in danger. We can ee | help. But we must act now. Minare'in Cox | Bangladesh. ve bi | supporting her and othe; | refugees in the region ¥ | SSOID POY YSHUG/UUD PY © 0}0Ud | Please give to our International Relief Fund today, if you can. | 0300 023 0825 or visit redcross.org.uk/humanity | Text APPEAL to 70141 to make a £10 donation. | By texting, you consent to future teleohone and SMS marketing contact from British Red Cross. | Text APPEAL NO to 70141 to give £10 without consenting to calls and texts.” | Please send to: 2021 Summer Appeal Press, Ref: 176337, Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSu, 176337 | British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | | would like to make a donation of £207] £4002] £60() £100[] Othere[_| | (_]| enclose a cheque, made payable to British Red Cross OR (_] Please debit my Visa/Mastercard/CAF Charity card with the amount specified | card number || | | JL] | LILLE T ILLES Expiry date [| ]/{] ] | Title Forename Surname | Address | Postcode | Phone number** **Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are | Email** happy for us to contact you in this way with updates about how your | gifts are helping and how you can donate and help in other ways. | Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. | Ol am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, as well as any future donations, until | | notify them otherwise. Please tick. | understand that if | pay less income/capital gains tax than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations in the tax ‘ ad it | year in which they are received, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to let us know of any changes to your tax status, including i) ( | changes to your name or address, or if you need to cancel this agreement. | Keeping in touch Your support makes a life-changing difference to people in crisis. We write to our supporters to update you about the work of the British Red Cross, and how you can | help and donate in other ways. You can change the way we contact you at any time by visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch or calling Freephone 0800 2800 491. | Privacy statement The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and will use personal data for the purpose it was collected or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for example, to provide goods, | services or information you have requested or to administer donations or services we provide. We may also analyse data we collect to better understand the people who support us or those who use or deliver our | services. Sometimes this means us combining that data with information from reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor communications and services in a more focused and cost-effective way, as | well as better meeting your needs and the needs of others like you. However, we will never do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with previously | expressed privacy preferences. For full details about how we use personal data, our legal basis for doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy. | The British Red Cross will use your donation to support our work overseas, wherever the need is greatest. For more information visit redcross.org.uk | “Texts cost £10 +1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile. Registered with | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), FUNDRAISING | Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). BRC21-087 REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
