270,"Ethiopia-Tigray Emergency Appeal | GIVE SHELTER | £159 could provide a shelter kit — giving safety to families | fleeing the dreadful conflict. | Violence in Ethiopia’s Tigray region has seen more than two million people forced to flee their homes since the conflict started in | November 2020. Over 63,000 have fled into neighbouring Sudan, while those displaced inside Ethiopia include around 100,000 | refugees from Eritrea. | The region remains.a tinderbox. There have been reports WOODEN GABLE FRAME SHELTER | of hundreds of people killed, of atrocities, including forced | military recruitment of men and boys, and of widespread | sexual violence against women. | Displaced families urgently need shelter. People have been | sleeping in the open air, with no access to water or food. | UNHCR teams on the ground are doing all they can to protect | people, but with funds running desperately low, they urgently | need your support. | £159 could pay for a shelter kit. As the diagram shows, each | kit contains bamboo poles, a bamboo floor mat, roof beams, | and other local building materials with which a family shelter | can be built. With the rainy season fast approaching, the shelter | you help provide could be lifesaving. And it will do more than ietachanad codealia~a: + Ok bhein ial’, beams, baniboo | protect families from the elements; it will allow people to socially poles and sticks, rope, a bamboo mat for flooring | distance to protect themselves from COVID-19, and give women and ‘straw mesh to Tine the walls. | and girls a safe haven. | Example shelter kit from Sudan. Content and structure vary depending on | | Without shelter, they are intensely vulnerable. UNHCR’s Country location and materials available. | Representative, Ann Encontre, said: “/ am deeply concerned by | the widespread allegations of sexual violence against women and girls. The level of cruelty being reported defies belief.” | RIGHT NOW, SHELTER WILL SAVE PEOPLE’S LIVES. | Families have been forced to flee the terrifying violence and sought safety in other parts of Ethiopia’s Tigray region or in Sudan. | And every day a family spends without shelter, is a day when they are more at risk of contracting COVID-19, and a day when | women and girls remain more vulnerable to sexual violence. Please give £159, or whatever you can afford, today — there is not a | - moment to lose. | £159 COULD PROVIDE A SHELTER KIT | Give now at UNrefugees.org.uk/tigraycrisis | Call 0so0o 029 3883. or fill in and return the form below | e The kit you can help provide builds a shelter like | this, using locally available materials. | | would like to give: ny £79 [| £159 L | £318 [| Other £ Please return this form along with your cheque to: | LJ] 1 enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR. Freepost UK FOR UNHCR Romccn theet a tani) | L] 1 would like to make a donation by debit/credit card Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate iftaid it | Card no. Expiry date [11 would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p og | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | | | | | | | El | | | | | | | | | | | / | | yéars to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand | that if! pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my | Signature Date donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax | / / and VAT do not qualify. | , If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Subdorter Care Team | L] Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Title First name Last name | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | Address donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | Postcode 5 Re Fe | : = unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | Email ‘time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | Phone ¢ | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: CL) By email LC) By phone V4 (A); ‘U Ai ea Cc ie | , Scan this | Registered with Your gift will help families displaced by the Ethiopia Emergency, QR code to i aia The UN Refugee Agency | FUNDRAISING __ funding shelter and other interventions, depending on greatest need. : United Kingdom for UNHCR | REGULATOR donate online | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). P21ETOBA2",Newspaper,NA,NA
271,"The power | _ of kindness | Observer readers, | we need you | Families and communities across | the world are in danger. We can | help. But we must act now. | SSOID POY YSIHE/IUEYE) PY © O}OUd | supporting her} nd o | refugees in the region | Please give to our International Relief Fund today, if you can. | - Please send to: 2021 Summer Appeal Press, Ref: 176338, Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ, 176338 | British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | | would like to make a donation of £20[] £40(] £60L] £100(] Othere|  _—i| | [_]! enclose a cheque, made payable to British Red Cross OR [_] Please debit my Visa/Mastercard/CAF Charity card with the amount specified | Card number ; Expiry date / | ‘Title Forename | Surname | Address . | Postcode | Phone number™ **Please only give us your telephone namber/emairaddress if you are | Email** happy for us to contact you in this way with updates about how your | gifts are helping and how you can donate and help in other ways. | Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. | Ol am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, as well as any future donations, until | | notify them otherwise. Please tick. | understand that if | pay less income/capital gains tax than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations in the tax ‘ aid ut | year in which they are received, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to let us know of any changes to your tax status, including | changes to your name or address, or if you need to cancel this agreement. | Keeping in touch Your support makes a life-changing difference to people in crisis. We write to our supporters to update you about the work of the British Red Cross, and how you can | help and donate in other ways. You can change the way we contact you at any time by: visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch or calling Freephone 0800 2800 491. | Privacy statement The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and will use personal data for the purpose it was collected or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for example, to provide goods, | services or information you have requested or to administer donations or services we provide. We may also analyse data we collect to better understand the people who support us or those who use or deliver our | services. Sometimes this means us combining that data with information from reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor communications and services in a more focused and cost-effective way, as | well as better meeting your needs and the needs of others like you. However, we will never do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with previously | expressed privacy preferences. For full details about how we use personal data, our legal basis for doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy. | The British Red Cross will use your donation to support our work overseas, wherever the need is greatest. For more information visit redcross.org.uk | “Texts cost £10 +1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile. | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), FU N B R AlS| N G | Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). BRC21-087 REGULATOR | Registered with | ae British RedCross | | - Humanity | triumphs | ~ when good people | do something | Around the world, Covid-19 has | had a_ catastrophic impact on | lives and livelihoods. The World | Bank estimates that the pandemic | pushed. a further 119-124 million | people into extreme poverty last | year — putting two decades of | progress into reverse. | Millions of people in the areas | worst affected were already reeling | - from the effects of climate change | and ongoing conflict, and are now | in an even more fragile position. The | scale of the challenge is immense. | But it is not insurmountable. | The Red Cross Movement | was Created for times like these. | With dedicated teams of staff and | volunteers on the ground in almost | every country, we know how to | get help to people in a crisis. | | Our new International Relief | Fund has been set up in response | to this urgent unfolding disaster. | Vital projects. are already | ~ underway in. Myanmar, Nepal, | Bangladesh, Sierra Leone, Nigeria, | Namibia; Kenya and. Sudan. | From helping people to grow | sustainable livelinoods, to providing | communities with life-saving | health awareness sessions and | first aid training, we focus on | building resilience for the future. | Every donation to the British Red | Cross empowers us to reach people | wherever the need is greatest — to | help communities lift themselves | out of hardship and restore hope | where it has been all but destroyed. | Please help us today. Your support | has never been more critical.",Newspaper,NA,NA
272,"—e —— >< s = ne =, — = 2 | SoS == Ss LSS Ss So | ""‘ACPMeC iI == = | MOY} ySNf },uop | OSPd9/d ""OPIsul | 491390) THeTTOauT | ue S.oJ0UL | i RNAAXY) | MN Wy | SSeS 2S Ss | SS SSeS SSeS = SSeS | Og A ag 2 SS en | The power | of kindness | To donate: | Call 0800 023 0827 | Visit redcross.org.uk/newfund | Text FUND to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact from British Red Cross. | Text FUND NO to 70141 to give £10 without consenting to calls & texts | Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Q recycle | Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). When you have finished | with this please gece it | Return address: British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM SN14 6NG | The aouee | of k | SSIPEADIO SELASSIE MEE LY | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | ( Call: 0300 0230827. LI Visit: redcross.org.uk/newfund | i Text FUND to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text FUND NO to give £10 without consenting to | Calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message (we receive 100%). | For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). | Please affix | postage stamp | | of BritishRedCross rosine ou | en enn | Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ | ROOM Q2SI21 | British Red Cross | Bumpers Way | Bumpers Farm | CHIPPENHAM | SN14 6NG } | MTT lw oe ean La | | UK Office | 44 Moorfields | BritishRedCross London | 0300 456 11 55 | redcross.org.uk | The British Red Cross Society, | incorporated by Royal Charter | 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), | People are in danger. of Man (0752) and Jersey (420) | But we have a plan. | L/L) | This is the response of our lifetime. | Dear reader, | I'm sure you'll agree that the recent news coverage from around the world has been bleak. My teams and | are | deeply concerned by what we’re hearing from our colleagues across the global Red Cross movement, too. | Today | wanted to tell you about the new international fund we’ve launched, dedicated to supporting | people overseas, and ask if you can help. | Every year since 1999, extreme poverty levels globally have fallen — but that changed last year. The World Bank | estimates that somewhere between 119-124 million people fell into extreme poverty last year. | That’s 20 years of progress, of communities lifting themselves out of poverty, damaged by the pandemic. It’s clear to | us that we need to act, now. | We've set up a new international fund specifically to reach people whose lives have changed for the worse. Their | reality is a stark contrast to ours here in the UK — because despite the pain of last year, our nation’s vaccine rollout is | going well, and things are opening up. | However, that’s not the case for millions of people worldwide. It’s far from it. That’s why we’re asking if you can | support our new fund with a donation today. | Take the communities we work with in Cox’s Bazar in Bangladesh, for example, who rely on busy trading to earn | money and provide for their families. Worryingly, there’s been more than a 60% drop in income for people there, | due to factors out of their control (travel restrictions, supply chain disruptions, and limited buyers in the market, to | name a few). | For them, there is no plan B. Their livelinoods have been crushed by Covid-19 — causing a spike in food insecurity | (which could turn into a food crisis, if nothing changes). | continued overleaf | Please pledge whatever you can. | 1 would like to make a donation of: | Gift Aid allows us to claim back ‘ . d tt | [ Jes [ ]e1 [ |e25 [ |#50 Mychoice |£ 25p of tax for every £1 you give, @! QU | making your donation go further | | am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross | to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, | [__] Please debit my Credit / Debit or CAF Card with the amount specified as well as any future donations, until | notify them | otherwise. Please tick to confirm [_] | | understand that if | pay less income / capital gains tax | than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations | Card No. : : : 5 Ney | in the tax year in which they are received, it is my | : responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to | Expiry / let us know of any changes to your tax status including | [ | | enclose a cheque or postal order, made payable to ‘British Red Cross’ OR | Date changes to your name or address or if you need to x | cancel this agreement. i) | Title (please tick): = Mr [_] Mrs [_] Miss a Ms [| Other | ii 9 = | Name Surname Keeping in touch | We're so grateful for your support, thank you. As part | Address | of the Red Cross, we write to you to tell you about | Postcode how your gifts help transform lives and how you can | donate and help in other ways, as well as to update | Telephone* you about our news and services. If you would rather | Email* we didn’t communicate with you in this way, you | can change the way we contact you at any time by | “Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are happy for us to visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch, e-mailing | contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and how youcan —s mailenquiries@redcross.org.uk writing to FREEPOST | donate and help in other ways. RED CROSS or calling Freephone 0800 2 800 491. \ | 6S1921/66S8d/1800S/-ZISZO | We’re seeing a similar dangerous pattern across the world. So that’s why we created this fund —- to reach | individuals, families and communities who urgently need help, wherever they are. | Our resilience project in Rakhine, Myanmar, has been running since 2017, and | think it’s another example worth | sharing with you. People face crises on top of crises — climate change and ongoing conflict has led to more frequent | cyclones and floods, household providers losing livelihoods, displacement, and limited access to healthcare. | As |’m sure you’d expect, adding Covid-19 to that list has hugely intensified the situation. People who were | vulnerable before the pandemic are now in an even more fragile position, and our help has never been more critical. | Communities like those in Rakhine need support that’s tailored to these intense, complex needs — that takes into | account every dimension of each crisis they’re facing. | The Red Cross is the organisation that can give that support. But we need your help to deliver it. | We were made for times like these. For context, in 191 countries, you’ll see a Red Cross — a team of dedicated staff | and volunteers, who work alongside vulnerable communities and know exactly what they need. : | That’s why our programmes really do work. We’re already part of the communities we help. | To take you back to Cox’s Bazar — before the pandemic, we’d been working with some particularly vulnerable | groups there, to help them become more financially resilient. And in the wake of coronavirus, our reports show that | those groups’ income had dropped less than others who hadn’t had that vital training. Ultimately, they were | more prepared for the worst. | With your help, we can continue to make a real impact and strengthen our programmes around the world, to reach | people whose lives depend on it. | These are people who have no safety net, nothing to fall back on, no savings to see them through. People who may | care for children or elderly relatives, who have no idea how they’ll get through the week, who need a lifeline more | than ever right now. | So please donate to our international fund if you can. | | know you might not have expected my letter to (quite literally) fall into your lap today. | know how easy it is to feel | small when the problem is so big. | Know you might be thinking: “there’s no way | can make a difference.” | But, if you’re still reading this letter, | also know that’s simply not true. | The only way we can tackle this is by coming together, taking action, and doing all we can to show that we are not | willing to leave anyone behind, no matter where they are. | It’ll be the response of our lifetime. But it’s what we do, and | hope you'll be a part of it. | Thank you for reading, | fasus. LAS, | Inmaculada Lopez De La Cova Pena | Director of Programmes and Partnerships, British Red Cross | The power | of kindness | P.S. | recognise that my letter may have landed at a hard time for you. If you need help from a friendly Red Crosser, | call our support line on 0808 196 3651. It’s open every day between 10am and 6pm. | mig BritishRedCross | No need to post, there are many ways that you can donate: | \ Call: 0300 023 0827 CI Visit: redcross.org.uk/newfund | 0 Text FUND to 70141 to make a £10 donation | By texting you consent to future telephone & SMS marketing contact | from British Red Cross. Text FUND NO to give £10 without consenting | to calls & texts. Texts cost £10 plus 1 standard message | (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile | The British Red Cross will use your donation to support our work overseas, wherever the | need is greatest. | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in | England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). | Registered with | (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Your Privacy | The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and | will use personal data for the purpose it was collected | or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for | example, to provide goods, services or information you | have requested or to administer donations or services | we provide. We may also analyse data we collect | to better understand the people who support us or | those who use or deliver our services. Sometimes this | means us combining that data with information from | reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor | communications and services in a more focused and | cost effective way, as well as better meeting your needs | and the needs of others like you. However, we will never | do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and | will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with | previously expressed privacy preferences. For full details | about how we use personal data, our legal basis for | doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy | notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy",Newspaper,NA,NA
273,"ee | | -+vUvU | vu oO | ao a | @® et | SJ@ADS}YBIS | Sightsavers Sightsavers | em > ery nn 4 | Nalukena g | Will you | help protect | children from | www.sightsavers.org/ ae www.sightsavers.org/closer www.sightsavers.org/closer | Trachoma steals sight with every blink... | Trachoma is an infection that’s both agonising, and blinding. | At first, it makes your eyes itchy and sore. But if left | untreated, it develops into the more severe trichiasis - | which steals your sight blink by painful blink... | Nalukena had suffered from trachoma since birth - and | at just two years old, it was clear she was in real pain. | Her devastated parents did all they could to help their | little girl, but they didn't understand what was wrong. | They just knew it was getting worse. | Without help, little Nalukena was at risk of losing her | sight altogether. | You can save children from a life of pain | That's why your support today is so vital. Together, we | can reach a whole class of children like Nalukena with | sight-saving treatment - and one day eliminate this cruel | infection for good. | From painful trachoma... | Trachoma starts with a | bite from an infected fly. | 2 WS | The eyes start to itch and weep, | and become very sore in sunlight. | £5 could protect a class of children | Thankfully, we could help Nalukena with an antibiotic called | Zithromax* - which costs just 15p per treatment, and has the | power to stop trachoma in its tracks. | Now, Nalukena no longer has to live in pain, and can look forward | to a happy future. But there are still millions of children across | Africa who are moving closer to blindness each day. It’s vital | we can treat them, before they lose their sight forever. | Your gift will save children’s sight | Just £5 from you is all it takes to provide Zithromax” for SE, | a class of 33 children - saving them from blindness, and | moving us closer to our goal of eliminating trachoma by 2025. | To make a donation, simply complete the form 