276,"a iad | DogsTrust | it Ase an p | ‘Canine Gared For | ect a called vu, = | Cane go ag < < | Make sure your dog is cared for | with a | and that shouldn’t change when life does. With a Canine Care Card, | Please call | You’ve always done what you can to protect your four legged friend, 2820 fSS7. 0006 | you won’t have to worry about what’s next for them, because we will look Bee | and rehome them at one of our 20 rehoming centres in the UK and one in Dublin. | ccc@dogstrust.org.uk 020 7837 0006 | Please quote “334884” or complete this coupon: | dogstrust.org.uk/ccc | [_] Please send me a Dogs Trust Canine Care Card poplication form | (Please fill out in block capitals) | Title First Name | Surname | Address | Postcode 334884 | From time to time we would like to send you exciting updates about our work, products, services and how you can support us, | including fundraising activities and research by post. If you’d rather not receive these mailings, please tick here (] | In order to communicate with you more effectively, better understand your preferences and ability to support our work, we may analyse | your data. We do share your information within the Dogs Trust Group; currently Dogs Trust Worldwide, Dogs Trust Ireland and Dogs Trust | Promotions. To read our full privacy policy visit dogstrust.org.uk/privacy. | Please send this coupon to: Freepost RTJE-SXGL-BEEJ, Dogs Trust, Moulton House, 10 Pond Wood Close, Northampton, NN3 6DF | (No stamp required.) N.B. Service only available for residents of the UK, Ireland, Channel Islands & Isle of Man. | €R) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | A dog is for life® | dogstrust.org.uk | © Dogs Trust 2021 | Registered charity numbers: 227523 & SC037843",Newspaper,NA,NA
277,"Lore) \ | | TA gm | LLY | LL TANS | Lifeboats at Lifeboats | Il ""s£.bk wk cr 4 wey - eG | 2 Aoat volunteers — | are on call right now around | 19,000 miles of coastline. | The RNLI is a charity | independent from | government, so we | rely on donations. | ® = lifeboat station | Donate today | The RNLI is the charity that saves lives at sea | The Royal National Lifeboat Institution, a charity registered in England and Wales (209603), Scotland (SC037736), | the Republic of Ireland (CHY 2678 and 20003326), the Bailiwick of Jersey (14), the Isle of Man (1308 and 006329F), | the Bailiwick of Guernsey and Alderney, of West Quay Road, Poole, Dorset, BH15 1HZ | ‘| don’t ask for payment. | | just ask for the kit and | training that keeps me | ready to save the | next life.’ | Dear friend, | There’s been so much uncertainty in the | last year or so, hasn't there? It makes | me all the more grateful for the things | | can depend upon in uncertain times. | As a volunteer lifeboat crew member, | | don’t know when I'll be called to launch | — or what I’ll face. | just know that I'll | be depending on protective gear, | well-maintained equipment and | up-to-date training. That’s what will get | me through. That's what helps us save lives, | and get home safe ourselves. And what | makes it all possible? Kindness. | That's why | need your help today. | I've been a volunteer here at Hayling Island | for 19 years, and something I’ve learned | from my time on the crew is that no two | rescues are the same. I’ve been called to | aid all sorts of people in all sorts of danger, | from swimmers, surfers and fishing crews | to beachgoers who might only visit the | coast once a year. | It’s the same for our crews all around and | across the UK, from Shetland to the Isles of | Scilly; from Loch Ness to the Thames: we’re | on call to save every one we can. Next time, | it could be someone you know and love. | But we can’t save lives without the kit and | training that keeps us ready. | Your £30 donation today will help | provide everything we need. | The need for our lifesaving service | is increasing — the weather’s unpredictable, | there’s been a surge in staycations and | this year is expected to be our busiest ever. | That means we have to be better prepared | than ever. But kit gets worn out. Lifeboats | need to be maintained. And our world-class | training needs to be maintained with them. | Those are the things that make | the difference. Those are the things that | we depend on. And, because the RNLI is | a charity, that means that we depend | on generous people like you. | Lifeboat volunteers re| | to save lives an | Will you help give the | y on kit and training | d come home safely, | m what they need? | As you read this, we're on call, ready to | launch, day or night, rain or shine. And if | the pager sounds, we'll be depending on | our fellow lifesavers: the crew members | around us, and you. | We would be so grateful for any | support you can give to help us | in the face of uncertainty. | Your sincerely, | etna. | Matt Farr, Volunteer Crew Member, | Hayling Island | How will your kind | gift | £10 © | could buy fuel for a lifeboat could go towards training a | and help our volunteers reach crew member so they have | people in danger at sea. the skills to keep others safe | — and themselves. | could buy a pair of sturdy, | protective, non-slip | seagoing boots, to keep a | volunteer sure-footed on deck. | Photos: Stephen Duncombe, Andy Lyons, RNLI/(Harrison Bates, Nigel Millard, Nathan Williams) | Will you send a gift that will help | to keep volunteers like Matt safe? | Three easy ways to donate: | Moe) PLEASE CUT HERE | C4 Online: \. By phone: | VISIT THE WEBSITE CALL US ON | RNLI.ORG/HOMESAFE 0300 300 0109 | WE'RE OPEN WEEKDAYS, 8AM-6PM | In 2020, for every £1 spent on charitable activities, 56p was on lifeboats, property and | equipment; 27p on running the lifeboat service; 11p on lifeguard rescue; 4p on safety, | education and awareness; and 2p on international drowning prevention. | % By freepost: | COMPLETE AND RETURN | THE FORM OVERLEAF IN AN | ENVELOPE ADDRESSED TO | ‘FREEPOST RNLI’ | NO STAMP IS REQUIRED | 33H LND ASVI1d | PREP21016 | PLEASE COMPLETE AND RETURN THIS | FORM IN AN ENVELOPE ADDRESSED TO | PLAN | ‘FREEPOST RNLI’. NO STAMP IS REQUIRED. Lifeboats | I WANT TO GIVE: (_] £10 [|] £30 [_]£55 | OR MY CHOICE OF: £ | 1S OY | Thank you for your | kind donation today | YOUR DETAILS (PLEASE COMPLETE IN CAPITALS) | Title First Name (in full) Surname | Address | Postcode | Email Mobile phone number | GIFT AID | Gift Aid your donation and boost every £1 by 25p at no extra cost | In order to Gift Aid your donations, you must tick the box below confirming all the below applies: | YES | want to Gift Aid all donations | make in the future or have made in the past 4 years to the RNLI | until | notify you otherwise. Please enter today’s date | | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of | Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | NO 1am unable to Gift Aid this donation. | Please notify the charity if you: want to cancel this declaration; change your name or home address; no longer | pay sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains. | Privacy Notice: We will always store your personal details securely, and they will only be used by the RNLI, RNLI Shop and RNLI College. | Your data may also be used for analysis purposes, to help us provide the best service possible. We will only allow information to be used by | suppliers working on our behalf and we'll only share it if required to do so by law. For full details see our Privacy Policy at RNLI.org/PrivacyPolicy | or contact our Supporter Experience Team on 0300 300 9918 (from the UK) or +44 1202 663234 (from outside the UK). | LET’S KEEP IN TOUCH! | Your support saves lives, and we look forward to keeping in touch with you by post and phone, sharing our | news, activities and appeals. Would you like to receive our emails and text messages too? | Ea Yes, I’m happy to hear from you by email | [| Yes, I'm happy to hear from you by text | Even if you have received our communications in the past, we'll make sure we honour the preferences you | express here. If you would rather not hear from us, or would like to change how we contact you, please | get in touch. Just visit RNLI.org/preferences or call 0300 300 9918. | PAYMENT METHOD | | enclose a cheque/postal order/charity voucher made payable to: ‘RNLI’, | Please debit the sum above from my debit/credit/CAF: | CARD NUMBER EXPIRY DATE | THANK YOU! (FR) FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
278,"A broken smile brings a life | of heartbreak | Clefts are the world’s third most common birth defect. | In the UK most babies receive corrective surgery within the first | year but children in the poorest countries have | no chance of life-saving surgery. | Every 3 minutes, a child is born with a cleft lip or cleft palate. | Children with a cleft are often malnourished, have difficulties | speaking, breathing and hearing. They are also bullied by other | children, so many are not attending school and are hidden away. | It can take as little as 45 minutes and | £150 to change a child’s life forever | Operation@)smile | re = ‘ma | mA | ae err | seg fll fff tte hy ae | Freepost RSYJ -HGEK-RGBX ] | peaatfonanle Please men | Slough | smile «SL our broken smiles | You are changing | a life today. | Thank you for | . your gift | Operation€)smile | Charity Registration Number 1091316 | “Hearing my daughters pronounce ‘Mama’ properly | for the first time brought me tears of joy” | Laila never heard “Mama” spoken properly by | her daughters Jheleen, aged four, and Andrea, | aged three. Each baby girl was born with a cleft | condition. This made feeding very difficult for them, | let alone speaking - and with their condition came | a young life full of ridicule and shame for this family | from the Philippines. | Laila and her husband Ronald doted on their two | beautiful daughters, but they lived in constant | worry as to how they would be able to heal their | daughters’ broken mouths. Ronald’s meagre | income barely allowed them to feed and clothe their | family - they couldn’t imagine how they could ever | afford the surgery that would change Jheleen and | Andrea’s lives. | Every | three minutes | a baby is | born with | medical team | operating | for free | for two weeks, for free. | A highly trained Ea | @ During a typical project, our volunteer medical | teams will operate on 120 children. | @ Everyone on the team is a specialist in their field. | @ Everyone gives up their time to work long hours, | @ Their expertise, skills and dedication are why | our operations can cost as little as £150. | When they received a neighbourhood flyer that told | them surgery was both possible for their young girls | and free, they immediately pre-registered for the | Operation Smile mission to Cavite, in the Philippines. | After surgery, the girls were each given a mirror | so they could see their new smiles. It took Andrea | three days before she accepted that she was the | little girl looking back at herself. | For Laila, hearing Jneleen & Andrea pronounce | ‘Mama’ properly for the first time brought her tears | of complete happiness. | The girls are no longer stared at, teased and called | names. They love to go to school and play with | other children. | It can take | Just 45 minutes | and £150 to | ange a life | BY A | Jheleen & Andrea AFTER | Medical Information | Scientific research | indicates that taking | multivitamins such as | vitamin B6, folic acid | and zinc one month | pre-conception and | during the early months | of pregnancy, as well as | not smoking or drinking | may reduce the | incidence of clefting | and other birth defects. | For more advice on | prenatal care,you should | consult your doctor or | healthcare expert. | Operation Smile provides free surgeries to repair cleft lip, cleft palate and other | facial conditions for children around the globe. | DETACH HERE | I am happy to mend a broken smile and change a life. | Here is my gift of... | LJ £150 helps provide cleft surgery for a child L] e15 pays for antibiotics for 10 children | L] £50 helps pay for medical supplies for an LJ My gift of £ | operation | Mr/Mrs/Ms/Miss/Other First Name Surname | Address | Postcode | Home Telephone Mobile. | Email | I authorise you to debit my card with the amount of £ | Amex LJ Mastercard L] Visa a Delta L] Maestro L] | ant tt | cardno.L_| Lt }LE tT Ly LL LLL LS a seo i | Start date LILI Expiry date LL WTI Issue No MAESTRO ONLY s | (See | Signature = | OR send a cheque: I enclose a cheque payable to Operation Smile UK for £ | | OR Give on 0800 408 1828 or operationsmile.org.uk/smile43 fk | FOLD | Please don’t forget to tick here and make your gift worth even more | Make your donation worth 25% more at no extra cost to you. | Yes, | am a UK tax payer. | would like Operation Smile to treat all donations that | have made over the past | four years and all donations that | make now and in the future as Gift Aid donations unless | notify you otherwise. | | confirm that | have paid or will pay an amount of Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax for each tax year (6 April to 5 April) that is at least | equal to the amount of tax that all the charities and CASC that | donate to will reclaim on my gifts for that tax year. | understand that other | taxes such as VAT and Council Tax do not qualify. | understand the charity will reclaim 25p of tax on every £1 that | give. | giftasd it | ( Your gift is changing children’s lives and we would like to show you the impact you are making. We will | send you information about our work, campaigns and fundraising: | (_} Don’t contact me by Post (_] YES, contact me byPhone (1 YES, contact me by email | (_] YES, contact me bySMS — [_] Please send me information on leaving a legacy to Operation Smile in my will | You can change your personal details or request that we stop contacting you at any time. Call 0203 475 5126 or | email info@operationsmile.org.uk. Operation Smile will not sell or swap your details with any other organisation. | Thank you from the children whose lives will change because of your gift | Operation@)smile | Charity Registration Number 1091316 | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | MOISTEN HERE",Newspaper,NA,NA
279,".... _ a ay : 42% he i - | a yor. | as Sightsavers atte: A Sightsavers | SJ@ADS}YBIS | nowwn | 2a7cc- | —- 330 | SFvuvuUS | UD OM @ et | aor as | 239 4 Ww | oz < | on = oO | Soo 5 | I< Ww | Will you | help protect | children from | Nalukena Geiss | ~ Just £5 fr . | could save her sight. | www.sightsavers.org/closer | www.sightsavers.org -_— www.sightsavers.org/closer | Trachoma steals sight with every blink... | Trachoma is an infection that’s both agonising, and blinding. | At first, it makes your eyes itchy and sore. But if left | untreated, it develops into the more severe trichiasis - | which steals your sight blink by painful blink... | Nalukena had suffered from trachoma since birth - and | at just two years old, it was clear she was in real pain. | Her devastated parents did all they could to help their | little girl, but they didn't understand what was wrong. | They just knew it was getting worse. | Without help, little Nalukena was at risk of losing her | sight altogether. | You can save children from a life of pain | That's why your support today is so vital. Together, we | can reach a whole class of children like Nalukena with | sight-saving treatment - and one day eliminate this cruel | infection for good. | From painful trachoma... | Trachoma starts with a | bite from an infected fly. | 2 WS | The eyes start to itch and weep, | and become very sore in sunlight. | £5 could protect a class of children | Thankfully, we could help Nalukena with an antibiotic called | Zithromax* - which costs just 15p per treatment, and has the | power to stop trachoma in its tracks. | Now, Nalukena no longer has to live in pain, and can look forward | to a happy future. But there are still millions of children across | Africa who are moving closer to blindness each day. It’s vital | we can treat them, before they lose their sight forever. | Your gift will save children’s sight | Just £5 from you is all it takes to provide Zithromax” for SE, | a class of 33 children - saving them from blindness, and | moving us closer to our goal of eliminating trachoma by 2025. | To make a donation, simply complete the form | opposite and return it in the attached envelope, | give online, or call O800 298 2200 today. | ...to blinding trichiasis | gs <> The eyelids then turn inwards, causing 4 <p> | the eyelashes to scrape the eye. | This condition is trichiasis, | which eventually steals sight. | ‘Will you send £5 today and save a class of children from blinding trachoma? | 4 DETACH HERE & | 4 DETACH HERE & | Yes, | want to give £5 to stop trachoma and save the sight of children like Nalukena | Title First name Surname | Full home address | Postcode | | Phone number | Email | Are you happy to receive updates and find out how you can help by email or telephone? | If so, please fill in your details above. | We want you to be really proud of the work you're helping make | happen and will be in touch from time to time with updates about ThroughGiftAid,any dik | how your support is changing lives. To do this, we'll use the details donation you give will giftaid | you've provided but promise never to sell or share your data. be worth 25% more. | If you'd rather not hear from us, please let us know by emailing tam a UK taxpayer and | would like | info@sightsavers.org or calling 01444 446600. Sightsavers to reclaim the tax paid on all my | past, present and future. | understand | | would like to make a donation of £ | = that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains | Tax in the current tax year than the amount | Please make cheque/postal order payable to Sightsavers | of Gift Aid claimed on my donations, it is my | Or debit my: O MasterCard OVisa O CAF noon responsibility to pay any difference. | St tT | TICE LLICLLLICLL ID (CO I'd like Sightsavers to claim | Gift Aid on my donations. | eC LICL) sy COCD | [Name on card | | Signature ] | Date | Your donation will be used to support our work wherever the need is greatest. | Please detach this form and return it, with your gift, in the FREEPOST envelope attached. | Alternatively, visit www.sightsavers.org/closer or call 0800 298 2200. Thank you. | 207544 and $CO38110 | 4@ DETACH HERE | 4& DETACH HERE & | MOISTEN HERE AND SEAL | SIN' | Registered with | FUNDRAIS | REGULATOR | iS) Sightsavers | Every penny counts | and for every pound we receive"" | 91% goes on vital charity work | and our funding | Thank you for your support | $s 207544 and SCO3B110 | Registered charity number",Newspaper,NA,NA
