282,"igs: BritishRedCross | Humanity triumphs when | _ good people do something | Millions of people worldwide are in danger. | The impact of Covid-19 has caused a truly | frightening rise in levels of extreme poverty, | putting the previous two decades of progress | into sharp reverse. | Communities already struggling to protect themselves from the worst effects | of climate change and ongoing conflict are now facing an even deeper crisis. | ‘It would be easy to read this and feel hopeless. It would be understandable | to think there’s nothing you can do to help. But we can do something. | The Red Cross Movement was created for times like these. We have the local | knowledge, the networks and teams on the ground to reach the people in this | desperate situation who have nowhere else to turn. We just need your support. Minara in Cox’s Bazar, | Bangladesh. We’ve been | Please give to our International Relief Fund today, if you can. supporting her and other | f in th ion) & | We must reach the people who need us most. edibek abe alibi! | 0300 023 0825 or visit redcross.org.uk/humanity | Text PROVIDE to 70141 to make a £10 donation. | SSOID POY YSHUG/IUBU TV @ O}0Ud | By texting, you consent to future telephone and SMS marketing contact from British Red Cross. | Text PROVIDE NO to 70141 to give £10 without consenting to calls and texts.* | Please send to: 2021 Summer Appeal Press, Ref: 176339, Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ, British Red Cross, 176339 | Bumpers Way, Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | | would like to make a donation of £20(] £4001] £60C] £100() Othere{ | | CI enclose a cheque, made payable to British Red Cross OR [_] Please debit my Visa/Mastercard/CAF Charity card with the amount specified | card number] TT ILE TT ILET TILE expiry date | | |/[_] | | Title Forename _ Surname | Address | Postcode | Phone number™ **Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are happy for | Email** ; us to contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and | how you can donate and help in other ways. ~ | Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. | Olam a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, as well as any future donations, until | rs a d ue | notify them otherwise. Please tick. | understand that if | pay less income/capital gains tax than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations in the tax year ~ Gf a | in which they are received, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to let us know of any changes to your tax status, including changes to | your name or address, or if you need to cancel this agreement. . | Keeping in touch Your support makes a life-changing difference to people in crisis. We write to our supporters to update you about the.work of the British Red Cross, and how you can help and donate in | other ways. You can change the way we contact you at any time by visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch or calling Freephone 0800 2800 491. | Privacy statement The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and will use personal data for the purpose it was collected or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for example, to provide | goods, services or information you have requested or to administer donations or services we provide. We may also analyse data we collect to better understand the people who support us or those who use or deliver our | services. Sometimes this means us combining that data with information from reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor communications and services in a more focused and cost-effective way, as well as | better meeting your needs and the needs of others like you. However, we will never do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with previously expressed privacy | preferences. For full details about how we use personal data, our legal basis for doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy. ; | The British Red Cross will use your donation to support our work overseas, wherever the need is greatest. For more information | visit redcross.org.uk | *Texts cost £10 +1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile FR Registered with Th e owe r | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in FU NDR AISING p ; | England and Wales (220949), Scotland (SC037738), Isle of Man (0752) and Jersey (430). BRC21-087 | REGULATOR of kindness",Newspaper,NA,NA
