287,"Auoa Anw uBisap Ao} 40S ; ¥ y | jyood awos}em igre, Ae Rh Ue | UnoA jo und sp y)) ‘ a: ali Re | Ao} WyOs D 306 0} A, wed Sa | opo, dn ubig Jeg | | / ar | ; Pa oe | a rt Cy ms | a mila | fe bo = | ; = = | = | b | . "" > | : | DODSL | WD = | \ i 7 | | ) ) Yo US: 1 Od! JOLL ) OL | Be d 4 | | fa"" m 4 “ | j OIi@lORE 810 1 @ 816 | t yA f L | } em BR a a= a S 1 1 +t gw | , aS | @ ) H kZ i Bg * »le | ’ -~, Clin { 9S | e Fi) ei< | \ i te a oe 7 3 D | One day, Derek will transform | someone's life, but we need | your help to get him there. | Sponsoring a guide dog puppy like Derek is an | unforgettable experience that follows their journey | from six weeks old to the moment they are partnered | with someone living with sight loss. As Derek's sponsor, | you will be at the heart of his journey as he grows up to | become a life-changing guide dog. You can also sponsor | Derek as a gift, to let a loved one know you are thinking | of them. | In our 90 years as a charity, | we have created over 35,000 | guide dog partnerships. | Guide Dogs works to empower people living with sight | loss and help to ensure they don't lose their freedom. | By sponsoring Derek your generosity will help transform | the lives of people living with sight loss, like Stacey. | Stacey lost her central vision when she was just 21. | I felt all my happiness and bubbliness | go away. I couldn't go out by myself. | But as soon as Toffee came trotting up | my road, I knew he was my dog. The | moment we met it was love! On the day | my friends graduated as nurses - | the day I would have graduated too | - I qualified as a guide dog owner | and started my new Life with Toffee. | He inspired me to live again. ~ | - Stacey | Did you know? Derek is named after Derek Freeman, founder of the Guide Dogs breeding programme. | There are hundreds of people | in the UK currently waiting for | a guide dog. You can be part of | their journey to independence. | You can help our newest recruits, Derek, Judy, and | Niko, become fully-trained guide dogs by sponsoring | them for yourself or a loved one from just £1 a week. | With your help, we can bring hope to the lives of even | more people in the UK living with sight loss. | Niko | Derek Judy | From just £1 a week, | your sponsorship will include: | ¢ Acuddly guide dog puppy toy | ¢ A fridge magnet | ¢ A photo album with regular photos | ¢ Asponsorship certificate | ¢ Access to your puppy's exclusive Facebook group | ¢ Regular ‘Pupdates’ for two years with news of | your puppy’s progress | ¢ An exclusive calendar at the end of each year | ® The chance to forever change the life of a | person who is blind or partially sighted | Designs may vary slightly. Electronic devices are | for illustrative purposes only, devices not included. | 2 pte | Bs ORE Nai alain. fe ccs soa Tee = | Order today to get a soft toy as part of your welcome pack! | Please ensure you have signed up online/via phone” by 5 September 2021. | Derek, Judy, and Niko will no longer be available for sponsorship after this date. | Guide Dogs is a working name of The Guide Dogs for the Blind Association. Registered Office: Hillfields, Burghfield Common, Reading, Berkshire RG7 3Y¥G. A company limited by guarantee registered in England and Woles | (291646) and a charity registered in England and Wales (209617) and Scotland (SCO38979). GDO389 04/21. Tel: 0800 052 0007 Email: sapenquiries@guidedogs.org.uk Website: guidedogs.org.uk/SponsorDerek S21016168",Newspaper,NA,NA
288,"A gift in your Will helps the dogs | and cats who deserve it most | For over 160 years, Battersea has been here | for every dog and cat, taking them in without | question and caring for them without judgement | until we find them the homes where they truly | belong. One in three of these animals is cared for | thanks to gifts in Wills. | By remembering Battersea in your Will, you help | ensure that we can continue to be here for every | dog and cat who needs us. Gifts in Wills are | vital to all areas of our work, So any gift you give, | whatever size, will make a big difference to the | animals in our care, | A gift in your Will costs you nothing today but | will help ensure that Battersea can continue to | support the animals who need us tomorrow. | Together, we will be here for every dog and cat. | ¢u BATTERSEA | Name | Address",Newspaper,NA,NA
289,"An open letter to | Guardian readers | The people of Yemen need your help. For more than six years, we’ve lived | under the shadow of war..In some areas of the country we are seeing near | famine conditions. Children, women and men could die from hunger. | Yet, the fighting goes on. The current offensive in Marib, less than 100 miles | from my home in Sana’a, has killed hundreds and forced tens of thousands to | flee. The war affects everything. Public sector workers, such as teachers and | police officers, haven’t been paid regularly since 2017. Electricity is 900% more | expensive than in 2015. People have sold all their assets, but many are barely | surviving. Tragically, some have taken their own lives. To me, they are just as | much casualties of this war as people who die when their homes are hit. | When the bombing starts, my wife and | take the children to the safe room. We | tell them the explosions are people playing with fireworks. We haven't suffered a | direct hit yet, but many of my neighbours haven't been so lucky. When | go for a | walk, | see displaced families living on the sidewalk and under bridges, with only | cardboard and plastic sheeting to protect them. | And then we have COVID-19, which has seen the international community cut aid | to Yemen. It feels as if, while our people suffer, the world is looking the other way. | UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres said recently: “Millions of Yemeni children, | women and men desperately need aid to live. Cutting aid is a death sentence.” | So yes, the situation is dire. But no, we will not give up. Famine is edging closer, | but it’s not too late to help people. UNHCR has identified the most at risk families, | and with your help today could provide them with an Emergency Payment of | £143. The payment of £143 supports a family of six and is based on the cost of | a ‘Survival Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of essentials such as food, water and | medicine. For a family on the brink of famine, it could be the difference between | life and death. | Thank you. | Ebrahim Madaghesh, UNHCR Yemen | £143 could provide a family with an EMERGENCY | PAYMENT to buy food and other essentials | Give now at | unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in and return the form below | I would like to give: |_| £72 |_| 2143 _] e286 LJ others | L]1 enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | _]1 would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. * | Expiry date | Signature Date | L] Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title First name Lastname | Address | Postcode | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: LJ By email O By phone | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | [i would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p for each £1 ti fad d aw | donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four = | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand that if | pay less | Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tex than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is | my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy. You can opt out of any communications at any | time me contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | va Scan this Registered with A Ny | (FR) FUNDRAISING y WU Ni ae CR | REGULATOR | QR code to | donate online | ‘a * A minimum of 75% of your gift will directly help displaced £ The UN Refugee Agency | ""2s people in Yemen, funding Emergency Payments and pict prae UL | [a] HAE other humanitarian interventions. | ne United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). P21YEGUB1",Newspaper,NA,NA
