294,"Create a kinder | future for | people living | with dementia » | Will you consider leaving a gift in your Will to | Alzheimer’s Society? | Your gift will help fund research into a cure. And | until we get there, you'll help tackle the injustices | in the system to ensure people with dementia are | not forgotten. | For too long, the UK’s unjust and underfunded | social care system has let people living with | dementia down, failing to recognise their needs, or | the emotional and financial impact their condition | has on those who love them. | Thanks to income from gifts in Wills, we were able | to react quickly during the pandemic, stepping in | to provide invaluable support for people struggling | to cope with isolation, anxiety and fear under | lockdown. | Agift in your Will can ensure people affected by | dementia always have somebody to turn to. | Dementia can leave everybody affected feeling | powerless. As the condition takes hold, people | I LJ Please send me my free guide to leaving a gift in my Will | see their loved ones diminish before their eyes. A | gift in your Will could fund the research that helps | you take back control of the future health of your | family, giving scientists the resources to develop | new treatments for generations to come. | For over 30 years, investing in research has been | central to Alzheimer’s Society’s mission. We now | Know so much more about the potential of fields | like genetics and immunology. The only thing | holding us back is lack of funding. | Your legacy can be the investment in research | that speeds up the search for a cure. | A gift in your Will, of even just 1% of your estate, | could help achieve the step-change we | desperately need. Because if we in the dementia | community don’t look out for each other, who will? | You can help us improve the dementia care | system at the same time as we develop new | treatments — ensuring people with dementia are | not forgotten. | Request your free guide to leaving a gift in your Will today. | visit alzheimers.org.uk/willguide | call 0370 0110290 or fill out and return the form below. | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode | Email Phone | We'd love to send you updates on our life-changing services | and research, as well as our fundraising, campaigning and | volunteering activities. Please tick below to let us know you're | happy for us to stay in touch. | L) By email L) By phone [) Please don’t contact me via post | We will never sell your details to any third | parties, please see alzheimers.org.uk/privacy | for more information. If you'd like to change | what you receive from us at any time, please | call Customer Care on 0330 333 0804 | | Postin your own envelope to: Freepost NOT FORGOTTEN iet | fl You do not need a stamp or any other address details. ponirn | q Please follow Government isolation and distancing guidelines if posting. a aoe A | Registered charity no. 296645. Alzheimer’s Society operates in England, | Wales and Northern Ireland. | Registered with | (FR FUNDRAISING | LGPRAQ721M REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
