310,"You can | trust us | WaterAid | . We'll use your donations in the best way possible. | For every £1 you give, 77p is spent on enabling | people to transform their lives with clean water, | decent toilets and good hygiene, and 23p | IS spent on fundraising**. | . We promise your details are safe with us. | We'll respect your privacy and never share your | details with any other organisation or charity | for commercial or fundraising purposes. | You can choose how often we contact you. | Just call our Supporter Care Team on | 020 7793 4594. | Your support helps deliver lasting solutions, | not short-term fixes. | We will share stories of the people you help. | **As of 2019/20 WaterAid Annual Report | a TWO MILLION POUNDS is a lot to ask we know. But look at it this way. | If every household in our country gives just £2 a month, WaterAid will be able | to start changing the lives of some of the 785 million people who still lack clean | water - and the 2 billion people without their own toilet. That’s one in four people | on the planet. | Some might say that’s impossible, but at WaterAid we don’t. We know you must think | big to solve a big problem. Let's face it, in the UK we all take clean water and decent | toilets as a human right and a normal part of everyday life. We couldn't imagine life | without them. What better reason for every household to give a little to share this | life-changing good fortune? | Over 800 children die every day because of dirty water and poor sanitation. But it’s not | just about saving lives. Water changes everything. With clean water, decent toilets and | good hygiene, children are free to grow up healthy and go to school. Women and men | get to earn a living. Whole communities start to thrive. Together, people like you have | already helped transform the lives of over 27 million people with clean water. | What we do works, but we need to do | more of it. | Olivia lives in Madagascar. Every day she collected | dirty water from a river, filled with germs and | bacteria that made her sick. WaterAid and local | partners worked with Olivia's community to help | them install waterpoints in the village and at | her school. Access to clean water has been life | changing for Olivia. “Now we have running water | from the tap at school”. With clean water, Olivia | doesn't have to worry about getting sick and | missing school - she can focus on her education. | Olivia's world is changing. For the better. | We could take our solution to everyone, | everywhere in this world of ours. But not | without you. Create the world that children | like Olivia should be living in. Every penny counts | - please fill in the form and send it back today. | Olivia is the next generation, | the one that will be different. | That’s what your small | gift of £2 a month can do. | Be the change. Be the change. | Say 5 RECYCLED Registered with | x Paper made from (FR) FUNDRAISING | 3 - f ‘a FSC recycled ache REGU LATO R | Pag * wwwtscomn FSC® COO960 | dW. Aid | Registered charity numbers 288701 (England and Wales) and SC039479 (Scotland) ro ater | pjejEWULeLpUeY JSBUIT/PIyiaIeM :sojoUd j}Vy | TEAR HERE AND SEAL MOISTEN HERE - TEAR HERE AND SEAL | MOISTEN | Fold here | I'll be the change. Here’s my monthly gift of £2. | Call now on 0300 123 4341"", fill in the form below or donate online at www.wateraid.org/52million | £2 a month could save children’s £5 a month could save children’s £10 a month could save children’s lives. | lives. In just 12 months your donations lives. In just 12 months your donations In just 12 months your donations could | could install a handwashing station for could provide a clean water tank for a install water pipes in Ethiopia | three families in Sierra Leone school in Burkina Faso | : : You can hear how you change lives. We hope you will | Here s my life-changing gift of fill out your contact details below to hear more about | £2 £5 £10 Surprise us! £ taht notce, Children like Olivia, fundraising, and opportunities to | get involved. If you are happy to hear from us by phone | ptanuiig OMe ate ae eae and email, please let us know your details: | | should be at least four weeks | Month Year | from date of signing Tel no. (home/mobile): | Title: First name: Email: | Sunaina: Many people love to receive postal updates. | Tick if you'd prefer not to _| | Home address: WaterAid and WaterAid Trading will use your personal details to communicate with you in the ways | , you have agreed to, and as explained in our Privacy Policy. We may use the information you share | with us and background information about you that we obtain from publicly available sources to | carry out analysis (sometimes using suppliers) to tailor our communications to be more appropriate | and relevant to your interests. You can withdraw your consent at any time. For full details, including | information about your privacy rights, see our Privacy Policy at www.wateraid.org/privacy | Postcode: To change your preferences, or request to stop receiving | communications please contact us on 020 7793 4594 or | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid without i s | ese tee eee at supportercare@wateraid.org SARA | 7) MRSA contend by signing uP to Gift Aid an no extra cost to you. Tick Heke: e , giftaid itr | e will be worth 2 more, at NO extra cost to yot ing up to Gift Aid is simple, all you nee ( tick the b | 2 paid on all your donations 1 t four years, and any futu ons you may | y as much UK income and/or capital gains tax aterAid (and any other organisation you may support) will reclaim in each tax year | you donate. If you pay less it is your responsibility to pay back any difference. Gift Aid will be used to fund WaterAid’s general work | WaterAid Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by direct debit. | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: Service user number ¢ g ) | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST, WaterAid, York House, York YO26 7NH. Ai0'6'7'8{9 DIRECT | Debit | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society (DO NOT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) | To the Manager: Bank/building society Reference (to be completed by WaterAid) | Branch address: | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please pay WaterAid | Direct Debits from the account detailed in this Instruction subject to | the safeguards assured by the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand | Postcode: that this Instruction may remain with WaterAid and, if so, details will | be passed electronically to my bank/building society. | Name(s) of account holder(s): Signature(s) | Bank/building society account number Branch sort code | = x xX Date | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account. | ay Pjo4",Newspaper,NA,NA
