316,"WOODLAND | TRUST | log "" | Please, if you love | | trees, you need to | read this... | The Woodland Trust is a charity registered in England and Wales (no. 294344) and in Scotland (no. SC038885). / ) ra ni | | responsible sources | Cy recycle Images: Stuart Shore, Wight Wildlife Photography. WTML/John Bridges. CP00048 06/21 € Fsc “eer | Help us protect the UK’s | threatened woods and | wildlife, with membership | of the Woodland Trust. | “| joined the Woodland Trust to U A | make sure children will always have | woods to play in, just as we did.” S m | Why od 5 | membership _ | _ matters | WOODLAND | TRUST | There are great | benefits to joining the | Woodland Trust. And | you'll be helping us do | all this too... | Protect | The Woodland Trust works tirelessly to save the | UR’s remaining precious and irreplaceable ancient | woodland and keep it safe for future generations. | By becoming a member you'll be directly helping us | continue this vital work - 1,225 ancient woods are | under threat right now. | Join the Woodland Trust and help us care for and | restore damaged woodland so we can help wildlife | and native plants to thrive once again. | “Llove taking my Woodland Trust | leaf swatch out to the woods to try | and identify all the trees I see.” | Rachel Harding, Member since 2006 | “It feels wonderful to know you’re | helping create brand new woodland.” | Danny Hewis, Member since 2013 | Create | Your membership will help us plant trees which | can grow into flourishing new woods in as little as | 12 years. We have planted more than 50 million | trees since 1972 and we'll be getting 50 million | more in the ground by 2025. | Your support means we can own and care for more | than 1,000 woods across the UK that we'll keep | open and completely free for everyone. | Help us protect the woodland homes | of our threatened plants and wildlife. | WOODLAND | TRUST | Thank you for | becoming a member | and protecting | UK’s woodland. | Please affix | postage | stamp here | to help | reduce our | costs. | Freepost RTHA-JRSU-SSIX | Membership Team | The woodland Trust | Kempton way | GRANTHAM | NG31 6LL | Jogo l fff fen tf fH Uhl |  | WOODLAND | TRUST | Please. If you love trees, Nas ¢ | join the Woodland Trust today | and fight for their future. | Dear friend, | My name is Darren Moorcroft and | am privileged to be the head of the | Woodland Trust - the UK’s largest woodland conservation charity. Maybe | you have already heard of us and what we are doing to protect woods, | plant trees and create havens for wildlife across the nation. | I’m writing today with a stark warning - and a plea for your help. | The natural world is in crisis and we are facing a catastrophic collapse in | biodiversity which, without urgent action, will have consequences for every | one of us. Our work standing up for woods and trees has never been more | important. | I’m sure you'll agree that the pandemic has really brought home how vital | fresh air, green space, parks and woodland are for our physical health and | mental wellbeing. But woods aren't just lovely places for a relaxing walk | among nature, and trees give us so much more than colour and beauty. | Both trees and woods are essential for the future of our planet. | Join the Woodland | Trust today to | receive this unique | leaf swatch book. | You may have seen in the news recently that the Woodland Trust has just | published a report with ground-breaking evidence showing in shocking | detail just how critical native woods and trees are in the fight against the | climate and nature crisis we are in. | Yet UK woodland, and the wildlife it supports, is in serious trouble. | Threats against woods and trees are escalating and woodland wildlife is | in sharp decline. Because you are reading this, | believe you care about | protecting the woodland the UK has, and helping us create more havens | for rare and precious wildlife species. Trees are crucial for our environment | and without them, we, our children and grandchildren, and of course the | wildlife that depends on them for survival, face an uncertain future. | Trees and woods in this country are under threat every day - from | development, from tree pests and diseases and from the effects of climate | change. And that means thousands of species are at risk too. But there is | a way you can help. | Continued overleaf | Yes, | will join the Woodland Trust today. | Yes, | want to keep woodlands safe and unspoiled wy | as a Woodland Trust member ae | ah Please fill in your details below - | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode Date of birth (optional) / / | Details of second member for joint membership (if applicable) | Title First name Last name | My email address is: My daytime telephone number is: | Let’s keep in touch! | In addition to receiving your membership benefits we would like to keep in touch with you about what we're doing for woods, trees and wildlife! You'll receive | regular updates, including our latest news, products and exciting events. Along with ways you can get involved with campaigns, fundraising and much more. | Would you like us to contact you by email? [_]Yes please, I'd like to hear from you by email. | We may contact you in the future by post and phone; please let us know if you'd prefer us not to. | [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not to hear from you by post [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not hear from you by phone | You can unsubscribe from marketing at any time: visit our online permission portal - woodlandtrust.yourpreferencecentre.com, call 0330 333 3300, or | email supporters@woodlandtrust.org.uk. Your privacy is our priority and we promise to keep your details safe. For full details on how and why we collect, | store and use your personal information take a look at our online Privacy Policy - woodlandtrust.org.uk/privacy-policy and our Legitimate Interest | Statement —- woodlandtrust.org.uk/legitimate-interests. CSO9 | Make a 25% bigger difference to woodland with Gift Aid | Boost your donation by 25p of Gift Aid for every £1 you donate. all my donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any | The Woodland Trust can reclaim the tax you pay for the current tax year. difference. Please notify us if you want to cancel this declaration, | C] ll P change your name or home address, or, if you no longer pay | YES. | confirm that | am a UK taxpayer and | want to Gift Aid my donation, andany sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains. i pe | donations | make in the future, or have made in the past 4 years to the Woodland Trust. QA d uw | If | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on L] Please tick if you are not a UK taxpayer. | Pay for your membership by Direct Debit | Single Membership LJ £4* LJ £5 L] £10 or [e | a month | Joint Membership LJ £4.50* L] £6 L] £10 or [fs a month *Minimurm monthly payment | Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by Direct Debit | Service user number Debit | To the Manager lo}3jol2fe]4| | Reference number (to be completed by The Woodland Trust) | Address | Postcode Instruction to your Bank or Building Society: Please pay The Woodland Trust Direct Debits | from the account detailed in this instruction subject to the safeguards assured by the Direct | Name(s) of account holder(s) Debit Guarantee. | understand that this instruction may remain with The Woodland Trust | and, if so, details will be passed electronically to my Bank/Building Society. Registered | office: The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire, NG31 6LL | Bank/building society account number | Signature(s) | Branch sort code | Date / / | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit instructions for some types of account. | Pay for your membership by cheque or Credit/Debit Car | Single Membership L] £48 a year*™ or [fe a year | Joint Membership L] £54 a year™* or [sid a year | **Minimum annual payment | I'd like to make a donation of E | | enclose a cheque made payable to: The Woodland Trust. | Total | £ | Please write your name and address on the reverse. | Please debit my Credit / Debit Card: [ ]yisa | |B) [ | Signatiires) | Card number Expiry date | LILI T IE ILE TT ILE Tt) Le] vain EE ~ | oan EE | Simply complete this form, fold it in half and return it to us at: M21ADT021 (FR) | Freepost RTHA-JRSU-SSJX, Membership Team, The Woodland Trust, Kempton Thank you FUNDRAISING | Way, Grantham NG316LL _ join online at woodlandtrust.org.uk/join | 2998/C/AB | Join the Woodland Trust from just | £4 a month and help save UK woods and | the wildlife that lives there. | Free welcome pack | when you join | Your membership will help us... | As a member of the UK’s largest woodland | conservation charity you'll be helping protect native | woodland and create new woods throughout the UK. | Our members have helped us plant more than | 50 million trees so far. | There are great benefits to joining the Woodland Trust: | + Your own ‘leaf swatch’ tree identification guide so you can | enjoy tree-spotting and get to know the great variety of | trees you are helping to protect as a member. | * A directory of over 1,000 woods to visit throughout the UK so | wherever you are, you'll be able to enjoy a walk in the woods. | * Four issues of Broadleaf, our exclusive members’ magazine, | each year and a membership card. | “Woods are so important | for future generations. It’s | devastating to think my | grandchildren won’t be able to | enjoy such delights as | do. There’s | nothing better for the soul than | being deep in a wood, watching | wildlife, hearing birdsong and | forgetting the hustle and bustle | of everyday life.” | Carol, Woodland Trust member, Essex. | Save the woodland homes of the wildlife | we love. | The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire NG31 6LL. Tel. 0330 333 3300 woodlandtrust.org.uk. The Woodland Trust is a charity registered in | England and Wales (No. 294344) and in Scotland (No. SCO38885). A non-profit-making company limited by guarantee. Registered in England No. 1982873.",Newspaper,NA,NA
