nd fight for their future. | Dear friend, | My name is Darren Moorcroft and | am privileged to be the head of the | Woodland Trust — the UK’s largest woodland conservation charity. Maybe | you have already heard of us and what we are doing to protect woods, | plant trees and create havens for wildlife across the nation. | I’m writing today with a stark warning - and a plea for your help. | The natural world is in crisis and we are facing a catastrophic collapse in | biodiversity which, without urgent action, will have consequences for every | one of us. Our work standing up for woods and trees has never been more | important. | I’m sure you'll agree that the pandemic has really brought home how vital | fresh air, green space, parks and woodland are for our physical health and | mental wellbeing. But woods aren't just lovely places for a relaxing walk | among nature, and trees give us so much more than colour and beauty. | Both trees and woods are essential for the future of our planet. | Join the Woodland | You may have seen in the news recently that the Woodland Trust has just | published a report with ground-breaking evidence showing in shocking | detail just how critical native woods and trees are in the fight against the | climate and nature crisis we are in. | Trust today to | receive this unique | leaf swatch book. | Yet UK woodland, and the wildlife it supports, is in serious trouble. | Threats against woods and trees are escalating and woodland wildlife is | in sharp decline. Because you are reading this, | believe you care about | protecting the woodland the UK has, and helping us create more havens | for rare and precious wildlife species. Trees are crucial for our environment | and without them, we, our children and grandchildren, and of course the | wildlife that depends on them for survival, face an uncertain future. | Trees and woods in this country are under threat every day - from | development, from tree pests and diseases and from the effects of climate | change. And that means thousands of species are at risk too. But there is | a way you can help. | Continued overleaf | Yes, | will join the Woodland Trust today. | Yes, | want to keep woodlands safe and unspoiled wy | as a Woodland Trust member a | eh Please fill in your details below - | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode Date of birth (optional) / i | Details of second member for joint membership (if applicable) | Title First name Last name | My email address is: My daytime telephone number is: | Let’s keep in touch! | In addition to receiving your membership benefits we would like to keep in touch with you about what we're doing for woods, trees and wildlife! You'll receive | regular updates, including our latest news, products and exciting events. Along with ways you can get involved with campaigns, fundraising and much more. | Would you like us to contact you by email? [_]Yes please, I'd like to hear from you by email. | We may contact you in the future by post and phone; please let us know if you'd prefer us not to. | [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not to hear from you by post [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not hear from you by phone | You can unsubscribe from marketing at any time: visit our online permission portal - woodlandtrust.yourpreferencecentre.com, call 0330 333 3300, or | email supporters@woodlandtrust.org.uk. Your privacy is our priority and we promise to keep your details safe. For full details on how and why we collect, | store and use your personal information take a look at our online Privacy Policy - woodlandtrust.org.uk/privacy-policy and our Legitimate Interest | Statement —- woodlandtrust.org.uk/legitimate-interests. CSO9 | Make a 25% bigger difference to woodland with Gift Aid | Boost your donation by 25p of Gift Aid for every £1 you donate. all my donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any | The Woodland Trust can reclaim the tax you pay for the current tax year. difference. Please notify us if you want to cancel this declaration, | C] i ; change your name or home address, or, if you no longer pay | YES. | confirm that | am a UK taxpayer and | want to Gift Aid my donation, andany sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains. hi ay fc | donations | make in the future, or have made in the past 4 years to the Woodland Trust. QA d uw | If | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on | Please tick if you are not a UK taxpayer. | Pay for your membership by Direct Debit | Single Membership LJ £4* LJ £5 L] £10 or [e a month | Joint Membership LJ £4.50* L] £6 LC] £10 or [fs a month *Minimum monthly payment | Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by Direct Debit | Service user number Debit | To the Manager lo}3jol2le]4| | Reference number (to be completed by The Woodland Trust) | Address | Postcode Instruction to your Bank or Building Society: Please pay The Woodland Trust Direct Debits | from the account detailed in this instruction subject to the safeguards assured by the Direct | Name(s) of account holder(s) Debit Guarantee. | understand that this instruction may remain with The Woodland Trust | and, if so, details will be passed electronically to my Bank/Building Society. Registered | office: The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire, NG31 6LL | Bank/building society account number | Signature(s) | Branch sort code | Date / / | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit instructions for some types of account. | Pay for your membership by cheque or Credit/Debit Card | I'd like to make a donation of E | | enclose a cheque made payable to: The Woodland Trust. | Total | £ | Please write your name and address on the reverse. | Please debit my Credit / Debit Card: [ |yisa | |B) [ |Z |; a | Card number Expiry date S | EEEE BEER BEE ee: eee vain EB ~ | Simply complete this form, fold it in half and return it to us at: M21ADT021 (FR) | Freepost RTHA-JRSU-SSJX, Membership Team, The Woodland Trust, Kempton Thank you | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Way, Grantham NG31 6LL join online at woodlandtrust.org.uk/join | 2998/C/AB | Join the Woodland Trust from just | £4 a month and help save UK woods and | the wildlife that lives there. | Free welcome pack | when you join | As a member of the UK’s largest woodland | conservation charity you'll be helping protect native | woodland and create new woods throughout the UK. | Our members have helped us plant more than | 50 million trees so far. | There are great benefits to joining the Woodland Trust: | + Your own ‘leaf swatch’ tree identification guide so you can | enjoy tree-spotting and get to know the great variety of | trees you are helping to protect as a member. | ¢ A directory of over 1,000 woods to visit throughout the UK so | wherever you are, you'll be able to enjoy a walk in the woods. | * Four issues of Broadleaf, our exclusive members’ magagine, | each year and a membership card. | Your membership will help us... | “Woods are so important | for future generations. It’s | devastating to think my | grandchildren won’t be able to | enjoy such delights as | do. There’s | nothing better for the soul than | being deep in a wood, watching | wildlife, hearing birdsong and | forgetting the hustle and bustle | of everyday life.” | Carol, Woodland Trust member, Essex. | Save the woodland homes of the wildlife | we love. | The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire NG31 6LL. Tel. 0330 333 3300 woodlandtrust.org.uk. The Woodland Trust is a charity registered in | England and Wales (No. 294344) and in Scotland (No. SCO38885). A non-profit-making company limited by guarantee. Registered in England No. 1982873.",Newspaper,NA,NA
325,"TA XNZ@ OSE § 10d M | ADVERTISEMENT | An open letter to | Observer readers | The people of Yemen need your help. For more than six years, we’ve.lived | under the shadow of war. In some areas of the country we are seeing near | famine conditions. Children, women and men could die from hunger. | Yet, the fighting goes on. The current offensive in Marib, less than 100 miles | from my home in Sana’a, has killed hundreds and forced tens of thousands to | flee. The war affects everything. Public sector workers, such as teachers and | police officers, haven’t been paid regularly since 2017. Electricity is 900% more | expensive than in 2015. People have sold all their assets, but many are barely | surviving. Tragically, some have taken their own lives. To me, they are just as | much casualties of this war as people who die when their homes are hit. | When the bombing starts, my wife and | take the children to the safe room. We | tell them the explosions are people playing with fireworks. We haven’t suffered a | direct hit yet, but many of my neighbours haven’t been so lucky. When | go fora | walk, | see displaced families living on the sidewalk and under bridges, with only | cardboard and plastic sheeting to protect them. | And then we have COVID-19, which has seen the international community cut aid | to Yemen. It feels as if, while our people suffer, the world is looking the other way. | UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres said recently: “Millions of Yemeni children, | women and men desperately need aid to live. Cutting aid is a death sentence.” | So yes, the situation is dire. But no, we will not give up. Famine is edging closer, | but it’s not too late to help people. UNHCR has identified the most at risk families, | and with your help today could provide them with an Emergency Payment of | £143. The payment of £143 supports a family of six and is based on the cost of | a ‘Survival Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of essentials such as food, water and: | medicine. For a family on the brink of famine, it could be the difference between | life and death. | Thank you. | EZ tahion | Ebrahim Madaghesh, UNHCR Yemen | £143 could provide a family with an EMERGENCY | PAYMENT to buy food and other essentials | Give now at | unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call O800 029 3883, or fill in and return the form below | I would like to give: |_| £72 |_| 2143 [_] e286 [_] other £_ | L]1 enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | L] 1 would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. | cs aie a Gee Pa ja =| at | Date | Expiry date | Fe ey Pala | Signature | fz) Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title Last name | Address | First name | Postcode | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: L] By email L] By phone | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need.a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | (7)! would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p for each £1 GO fa d uw | donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand that if! pay-less | Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is | my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy. You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | FUNDRAISING | a Scan this FUNDRAISING ¢ W@W) YU Ra H CR | QR code to | donate online | * Aminimum of 75% of your gift will directly help displaced > & The UN Refugee Agency | people in Yemen, funding Emergency Payments and United Kingdom for UNHCR | . other humanitarian interventions. | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). | Registered with | P21YEOBB1",Newspaper,NA,NA
