332,"An open letter to | Sunday Mirror readers | The people of Yemen need your help. For more than six years, we’ve lived | under the shadow of war. In some areas of the country we are seeing near | famine conditions. Children, women and men could die from hunger. | Yet, the fighting goes on. The current offensive in Marib, less than 100 miles | from my home in Sana’a, has killed hundreds and forced tens of thousands to | flee. The war affects everything. Public sector workers, such as teachers and | police officers, haven’t been paid regularly since 2017. Electricity is 900% more | expensive than in 2015. People have sold all their assets, but many are barely | surviving. Tragically, some have taken their own lives. To me, they are just.as | much casualties of this war as people who die when their homes are hit. | When the bombing starts, my wife and | take the children to the safe room. We | tell them the explosions are people playing with fireworks. We haven’t suffered a | direct hit yet, but many of my neighbours haven’t been so lucky. When | go fora | walk, | see displaced families living on the sidewalk and under bridges, with only | cardboard and plastic sheeting to protect them. | And then we have COVID-19, which has seen the international community cut aid | to Yemen. It feels as if, while our people suffer, the world is looking the other way. | UN Sécretary-General Antdénio Guterres said recently: “Millions of Yemeni children, | women and men desperately need aid to live. Cutting aid is a death sentence.” | So yes, the situation is dire. But no, we will not give up. Famine is edging closer, | but it’s not too late to help people. UNHCR has identified the most at risk families, | and with your help today could provide them with an Emergency Payment of | £143. The payment of £143 supports a family of six and is based on the cost of | a ‘Survival Minimum Expenditure Basket’ of essentials such as food, water and | medicine. For a family on the brink of famine, it could be the difference between | life and death. | Thank you. | EZ bah | Ebrahim Madaghesh, UNHCR Yemen | £143 could provide a family with an EMERGENCY | PAYMENT to buy food and other essentials | Give now at | unrefugees.org.uk/helpyemen | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in and return the form below | I would like to give: |_| £72 [_] £143 [_]-c286 [_] other | L]1 enclose a cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | LJ 1 would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | meee Seco | Signature Date | Expiry date | Se ae | L] Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: | By email C] By phone | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | Increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | Oo would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p for each £1 Gf fas d a | donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm!ama UK taxpayer and | understand that if! pay less | Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year it is | my responsibility to pay any difference. | understand that council tax and VAT do not qualify. | ‘If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team — | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to date.with our work, fundraising activities and | other events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy. You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | tr [a] Scan this Registered with Y | FUNDRAISING 4 .) | REGULATOR \, Ny | * QR code to | —7~= The UN Refugee Agency | donate online | A minimum of 75% of your gift will directly help displaced , | people in Yemen, funding Emergency Payments and United Kingdom for UNHCR | other humanitarian interventions. | United Kingdom for UNHCR is a registered charity in England and Wales (1183415). P21YEMIB1",Newspaper,NA,NA
