sy _Please fill in the whole form using a ball point pen and send it to The Leprosy DIRECT | Mission Mission England, Wales, the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man, Goldhay Way, Debit | Orton Goldhay, Peterborough PE2 5GZ (do not return to your bank). | Name(s) of account holder(s) | Bank/Building Society account number: —_ Branch sort code: Name and full postal address of your Bank or Building Society | PDF [ |L] - [ E] - [ 1L] To: The Manager Bank/Building Society | Reference Service User Number Acres | LIT ETT TTT yy [4|1/sl1is[s| | Instruction to your Bank or Building Society. Please pay The Leprosy Mission England, Wales, the Channel Islands | and the Isle of Man, Direct Debits from the account detailed in this instruction, subject to the safeguards assured by | the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand that this instruction may remain with The Leprosy Mission England, Wales, Postcode | the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man and. if so, details will be passed cally to my bank/building society. | Signature(s) Date | Banks and Building Societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account | 3u3H 1V39S 8 NAILSIOW | C] Tick here and make your gift go 25% further with Gift Aid - at no cost to you | ‘ bs re | ( aA d Please treat all donations I have made to The Leprosy Mission for the four years prior to this donation, and all further donations | i, I make, as Gift Aid donations. I am a UK taxpayer and understand that if I pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the | amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my charitable donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. | MOISTEN & SEAL HERE | 21RECOBS | The Leprosy Mission England, Wales, Registered with | The Lepr osy the Channel Islands and the Isle of Man, FUNDRAISING | M e e Goldhay Way, Orton Goldhay, Peterborough PE2 5GZ REGULATOR | ission Tel: 01733 370505 Email: post@TLMEW.org.uk | Web: leprosymission.org.uk | Registered charity no.: 1050327 Registered company no.: 3140347 €) The Leprosy Mission England and Wales W @leprosytalk | MOISTEN & SEAL HERE | LEPROSY? | You may think leprosy is a disease of the | past. But it still exists for people living | in poverty across Asia and Africa. For | too long leprosy has torn lives apart. It | separates families, breaks up communities | and can cause disability and blindness. | The Leprosy Mission is a global Christian | organisation working to end the disease, the | isolation and the discrimination for good. | By working together, we believe that leprosy | ri \\ | can be a thing of the past. Until then, we | will stop at nothing to ensure that people | affected by leprosy are cured and supported | to change their lives for the better. | More information can be found online: | leprosymission.org.uk | TODAY, YOU CAN JOIN THIS | FIGHT BY BECOMING PART OF | THE GLOBAL RECIPE CLUB. | When you sign up, you'll become | part of a growing global community | of food enthusiasts and people | affected by leprosy who share the | love of tasty, nutritional cuisine. | You'll hear from incredible people | you are helping to overcome | leprosy, who can't wait to share | their delicious recipes with you. | Each month you'll travel to a | different country in Asia or Africa | from the comfort of your own | home. As you learn how to cook | authentic recipes, you'll also be | investing in communities affected | by leprosy to bring change. | When you choose to make a | regular gift of just £8 a month to | the Leprosy Mission, you'll receive | a new recipe card every month | from a different county. And each | recipe card comes with a story | about how your donation is helping | those most in need. Your money will | provide food, medicine, and support | to individuals, families and whole | communities affected by leprosy. | You CAN Find Yove | FREE TASTER PECIPE | on THE PACK/ | | WOULD PREFER TO GIVE A ONE-OFF GIFT TO HELP PEOPLE AFFECTED BY LEPROSY | First name: | Surname: | Address: | Postcode: | Telephone: | We love keeping in touch with you, but if you would like to change | how you hear from us, or would like a copy of our privacy policy, | simply call us on 01733 370505 or email post@TLMEW.org.uk | PLEASE SEND ME INFORMATION ON HOW | TO LEAVE A GIFT IN MY WILL | The Leprosy Registered with | lcctinn FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | Registered Charity No. 1050327 | A Company Limited by Guarantee | Registered in England and Wales no. 3140347 | MY GIFT: | £16 £32 £64 | If you are sending your own amount please complete the amount below. Thank you | I enclose a cheque / postal order payable to ‘The Leprosy Mission’ | Or please debit my: Visa MasterCard CAF Card | Card No.: | Expiry Date: / Card Security Code: | Signature: | Email: | Ae IN ORDER TO GIFT AID YOUR DONATION YOU MUST CROSS | giftasd “ = THE BOX AND AGREE TO THE STATEMENT BELOW: | Please treat all donations | | and all further donations * make, as Gift Aid donations | less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my charitable | donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference | DONATE ONLINE: | nave made to The Leprosy Mission for the four years prior to this donation, | am a UK taxpayer and understand that if I pay | 21RECOBS | 00001 | I'M JOINING THE GLOBAL | RECIPE CLUB TODAY! | The Leprosy Please affix | ee postage | Mission stamp here to | help reduce | our costs. II III | Freepost RTKU-RRBS-ZEHZ | The Leprosy Mission | Goldhay way | Orton Goldhay | PETERBOROUGH Thank Y ou | PE2 5GZ | 21RECOBS",Newspaper,NA,NA
334,"You can | trust us | WaterAid | . We'll use your donations in the best way possible. | For every £1 you give, 77p is spent on enabling | people to transform their lives with clean water, | decent toilets and good hygiene, and 23p | Is Spent on fundraising**. | . We promise your details are safe with us. | We'll respect your privacy and never share your | details with any other organisation or charity | for commercial or fundraising purposes. | You can choose how often we contact you. | Just call our Supporter Care Team on | 020 7793 4594. | Your support helps deliver lasting solutions, | not short-term fixes. | We will share stories of the people you help. | **As of 2019/20 WaterAid Annual Report | a TWO MILLION POUNDS is a lot to ask we know. But look at it this way. | If every household in our country gives just £2 a month, WaterAid will be able | to start changing the lives of some of the 785 million people who still lack clean | water - and the 2 billion people without their own toilet. That’s one in four people | on the planet. | Some might say that’s impossible, but at WaterAid we don’t. We know you must think | big to solve a big problem. Let's face it, in the UK we all take clean water and decent | toilets as a human right and a normal part of everyday life. We couldn't imagine life | without them. What better reason for every household to give a little to share this | life-changing good fortune? | Over 800 children die every day because of dirty water and poor sanitation. But it’s not | just about saving lives. Water changes everything. With clean water, decent toilets and | good hygiene, children are free to grow up healthy and go to school. Women and men | get to earn a living. Whole communities start to thrive. Together, people like you have | already helped transform the lives of over 27 million people with clean water. | What we do works, but we need to do | more of it. | Olivia lives in Madagascar. Every day she collected | dirty water from a river, filled with germs and | bacteria that made her sick. WaterAid and local | partners worked with Olivia's community to help | them install waterpoints in the village and at | her school. Access to clean water has been life | changing for Olivia. “Now we have running water | from the tap at school”. With clean water, Olivia | doesn't have to worry about getting sick and | missing school - she can focus on her education. | Olivia's world is changing. For the better. | We could take our solution to everyone, | everywhere in this world of ours. But not | without you. Create the world that children | like Olivia should be living in. Every penny counts | - please fill in the form and send it back today. | Olivia is the next generation, | the one that will be different. | That’s what your small | gift of £2 a month can do. | Be the change. Be the change. | SOY: \d RECYCLED Registered with | FS 4 2: ibe an (FR) FUNDRAISING | ‘ot ESC sce c009603 REGULATOR | ®aldg ° | 3 WaterAid | Registered charity numbers 288701 (England and Wales) and SC039479 (Scotland) ro ater i | PjE}EWLeLIpUeY JSBUIT/PIyiaIeM :sojoUd j}Vy | TEAR HERE AND SEAL MOI | MOISTEN | Fold he | -N HERE - TEAR HERE AND SEAL | iva) | I'll be the change. Here's my monthly gift of £2. | Call now on 0300 123 4341°, fill in the form below or donate online at www.wateraid.org/52million | £2 a month could save children’s £5 a month could save children’s £10 a month could save children’s lives. | lives. In just 12 months your donations lives. In just 12 months your donations In just 12 months your donations could | could install a handwashing station for could provide a clean water tank for a install water pipes in Ethiopia | three families in Sierra Leone school in Burkina Faso | 1 You can hear how you change lives. We hope you will “ | et Here s my life-changing gift of fill out your contact details below to hear more about “a | £2 £5 £10 Surprise us! £ eachmonth children like Olivia, fundraising, and opportunities to ~ | ‘ get involved. If you are happy to hear from us by phone = | Starting onthe 1st 130. eae and email, please let us know your details: | | should be at least four weeks se | Month Year | from date of signing Tel no. (home/mobile): ok | . Mm | Title: First name: Email: | eimname Many people love to receive postal updates. | Tick if you'd prefer not to _| | Home address: WaterAid and WaterAid Trading will use your personal details to communicate with you in the ways | o . you have agreed to, and as explained in our Privacy Policy. We may use the information you share | with us and background information about you that we obtain from publicly available sources to | carry out analysis (sometimes using suppliers) to tailor our communications to be more appropriate _ | and relevant to your interests. You can withdraw your consent at any time. For full details, including oO. | information about your privacy rights, see our Privacy Policy at www.wateraid.org/privacy ete | Postcode: To change your preferences, or request to stop receiving & | communications please contact us on 020 7793 4594 or | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid without at supporterca re@wateraid.org Sa RIONR | your full name and address. | y) Give ya cee een by signing up to Gut Aid at no extra cost to you. Tick hers: e giftaid itr | will be worth 25% more, at NO extra cost to you. Signing up t ft Aid is simple, all you need to do i: k the box | aim the tax you Nave paid on all your donatio yur years, and any ft donations you may | ay as much UK income and/o apital gains tax as WaterAid (and any other organisation you may support) will reclaim in each tax year | you donate. If you pay less it is your responsibility to pay back any difference. Gift Aid will be used to fund WaterAid’s general work | WaterAid Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by direct debit. 4) | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: Service user number | Freepost Plus RTXT-JATZ-LJST, WaterAid, York House, York YO26 7NH. AIOI6:718I9 DIRECT | Debit | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society (DO NOT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) | To the Manager: Bank/building society Reference (to be completed by WaterAid) | Branch address: | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please pay WaterAid | Direct Debits from the account detailed in this Instruction subject to | the safeguards assured by the Direct Debit Guarantee. I understand | Postcode: that this Instruction may remain with WaterAid and, if so, details will | be passed electronically to my bank/building society. | Name(s) of account holder(s): Signature(s) | Bank/building society account number Branch sort code xX | = = Date | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account.",Newspaper,NA,NA
335,"3 MY PROTECTION AT SEA | $4 Matt Church, Volunteer Crew Member, Penarth Lifeboat Station — | You can help RNLI volunteers like Matt face the full force of the sea with a gift in your Will. | You can provide the kit and training that keeps them safe, day or night. | 6 in 10 launches are only possible thanks to gifts | in Wills. Countless lives saved because of the | generosity of people like you. | A gift in your Will could provide the equipment that | protects our volunteers from the elements. It could | fuel the lifeboat so they can race to the rescue. | Find out how you can leave a lifesaving legacy. | Return the form below, or call | And it could provide the training brave volunteers like | Matt need to become a lifesaver. | It’s a gift that won't be forgotten - because your name | will be added to the side of a lifeboat. So you'll always | be a part of our lifesaving family. | To receive a free no obligation ‘Gifts in Wills Guide’, fill in the form below and send to: | FREEPOST RNLI WILLS (no stamp or other address details required) | Title: Full Name: | 8LOLZV-W1 | Keep in touch | Address: | Your support saves lives, and we look forward to keeping | in touch with you by post and phone, sharing our news, | activities and appeals. | Post code: Phone: | Would you like to receive our emails and text messages too? | L Yes, I'm happy to hear from you by email | Email: | CO Yes, I’m happy to hear from you by text | Privacy Notice: We will always store your personal details securely, and they will only be used by the | RNLI, RNLI Shop and RNLI College. Your data may also be used for analysis purposes, to help us provide the | best service possible. We will only allow your information to be used by suppliers working on our behalf and | we'll only share it if required to do so by law. For full details see our Privacy Policy at RNLI.org/PrivacyPolicy | or contact our Supporter Experience Team on 0300 300 9918. | Even if you have received our communications in the past, | we'll make sure we honour the preferences you express here. | If you would rather not hear from us, or would like to change | how we contact you, please get in touch. Just visit | RNLI.org/preferences or call 0300 300 9918: | RE GULATOR (209603), Scotland (SC037736), the Republic of Ireland (CHY 2678 and 20003326), the Bailiwick of Jersey (14), the Isle of Man | Registered with | FU N DR Al S] NG The RNLI is the charity that saves lives at sea. The Royal National Lifeboat Institution, a charity registered in England and Wales | (1308 and 006329F), the Bailiwick of Guernsey and Alderney, of West Quay Road, Poole, Dorset, BH15 1HZ",Newspaper,NA,NA
336,"WOODLAND | TRUST | Please, if you love | trees, youneedto | read this... E | The Woodland Trust is a charity registered in England and Wales (no. 294344) and in Scotland (no. SCO38885). / ) a | | responsible sources | Cy recycle Images: Stuart Shore, Wight Wildlife Photography. WTML/John Bridges. CP00048 06/21€9 Fsc or | Help us protect the UK’s | threatened woods and | wildlife, with membership | of the Woodland Trust. | “| joined the Woodland Trust to U f ¢ | make sure children will always have , ob | woods to play in, just as we did.” is | Why _- | ‘.°% | membership _ | - matters _ ag | WOODLAND | TRUST | Pek. TRUST Uae. | Fo Lie | There are great | benefits to joining the | Woodland Trust. And | you'll be helping us do | all this too... | Protect | The Woodland Trust works tirelessly to save the | UR’s remaining precious and irreplaceable ancient | woodland and keep it safe for future generations. | By becoming a member you'll be directly helping us | continue this vital work - 1,225 ancient woods are | under threat right now. | Restore | Join the Woodland Trust and help us care for and | restore damaged woodland so we can help wildlife | and native plants to thrive once again. | “Llove taking my Woodland Trust | leaf swatch out to the woods to try | and identify all the trees I see.” | Rachel Harding, Member since 2006 | “It feels wonderful to know you’re | helping create brand new woodland.” | Danny Hewis, Member since 2013 | Create | Your membership will help us plant trees which | can grow into flourishing new woods in as little as | 12 years. We have planted more than 50 million | trees since 1972 and we'll be getting 50 million | more in the ground by 2025. | Your support means we can own and care for more | than 1,000 woods across the UK that we'll keep | open and completely free for everyone. | Help us protect the woodland homes | of our threatened plants and wildlife. | WOODLAND | TRUST | Thank you for | becoming a member | and protecting | UK’s woodland. | Please affix | postage | stamp here | to help | reduce our | costs. | Freepost RTHA-JRSU-SSIX | Membership Team | The woodland Trust | Kempton way | GRANTHAM | NG31 6LL |  | WOODLAND | TRUST | Please. If you love trees, i | join the Woodland Trust today | and fight for their future. | Dear friend, | My name is Darren Moorcroft and | am privileged to be the head of the | Woodland Trust — the UK’s largest woodland conservation charity. Maybe | you have already heard of us and what we are doing to protect woods, | plant trees and create havens for wildlife across the nation. | I’m writing today with a stark warning - and a plea for your help. | The natural world is in crisis and we are facing a catastrophic collapse in | biodiversity which, without urgent action, will have consequences for every | one of us. Our work standing up for woods and trees has never been more | important. | I’m sure you'll agree that the pandemic has really brought home how vital | fresh air, green space, parks and woodland are for our physical health and | mental wellbeing. But woods aren't just lovely places for a relaxing walk | among nature, and trees give us so much more than colour and beauty. | Both trees and woods are essential for the future of our planet. | Join the Woodland | Trust today to | receive this unique | leaf swatch book. | You may have seen in the news recently that the Woodland Trust has just | published a report with ground-breaking evidence showing in shocking | detail just how critical native woods and trees are in the fight against the | climate and nature crisis we are in. | Yet UK woodland, and the wildlife it supports, is in serious trouble. | Threats against woods and trees are escalating and woodland wildlife is | in sharp decline. Because you are reading this, | believe you care about | protecting the woodland the UK has, and helping us create more havens | for rare and precious wildlife species. Trees are crucial for our environment | and without them, we, our children and grandchildren, and of course the | wildlife that depends on them for survival, face an uncertain future. | Trees and woods in this country are under threat every day - from | development, from tree pests and diseases and from the effects of climate | change. And that means thousands of species are at risk too. But there is | a way you can help. | Continued overleaf | Yes, | will join the Woodland Trust today. | Yes, | want to keep woodlands safe and unspoiled Sy | as a Woodland Trust member a | 4 Please fill in your details below - | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode Date of birth (optional) / / | Details of second member for joint membership (if applicable) | Title First name Last name | My email address is: My daytime telephone number is: | Let’s keep in touch! | In addition to receiving your membership benefits we would like to keep in touch with you about what we're doing for woods, trees and wildlife! You'll receive | regular updates, including our latest news, products and exciting events. Along with ways you can get involved with campaigns, fundraising and much more. | Would you like us to contact you by email? [_]Yes please, I'd like to hear from you by email. | We may contact you in the future by post and phone; please let us know if you'd prefer us not to. | [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not to hear from you by post [_]No thank you, I'd prefer to not hear from you by phone | You can unsubscribe from marketing at any time: visit our online permission portal - woodlandtrust.yourpreferencecentre.com, call 0330 333 3300, or | email supporters@woodlandtrust.org.uk. Your privacy is our priority and we promise to keep your details safe. For full details on how and why we collect, | store and use your personal information take a look at our online Privacy Policy - woodlandtrust.org.uk/privacy-policy and our Legitimate Interest | Statement - woodlandtrust.org.uk/legitimate-interests. CSO9 | Make a 25% bigger difference to woodland with Gift Aid | Boost your donation by 25p of Gift Aid for every £1 you donate. all my donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any | The Woodland Trust can reclaim the tax you pay for the current tax year. difference. Please notify us if you want to cancel this declaration, | gE ll - change your name or home address, or, if you no longer pay | YES. | confirm that | am a UK taxpayer and | want to Gift Aid my donation, andany sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains. i A peas | donations | make in the future, or have made in the past 4 years to the Woodland Trust. d uw | If | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on L] Please tick if you are not a UK taxpayer. | Pay for your membership by Direct Debit | Single Membership LJ £4* LJ £5 L] £10 or [e | a month | Joint Membership LJ £4.50* L] £6 L] £10 or [fd a month *Minimum monthly payment | Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by Direct Debit | Service user number Debit | To the Manager lo}3jol2ie]4| | Reference number (to be completed by The Woodland Trust) | Address | Postcode Instruction to your Bank or Building Society: Please pay The Woodland Trust Direct Debits | from the account detailed in this instruction subject to the safeguards assured by the Direct | Name(s) of account holder(s) Debit Guarantee. | understand that this instruction may remain with The Woodland Trust | and, if so, details will be passed electronically to my Bank/Building Society. Registered | office: The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire, NG31 6LL | Bank/building society account number | Signature(s) | Branch sort code | Date / / | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit instructions for some types of account. | Pay for your membership by cheque or Credit/Debit Card | Single Membership L] £48 a year™* or [fe si a year Prot the we | **Miniraum annual payment | I'd like to make a donation of E | | enclose a cheque made payable to: The Woodland Trust. | Total | £ Please write your name and address on the reverse. | Please debit my Credit / Debit Card: [ |yisa | |B) [ | |; ee | Card number Expiry date 2 | LETT WT Ey LET TILE TT CL va ~ | Simply complete this form, fold it in half and return it to us at: M21ADT021 (FR) | Freepost RTHA-JRSU-SSJX, Membership Team, The Woodland Trust, Kempton Thank you Bye | Way, Grantham NG31 6LL join online at woodlandtrust.org.uk/join recta ate at | 2998/C/AB | Join the Woodland Trust from just | £4 a month and help save UK woods and | the wildlife that lives there. | Free welcome pack | when you join | As a member of the UK’s largest woodland | conservation charity you'll be helping protect native | woodland and create new woods throughout the UK. | Our members have helped us plant more than | 50 million trees so far. | There are great benefits to joining the Woodland Trust: | - Your own ‘leaf swatch’ tree identification guide so you can | enjoy tree-spotting and get to know the great variety of | trees you are helping to protect as a member. | * A directory of over 1,000 woods to visit throughout the UK so | wherever you are, you'll be able to enjoy a walk in the woods. | * Four issues of Broadleaf, our exclusive members’ magagine, | each year and a membership card. | Your membership will help us... | “Woods are so important | for future generations. It’s | devastating to think my | grandchildren won’t be able to | enjoy such delights as | do. There’s | nothing better for the soul than | being deep in a wood, watching | wildlife, hearing birdsong and | forgetting the hustle and bustle | of everyday life.” | Carol, Woodland Trust member, Essex. | Save the woodland homes of the wildlife | we love. | The Woodland Trust, Kempton Way, Grantham, Lincolnshire NG31 6LL. Tel. 0330 333 3300 woodlandtrust.org.uk. The Woodland Trust is a charity registered in | England and Wales (No. 294344) and in Scotland (No. SCO38885). A non-profit-making company limited by guarantee. Registered in England No. 1982873.",Newspaper,NA,NA
