338,"WEAR | JEANS | CHANGE | LIVES | MON 13 - SUN 19 SEPT | SIGN UP TO | TAKE PART AT | JEANSFORGENES.ORG | Join Malin Andersson - TV personality | and Motivational Speaker - and show your | support for this year’s Jeans for Genes appeal. | Every purchase of one of our brand colour | t-shirts comes with a built in donation - | meaning that your shopping can help us | fund counselling, clinical nurses and critical | services for individuals and families living | with a genetic disorder in the UK. | Available in yellow, bright blue | (as modelled by Malin here) and navy. | Show your support and buy yours today at | jeansforgenes.org/shop | Jeans for Genes® © 2021 Jeans for Genes Campaign. | All rights reserved. Registered Charity Number 1194407.",Newspaper,NA,NA
339,"A gift in your Will helps the dogs | and cats who deserve it most | For over 160 years, Battersea has been here for | every dog and cat, taking them in without question | and caring for them without judgement until we find | them the homes where they truly belong. One in three | of these animals is cared for thanks to gifts in Wills. | By remembering Battersea in your Will, you help | ensure that we can continue to be here for every dog | and cat who needs us. Gifts in Wills are vital to all | areas of our work, so any gift you give, whatever size, | will make a big difference to the animals in our care. | A gift in your Will costs you nothing today but will help | ensure that Battersea can continue to support the | animals who need us tomorrow. | Together, we will be here for every dog and cat. | dt BATTERSEA | OF B | GIVE THE GIFT | ELONGING",Newspaper,NA,NA
340,"BritishRedCross | Afghanistan Is In crisis | Please send to: Afghanistan Crisis Appeal, Ref: 171820, Freepost Plus RUCB-JCXU-SRSJ, British Red Cross, Bumpers Way, | Bumpers Farm, CHIPPENHAM, SN14 6NG | | would like to make a donation of £20[] £40(] £60C] £100C] Othere[ | | (JI enclose a cheque; made payable to British Red Cross OR [_] Please debit my Visa/Mastercard/CAF Charity card with the amount specified | cardnumber| | [TILE TT ILE TT LET TI Expiry date | | /[_] | | Title Forename Surname | Address | Postcode | Phone number™ **Please only give us your telephone number/email address if you are happy for | Email** us to contact you in this way with updates about how your gifts are helping and | how you can donate and help in other ways. | Gift Aid allows us to claim back 25p of tax for every £1 you give, making your donation go further. | Ol am a UK taxpayer and | would like the British Red Cross to reclaim the tax on all qualifying donations | have made, as well as any future donations, until | ‘ ‘ d it | notify them otherwise. Please tick. | understand that if | pay less income/capital gains tax than the amount of gift aid claimed on all my donations in the tax year Ey! { fia | in which they are received, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. Please remember to let us know of any changes to your tax status, including changes to | your name or address, or if you need to cancel this agreement. 171820 | Keeping in touch Your support makes a life-changing difference to people in crisis. We write to our supporters to update you about the work of the British Red Cross, and how you can help and donate in other ways. | You can change the way we contact you at any time by visiting redcross.org.uk/keepingintouch or calling Freephone 0800 2800 491. | Privacy statement The British Red Cross is committed to privacy and will use personal data for the purpose it was collected or other legitimate purposes we tell you about: for example, to provide goods, services or | information you have requested or to administer donations or services we provide. We may also analyse data we collect to better understand the people who support us or those who use or deliver our services. Sometimes | this means us combining that data with information from reliable public sources. Our research allows us to tailor communications and services in a more focused and cost-effective way, as well as better meeting your needs | and the needs of others like you. However, we will never do this in a way that intrudes on personal privacy and will not use your data for a purpose that conflicts with previously expressed privacy preferences. For full details | about how we use personal data, our legal basis for doing so and your privacy rights, please see our privacy notice online at redcross.org.uk/privacy. | The Afghanistan Crisis Appeal will support people in areas currently affected and those potentially affected in the future by | the crisis. In the unlikely event that we raise more money than can be reasonably and efficiently spent, any surplus funds will | be used to help us prepare for and respond to other humanitarian disasters anywhere in the world. For more information visit | https://donate.redcross.org.uk/appeal/disaster-fund Registered with eG owe r | *Texts cost £10+1 standard message (we receive 100%). For full T&Cs visit redcross.org.uk/mobile FU N DR Al S| NG | The British Red Cross Society, incorporated by Royal Charter 1908, is a charity registered in England and Wales (220949), f k ad | Scotand (S0087798), Se of Man (0752) and Jersay 420) Se REGULATOR OT KiINGQnesSS",Newspaper,NA,NA
341,"British Heart | Foundation | ears | of sa | Researchers funded by the British Heart | Foundation have spent the last 60 years | taking on the world’s biggest killers: | heart and circulatory diseases. They’ve | been powered, in part, by gifts in Wills | from people like you. We call it Will Power. . | Will Power has helped to save countless lives | — lives like Zena’s. In 2017, Zena had a heart | attack and a stroke, and was diagnosed | with a genetic condition that causes high | cholesterol. But today, she is alive and well | — thanks to treatments that BHF-funded | researchers helped discover. | Find out more: search online | for ‘BHF gifts in Wills’ | ving | | But heart and circulatory diseases are still | the world’s biggest killers. They kill one in | four of us in the UK — and affect millions | more. That’s why, when it comes to research, | we're not slowing down. | To do it, we absolutely rely on gifts left | in the Wills of people like you. Today, | they fund more than half of our research — | and tomorrow, yours could help us achieve | even more. | This is Will Power. | Just think what yours could do. | Registered with | RECLILATO | © British Heart Foundation 2021 registered charity in England and Wales (225971) and Scotland (SC039426) 2ILA01 RE U TO",Newspaper,NA,NA
