347,"amend | oveslanenees iil | I | | BROTHER | MUSICIAN | Freepost Plus RTKS-ZCXS-HSBT | Crisis ILUNTEER | 126 Fairlie Road a | SLOUGH FRIENI | SL1 4PY | Homelessness | is part of | my journey, | but it | doesn't | experienced | Homelessness | I've always been passionate about music and art. | teach, volunteer, and have great | relationships with my sister Irma and my childhood friend, Deep. | This is the real me. | You might be surprised to hear that I've also been homeless. | When it first happened, my relationship broke down and | was left with nowhere to go. | was | embarrassed and felt pressure to sort myself out. | didn’t know what help was out there or if | | even deserved it. | had mental health struggles too, which made everything more difficult. | Now | know that it wasn’t my fault, but back then | couldn't see a way out. | I'm sure you'll agree that when you have no one fighting your corner, life can be much | harder. So imagine how it feels when you're homeless too. | There's a constant pressure hanging over you. To lead a productive life, find somewhere | to sleep, and fight prejudice and bureaucracy. You're demeaned again and again and | abandoned by a system that’s supposed to be helping you. It’s no way to live, is it? | Support from someone who cares can break that cycle. When you're at your lowest, | like | was, it gives you the strength to keep going. | Will you give £5 a month so that people like me don’t go through homelessness alone? | Crisis helped me get my life back on track. They found me a place to live and set me up with | some online art classes that gave me confidence and hope for a better future. | And while | still feel those pressures at times, | have help there at the end of the phone when | | need it. For those who don't, life gets harder every day. With 160,000 homeless households | in Britain, regular support from someone like you has never been more important. | £5 a month will help someone like me end their homelessness. | Just like you and | do, people experiencing homelessness have passions, skills, and dreams. | If you decide to fill in the form opposite, you'll be helping them live the life they were meant | to live, not one defined by homelessness. | He! om; & & | Crisis UK (trading as “Crisis’) is a registered charity and company limited by guarantee. Registered charity numbers: E&W1082947, | $C040094. Company No: 4024938. Registered address: Crisis, 66 Commercial Street, London, E1 6LT. Tel: 0300 636 1967. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | REGULATOR | 3Y44H N3LSIOW | A regular gift of £5 could pay for one-on-one support to help someone like Harry take the | first steps out of homelessness. Fill in this form or give now at crisis.org.uk/harry | @ £5 per month £8 per month £10 per month Other: £ per month | ; (should be at least four weeks | Starting on the 1st 15th Month Year from date of signing) | Title: First name: Last name: | Home address: | Postcode: | Please note we are unable to process your Direct Debit or claim Gift Aid without your full name and address and may write to you to process your gift. | We would like to keep you updated on our work and how you can help us end homelessness | through donating, fundraising, campaigning and volunteering. Please tell us if you'd like this | by email and/or phone by supplying your details below. | Email: Tel no. (home/mobile): | Many people like to receive post from us. Tick if you'd prefer not to | You can change your preferences at any time by calling 08000 38 48 38 or by emailing | mydetails@crisis.org.uk. We promise to respect the information you give us. You can see our | privacy statement at www.crisis.org.uk/privacy eaeinsuena anne | Q Please make every pound you give worth 25% more to Crisis by ticking this Gift Aid declaration. | | am a UK taxpayer and | would like Crisis to treat this donation and any donations | make in the future and have | made in the past 4 years as Gift Aid donations, until | notify you otherwise. With this declaration, Crisis can reclaim | 25p of tax on every £1 that | give. | understand that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the | amount of Gift Aid claimed on all my donations in that tax year, it is my responsibility to pay any difference. nares | Please remember to write your full name and home address to allow us to claim Gift Aid. giftaid “wo | 4) Instruction to your bank or building society to pay by Direct Debit. | All you need to do is complete the form, moisten, fold and seal, and return to: DIRECT | Freepost Plus RTKS-ZCXS-HSBT, Crisis, 126 Fairlie Road, SLOUGH, SL1 4PY. (D0 NOT RETURN TO YOUR BANK) Debit | Name and full postal address of your bank or building society Service user number | To the Manager: Bank/building society: 8 0 6 2 2 7 | Reference (to be completed by Crisis): | Branch address: 6 | Instruction to your bank or building society: Please pay | Postcode: Crisis Direct Debits from the account detailed in this Instruction | subject to the safeguards assured by the Direct Debit Guarantee. | | understand that this Instruction may remain with Crisis and, if so, | details will be passed electronically to my bank/building society. | Name(s) of account holder(s): ee Me: ""9 24 | Signature(s): | Bank/building society account number: Branch sort code: | Date: | Banks and building societies may not accept Direct Debit Instructions for some types of account. | The Crisis promise — Although we can't guarantee your donation will be spent on specific items | or services, we can guarantee your donation will be used wherever it is needed most to help our | work with people facing homelessness. | MOISTEN HERE | FOLD | JY3H NALSIOW",Newspaper,NA,NA
348,"WEAR | JEANS | CHANGE | LIVES | MON 13 - SUN 19 SEPT | SIGN UP TO | TAKE PART AT | JEANSFORGENES.ORG | Join Malin Andersson — TV personality | and Motivational Speaker — and show your | support for this year’s Jeans for Genes appeal. | Every purchase of one of our brand colour | t-shirts comes with a built in donation — | meaning that your shopping can help us | fund counselling, clinical nurses and critical | services for individuals and families living | with a genetic disorder in the UK. | Available in yellow, bright blue | (as modelled by Malin here) and navy. | Show your support and buy yours today at | jeansforgenes.org/shop | Jeans for Genes® © 2021 Jeans for Genes Campaign. | All rights reserved. Registered Charity Number 1194407.",Newspaper,NA,NA
349,"British Heart | Foundation | Researchers funded by the British Heart - | Foundation have spent the last 60 years | taking on the world’s biggest killers: | heart and circulatory diseases. They've | been powered, in part, by gifts in Wills | from people like you. We call it Will Power. | Will Power has helped to save countless lives | — lives like Zena’s. In 2017, Zena had a heart | attack and a stroke, and was diagnosed | with a genetic condition that causes high | cholesterol. But today, she is alive and well | — thanks to treatments that BHF-funded | researchers helped discover. | Find out more: search online | for ‘BHF gifts in Wills’ | © British Heart Foundation 2021 registered charity in England and Wales (225971) and Scotland (SC039426) 21LA0] | But heart and circulatory diseases are still | the world’s biggest killers. They kill one in | four of us in the UK — and affect millions | more. That’s why, when it comes to research, | we're not slowing down. | To do it, we absolutely rely on gifts left | in the Wills of people like you. Today, | they fund more than half of our research — | and tomorrow, yours could help us achieve | even more. | This is Will Power. | Just think what yours could do. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | @ REGULATOR",Newspaper,NA,NA
