355,"I would like to give: [_] 82 [_] e164 (_] others | YOU CAN HELP | THE PEOPLE | OF AFGHANISTAN | A HUMANITARIAN CRISIS IS UNFOLDING | At the time of writing, UNHCR staff are continuing to work on | the ground across Afghanistan: They will stay for as long as the | security situation allows it, to protect the hundreds of thousands of | people forced to flee within the country and made vulnerable by | the conflict. The increasing numbers of people needing help has, | however, seen stocks of humanitarian supplies running low and | time running short. UNHCR’s team in Afghanistan urgently need | your support. | People’s most immediate needs are safety-and protection, shelter, | food, sanitation and drinking water. | Please will you give £82 to help UNHCR teams | provide lifesaving humanitarian support to the people | of Afghanistan? | The situation is complex and dynamic, and the next few days and | weeks could see a further increase in humanitarian needs. We | are concerned about the risk of serious human rights abuses and | violations in the communities most affected by the fighting. Our | teams are particularly concerned about the impact of the violence | on women and children. | Speaking from Kabul on Sunday August 15, Caroline Van Buren, | UNHCR’s Representative in Afghanistan, said: | “We are getting reports that women who are fleeing are giving birth | on the road, without any medical assistance. The information we | have now is that women and children are almost 50% of the civilian | casualties, people who are killed or injured during all this violence.” | “People need help. Afghans need help.” | The unfolding situation is deeply alarming, but there is something | you can do to help. | With a gift of £82 today, or whatever you can afford, you could | help UNHCR get lifesaving supplies through to the people who | most need them. | Your support can help save lives. | could help provide an Afghan family | with emergency essentials: shelter | materials (such as tarpaulins), food, | water and sanitary supplies. | Give now at Unrefugees.org.uk/afghanappeal | Call 0800 029 3883, or fill in the form below | (J benclose a.cheque made payable to UK for UNHCR OR | (J t would like to make a donation by debit/credit card | Card no. Expiry date | BBARVAeRe es oboe ee | Signature Date | | Tick here, if you don’t want to receive an acknowledgement by post | Title First name Last name | Address | Postcode | Email | Phone | Please tell us if you are happy to hear about UNHCR’s work: OC By email eal By phone | Please return this form along with your cheque to: | Freepost UK FOR UNHCR (you don’t need a stamp) | increase your donation by 25p for every £1 you donate | gifted we | Ch would like UK for UNHCR to claim Gift Aid on this donation (currently 25p | for each £1 donated), as well as any donations | make in the future and have made in the past four | years to UK for UNHCR, until | notify you otherwise. | confirm | am a UK taxpayer and | understand | that if | pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid claimed on ail my | donations in that tax year it is my responsibility to pay any difference. !| understand that council tax | and VAT do not qualify. | If your circumstances change or you have any questions, please contact our Supporter Care Team | on 0800 029 3883 or email supportercare@unrefugees.org.uk | Respecting your personal data: We will use your details to process your | donation and to keep you up to.date with our work, fundraising activities and other | events. You can read more about how we use your data in our Privacy Policy | unrefugees.org.uk/privacy-policy You can opt out of any communications at any | time by contacting our Supporter Care Team using the details above. | sae (i) UNHCR | Registered with Aminimum of 75% of your gift will directly help displaced people in Afghanistan, QR code to The UN Refugee Agency | FUNDRAISING funding survival essentials and other humanitarian interventions.