360,"Researchers funded by the British Heart | Foundation have spent the last 60 years | taking on the world’s biggest killers: heart | and circulatory diseases. They ve been | powered, in part, by gifts in Wills from | people like you. We call it Will Power. | Will Power has helped to save countless | lives — lives like Zena’s. In 2017, Zena had | a heart attack and a stroke, and was | diagnosed with a genetic condition that | causes high cholesterol. But today, she is | alive and well—thanks to treatments that | BHF-funded researchers helped discover. | Find out more: search online | for ‘BHF gifts in Wills’ | But heart and circulatory diseases are still | the world’s biggest killers. They kill one in | four of us in the UK—and affect millions | more. That's why, when it comes to research, | we re not slowing down. | To do it, we absolutely rely on gifts left in | the Wills of people like you. Today, they | fund more than half of our research —and | tomorrow, yours could help us achieve | even more. | This is Will Power. | Just think what yours could do. | Registered with | FUNDRAISING | © British Heart Foundation 2021, a registered charity in England and Wales (225971) and Scotland (SC039426) 21LA01 REGULATOR |",Newspaper,NA,NA
