09,"CHR44_3_L809461_170621\012496\24991\10f2\ | AMYOA OURAIIS/PIY UENSLIY :010Yd | 15th June: Asunta, 55, with her grandchild in Aweil South, | Northern Bahr El Ghazal state, South Sudan. Since last year, | floods and drought have caused hunger in her village. | June 2021 | We urgently need your support to help people around the world facing extreme hunger. Please send a gift today. | Dear | As the Head of Global Humanitarian Response, I'm writing to request your support. Currently, more than 30 million people in | 20 countries are living in serious hunger, teetering on the brink of famine. I’ve seen how the Covid-19 pandemic, climate crisis, | and continued conflict have worsened hunger and insecurity around the world. The possibility of starvation threatens many - | but these deaths are preventable. | Your support is needed now to help our partners work alongside people around the world to save lives. Together we can | distribute life-saving food, support and build resilience. | If you've already donated to our Global Hunger Appeal then please accept my heartfelt thanks for your life-saving gift. | The situation is particularly dire in South Sudan, where it is estimated that up to 60% of people will likely experience severe food | insecurity. Here, we see the impact of the climate crisis on the world’s most vulnerable: flooding in the low-lands of Jonglei and | Upper Nile and drought in the Bar El Ghazal areas mean food is scarce. Conflict and the pandemic only compound this. | Please will you donate £25, or whatever you can afford, to support our vital work? | We're responding now with our local partners in South Sudan, and other affected places including north-east Nigeria, Ethiopia, | Burkina Faso and Afghanistan. We're distributing and enabling access to clean water, nutritional food, seeds and tools, to | support food production and prevent malnutrition. | 656589_LTUK | Yes, | want to help those around the world facing extreme hunger | Here is my emergency gift of: | C) £25 CL) £60 CL) £100 Other £ | Please make your cheque / postal order / CAF voucher* payable to: Christian Aid | (Please do not send cash by post) “delete as appropriate | OR debit my (] Mastercard [Visa [Maestro [] CAF Card | Please copy the long number from the middle of your card, and add the issue number (if applicable) below. | cardno.L 11 tT JLE ETI LEE EY LEE TI LET Vimtaestro oniyy | Start date [T] / LT] Expiry date [rea] / YD] Issue no. ARE (Maestro only) | Signature | patel! J/Lt |/LLJ | C1 would prefer not to receive an acknowledgement of my gift | If we raise more than needed, rest assured, your donation will be used wherever we consider the need is greatest. | Our records show you have agreed giftaid an | to Gift Ald your donations | As a result of your action, every gift you make to Christian Aid is worth 25 | per cent more. This additional amount will be spent on our vital work | wherever the need is greatest. | Please note that if you pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than | the arnount of Gift Aid claimed on all your donations in that tax year it is | your responsibility to pay any difference. Thank you. | Please notify Christian Ald if you: | * want to cancel this declaration | + change your name or home address | + no longer pay sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains | You can also donate online at caid.org.uk/hunger or call 08080 004 004 | CHR44_3_L809461_170621\012496\24992\2o0f2\ | Please give today - your generosity could help save lives. | e £25 could buy food for a family for a month. | e £60 could buy a seasons’ worth of seeds and the tools to grow vegetables for four families. | e £100 could provide water hygiene kits for 20 families so they can make water safe to drink. | We must act, now. This is a global emergency. In South Sudan alone, millions of women, men and children are in need of food. | Hundreds of thousands of people are likely to face famine. | My colleague in South Sudan, James Wani, told me: ‘People, at this time, are dependent on our good will and compassion.’ | So, if you can, please stand with your global neighbours by sending a gift today. The sooner we receive your donation, | the sooner we can turn your compassion into action. | Thank you in advance for your support. | Yours sincerely, | Salome Ntububa | Head of Global Humanitarian Response | PS This is a global hunger crisis. We must act now to prevent a huge loss of life. Please give whatever you can today. | Thank you. | If you would like to stop receiving information by post, or you would like to change the way you hear from us, | please call our Supporter Care team on 020 7523 2493 or email info@christian-aid.org including your full name | and address. We promise never to share your details with any other organisation for marketing purposes. For | more information, please visit caid.org.uk/privacy | PO Box 100, London SE1 7RT ® Teleph 020 7620 4444 ee FUNDRAISING | ox 100, London * Telephone: 5 | Email: info@christian-aid.org * caid.org.uk actalliance REGULATOR | Christian Aid is a key member of ACT Alliance. Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 Scot charity no. SC039150 Company no. 5171525. The Christian Aid name and logo are trademarks of | Christian Aid. Printed exclusively on material sourced from responsibly managed forests © Christian Aid 2020 J177825 | Save a trip to | the postbox | Scan the code with | your phone to donate | online, or go to | caid.org.uk/hunger | Thank you | Scan me | Were there before, during and | after an emergency to save lives | and support people long term. | 4 a ek | 4 my lo | a a8 hs | Freepost Plus RTHB-AKAE-UUSX | Christian Aid | The Data Solution Centre | Manton Wood Enterprise Park | WORKSOP | S80 2RT | PN3709901 | Qrrecycle Return Address: Christian Aid, PO Box 100, London SE1 7RT | Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 Scot charity no. SC039150 Company no. 5171525. | Printed exclusively on material sourced from responsibly managed forests. © Christian Aid 2020. | Global | Hunger | Appeal | 15th June: Asunta, 55, with her grandchild in Aweil South, | Northern Bahr El Ghazal State, South Sudan. Since last year, | floods and drought have caused hunger in her Village. | June 2021 | SMO, OURAIIS/pIy UeRSUYD «",Mailout,NA,NA
10,"CAM-001787 | Freepost Plus RTHB-AKAE-UUSX | Appeal & Emergencies - High | Christian Aid | The Data Solution Centre | Manton Wood Enterprise Park | Worksop | S80 2RT | Christian Aid is a key member of ACT Alliance. Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 Scot charity ng. §C039150 Company no. 5177525. The Christian Aid name | and logo are trademarks of Christian Aid. Printed exclusively on material sourced from responsibly managed forests, © Christian Ald June 2021 J238455 | Thank you for your gift of love today. | With no income, this determined | grandma farms a small patch of land | where she grows sweet potatoes and | cassava - in spite of her age and the | diabetes she’s battling. | So thank goodness for next-door | neighbours like 18-year-old Sunny, who | is there when Elizabeth needs him: ‘I | help her with daily activities and also | with farming her land.’ | Faraway neighbours like you have | been there for Elizabeth too. She | had no means of protection from | coronavirus, but through your kindness | she received a hygiene kit that she | could use to protect herself and the | children. Thank you. | Everyone needs good neighbours | - Elizabeth, who is single-handedly | raising her three young | grandchildren, is no exception. | Consolate, who lives in southern Burundi, | is amum whose children were at risk of | malnutrition. Poverty severely limited | her family's diet: ‘My spouse and | had no | knowledge of nutrition, and we didn’t have | enough food to feed our children.’ | But through a Christian Aid project, | Consolate gained the knowledge and | skills she needed to turn these problems | around. | ‘I've continued to improve | my knowledge of Pia \ ‘| learned how to feed my children a | preparation and childcare’, nutritious diet using local foods. | also | Consolate says. learned how to grow vegetables and | now have my own vegetable garden. | Thanks to the project my children are | now well nourished.’ | Salamatu, from Nigeria, is a widow who | was supporting a household of eight on | a small, irregular income. When | lockdown came, that tiny income dried | up. The family’s existence became even | more fragile. | But then, thanks to people like you, | Salamatu received a lifeline. We identified | her as qualifying for a cash payment, | the most empowering way to give | someone in a desperate situation the | support they need. | It not only helped Salamatu get her | family through a terrible time, it helped | her start a business that provides an | income and daily meals for her family. | Thank you for all the loving support | you have given to help others | take their futures back into their | own hands. | Your kindness and generosity | | has helped global neighbours like | Salamatu to find a new beginning | in the darkest of times. | Thanks to you, Christian Aid is working in Ly | towards a world where everyone can live a lif | poverty. Our humanitarian emergency programm | alone are reaching 1.7 million people across the wo r | That's quite a global neighbourhood! A neighbourhood | connected by love, enriching life in so many different ways | for each one of us. | In Kaduna State, | Nigeria, a COVID-19 | rapid response project | is empowering | vulnerable households \ | to protect their families }% | | by delivering water and bn | hygiene kits. | nof 0} yonq | sHhulssalq pun | aac] Hurburrq | Xe ss $aTI07g | ue ae aADY nok aAoj aU} 10} | Sombo Mansay and | her 10-day-old twins | in the village of | « Sawula, Sierra Leone | 1rough Christian | Aid, your love reaches | families across the | world. Thank you so | much for your support! | Christian Aid is a key member of ACT Alliance. Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 | Scot charity no. SC039150 Company no. 5171525. The Christian Aid name and | logo are trademarks of Christian Aid. Printed exclusively on material sourced from | responsibly managed forests © Christian Aid June 2021 Christian Aid/Latitude | Space, Kunle Amuwo Jr, Jerry Clinton, Shafi Salehy,Tom Pilston J238455 | People are doing everything they can to survive the devastating effects of | poverty, war and the climate crisis. And now coronavirus is threatening lives | and livelihoods worldwide. | With your incredible love and support, there can be a way forward. | Love connects us all. And every time we reach out to others, we make the | circle of love even bigger and stronger. | A group of women receive food | packages and hygiene kits in the | distribution centre, to stop the | spread of coronavirus in Afghanistan. | For your global neighbours battling poverty, lack of water, food and healthcare, there | is little hope of a vaccine rollout. | With your help, Christian Aid will continue standing with people across the globe, | providing practical support so they can keep themselves safe. | Thanks to loving | neighbours like you, | Elizabeth received a | COVID-19 hygiene kit to | protect herself and her | grandchildren - Mary, | Dookenger and Oryina. | Love like yours has helped to transform the | lives of Denise and her family. | July 2021 | Dear | Thank you for the loving support you have given through Christian Aid to global neighbours who are battling | poverty around the world. Like you, | believe in being there for my neighbours, from all faiths and none. That's | why | work with Christian Aid in Burundi. | | really believe that love connects us all - and that every time we reach out to others, we make the circle of love | even bigger and stronger. So today I’m delighted to be able to reach out to you, with loving wishes and uplifting | stories from my neighbourhood and beyond, in our global community. | We are all in this together. But if it weren't for people like you, many of us might not be here today - | strong in the knowledge that you and others are standing in solidarity with us. | | would especially like to thank you for your wonderful, committed support for Christian Aid’s work. Month after | month, your regular gifts are helping to fight the outrage of poverty and all its impacts - from lack of access to | food, water and healthcare, to the huge threat of the climate crisis for our poorest, most vulnerable | neighbours. | In the ‘thank you’ I've enclosed, you'll see stories bearing witness to the power of love, from communities miles | away from yours in Norwich. | think these stories show that wherever we may be, we are connected by a | love that dignifies us all. | For example, here in Burundi, our country is recovering from a conflict which took thousands of lives and | displaced many families. We're a densely-populated nation where many families subsist on tiny plots of land. | Christian Aid has worked with loving, local church partners to help families improve their lives and stop their | children suffering from malnutrition, by supporting women like Denise through our Health Legacy project. | Denise got involved with the project after bringing her children to one of our health clinics to be screened for | malnutrition. When the screening revealed her children were very unwell with anaemia, Denise was desperate | to do all she could to help them recover. So she jumped at the chance to get dietary advice and farming | training, and to join a women’s savings and loan scheme: | ‘| participated in farming school and started to produce vegetables with my children. | set up a vegetable | Please turn over | fe?) | fo?) | pa | | In your enclosed ‘thank you’ you'll meet | Elizabeth, and find out how | believe | your love has made a difference to her. | business thanks to a loan, which allowed me to buy sweet potato | and beans that | mixed with vegetables to make balanced meals. | ‘After a while, my anaemic children, for whom the doctor had | recommended a blood transfusion, recovered’. | Full of relief and hope, Denise also bought a goat, to provide further | independence in growing her family’s income. It proved to be a great | success - and even led to a transformation in her marriage, reigniting | her loving connection with her husband: | ‘Ayear later, my goats had multiplied to nine - and from that day | on, my husband has called me ‘my honey’. | am very happy | to be called this. We live together thanks to this project.’ | It's a joy for me to speak to people like Denise and to hear about the changes they have been able to make | in their lives. I've seen the Health Legacy Project bring truly wonderful benefits to two communities in south | ‘Burundi. Nearly 2,500 households can now grow vegetables of their own. And over 3,800 inspiring women can | now access a community loans scheme to pay for the essentials they need, like food for their children. Your | donations have helped to fund projects like these for people all over the world. | In our enclosed ‘thank you’, you'll see more examples of how your love connects you with others. | People like you, who show such love to their neighbours, are | an inspiration to me in my work. So may | ask you a question: | what inspired you to love your neighbour by supporting | Christian Aid? Please do share your thoughts using the enclosed | form - you'll see there’s a space where you can write a few words. | We would love to hear from you. | As a global family, we can make such positive changes to our | world through our loving connection with each other. | am so | pleased to have this chance to send our love to you, with all our | thanks for your kindness to us and so many others. It’s people like | you who keep the circle of love growing ever bigger and stronger. | Thanks to loving support like yours, | hygiene kits with masks, hand sanitiser and | soap reached thousands of people in Adagi | community, Nigeria. | ~, ae | Blaise Kubwayo | Health Project Officer | Burundi | With every good wish to you and your family, | PS Your loving kindness gives people the means not only to survive, but empowers them to stand up for | the dignity they deserve. | If you feel you could send another gift today, please return the enclosed form, visit caid.org.uk/health or | call us on 0333 555 1060. Thank you so much. | If you'd like to change the way we contact you, or stop | hearing from us altogether, please call 020 7523 2493 or Noman Giscamrtnnaer FR) Registered with | email info@christian-aid.org - make sure to tell us your H FUNDRAISING | full name and address so we can identify you. actTalliance REGULATOR | Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 Scot charity no. SCO39150 Company no. 5171525. The Christian Aid name and logo are trademarks of Christian Aid. Printed exclusively on material sourced from | responsibly managed forests © Christian Aid June 2021 Photos: Christian Aid/Latitude Space, Shafi Salehy, Christian Aid J238455 | What inspired you to love your 2 | neighbour through Christian Aid | 6Do everything | in love | 1 Corinthians 16714 | Thanks to the love of | supporters like you, | children just like Dookenger | had food and soap to take | home and stay safe. | You have shown such love to others by supporting Christian Aid. | What inspired this connection? What are your hopes for those whose lives you have touched? | Has your connection with your global neighbours brought unexpected gifts to you? | Please tell us your thoughts here! | [_]! would be happy for my words to be shared in a future issue of Christian Aid Magazine or other communications. | D Girling | v) 13 Hilly Plantation | NORWICH | NR7 OJL | I'd like to send another | gift of love today. | C-5036474 CAM-002010 | F Here is my extra gift of: ) { : | L_] £10 | [J £15 Donate quickly and securely online | L] £20 : at caid.org.uk/health or by calling | LI or my choice of £ us on 0333 555 1060 | We will use your kind donation to support projects | like the ones featured in this letter and wherever | the need is greatest. | Enterprise Park, Worksop, S80 2RT. Thank you. | Christian Aid is a key member of ACT Alliance. Eng and Wales charity no. 1105851 Scot charity no. SC039150 Company no. 5171525. The Christian Aid name and logo are trademarks of | Christian Aid. Printed exclusively on material sourced from responsibly managed forests © Christian Aid June 2021 J238455 | Ss 7 & ; 4 | (i . . . . . . =) | [Ji enclose a cheque / postal order / Charity Voucher (circle as appropriate) payable to Christian Aid | OR debit my L] MasterCard L]Visa | Maestro L_] CAF Card | Please copy the long number from the middle of your card, and add the issue number (if applicable) below. Please do not send cash by post. | Card no. (Maestro only) | Start date / Expiry date / Issue no. (Maestro only) | Signature | Date / / | XY 4 | = : 5 >» | ( Our records show you have agreed to Gift Aid your donations | As a result of your action, every gift you make to Christian Aid is worth 25 per cent more, which | means your gift goes further towards helping the world’s poorest communities. | Please note that if you pay less Income Tax and/or Capital Gains Tax than the amount of Gift Aid iftaid ub | claimed on all your donations in that tax year it is your responsibility to pay any difference. g | Thank you. | Please notify Christian Aid if you: | * want to cancel this declaration | * change your name or home address | * no longer pay sufficient tax on your income and/or capital gains | %  (Emailand Telephone details 2) | for) | 8 You have already kindly provided your details to email you. Thank you. If you would also be happy to hear from us by telephone, please | = provide those details below. We will keep you updated about our work and the difference your support is making. We promise never to | 8 share your details with any other organisation for marketing purposes. For more information please visit caid.org.uk/privacy. | N Telephone number: | es To save paper, we'll send our thanks for your support via email if possible. | g | J | “I Please return your completed form in the envelope provided to: Registered with | “I Freepost Plus RTHB-AKAE-UUSX, Christian Aid, The Data Solution Centre, Manton Wood FUNDRAISING | 2 REGULATOR",Mailout,